1. d4 {1)Tal and Koblencs in Tournament Bulletin 1957. reprinted in 2) Kirillov: Mikhail Tal 1949.1961.Riga 1996. p.101-102.} d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. e3 Bg4 5. Bxc4 e6 6. h3 Bh5 7. Qb3 Bxf3 8. gxf3 Nbd7 9. Qxb7 c5 10. dxc5 Bxc5 11. a3 (11. f4) 11... O-O 12. b4 Ne5 13. bxc5 (13. Be2 Nd3+ 14. Bxd3 Qxd3 $17 15. bxc5 $142 Rab8 $132) 13... Nxc4 14. O-O Nd5 15. Nd2 Qg5+ 16. Kh1 Qh4 17. Kh2 Rad8 {'Tal's position looks OK but White's position also has virtues. The game now enters a scrappy phase where Tal's formidable powers of imagination and calculation shine.'} 18. Ra2 (18. Nxc4 Qxc4 19. Rg1) 18... Ne5 19. Rc2 $1 f5 20. c6 Nxe3 (20... Qa4 21. Rg1 $2) (20... Nd3 $1 21. Rg1) (20... Nf4 21. exf4 Qxf4+) (20... Nc7) 21. c7 $2 (21. fxe3 Ng4+ {'!'} 22. fxg4 fxg4 23. c7 (23. Kg1 Qg3+ {'!'} 24. Kh1 Qxh3+ 25. Kg1 Qxe3+ {'!'} 26. Kh1 g3 {'!'} 27. Nf3) (23. Qd7 Qxh3+ (23... Rxd7 24. cxd7 Qxh3+) 24. Kg1 Qxe3+ 25. Kg2 Qe2+ $2 26. Kg1 Rxd7 $2 27. cxd7 Qe3+ 28. Kh1 Rd8 29. Rc8 Qh3+ 30. Kg1 Qg3+ 31. Kh1 Qh4+ 32. Kg1 Qe7) (23. Kh1) 23... Rxd2+) 21... Rxd2 22. Rxd2 Qf4+ 23. Kh1 {'Just when White might have thought he was getting somewhere...'} Nxf1 $1 (23... Nxf3 24. fxe3) 24. Kg2 Nxd2 25. c8=Q Rxc8 26. Qxc8+ Kf7 $1 {[#]} 27. Qc7+ Kg6 28. Bxd2 Qxf3+ {'!'} 0-1

