eces to the greatest extent.'''} 44. Rg5 Ra5 45. Rh5 {Mikhail Tal: 'This position offers Black a comparatively easy path to victory.' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Bulletin: 'Mikhail Tal: 'This position offers Black a comparatively easy path to victory.'''} Ra2+ (45... Rb5 46. Rg5 Rc5 {Mikhail Tal: 'White is forced either to let the black king move to h2 ('} 47. Rh5 ({Mikhail Tal: 'or to let the c-pawn advance ('} 47. Rg8 Rc2+ 48. Ke3 c5 {Mikhail Tal: '). In my adjournment analysis I could find no satisfactory defence for White, but just before the resumption I thought of another winning plan and decided to implement it. It was based on some of the specific features of this position, and it surprised my opponent.'}) 47... Rc2+ 48. Ke3 Kg3 49. Rg5+ Kh2 {h4-h3 Mikhail Tal: ') and the h-pawn advances'}) (45... Rd5 $142 {(Komodo 9 64-bit (20s)) keeps an even firmer grip} 46. Rh8 c5 47. Rh7 $19) 46. Ke3 {Mikhail Tal: 'With' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Bulletin: 'Mikhail Tal: 'With'''} Kg2 $1 {Mikhail Tal: 'Black abandons the pawn by choice.' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Bulletin: '!' Bulletin: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Black abandons the pawn by choice.'''} 47. Rxh4 ({Mikhail Tal: 'After'} 47. Rxf5 h3 48. Rg5+ Kf1 $19 {Mikhail Tal: 'Black naturally wins.'}) ({Mikhail Tal: 'Also,'} 47. Rg5+ Kf1 48. Rh5 c5 $1 49. Rxh4 Ra3+ 50. Kd2 Rxf3 $19 {Mikhail Tal: 'is 'out'.'}) (47. Z0) 47... Ra3+ 48. Ke2 (48. Kd4 Kg3 {Mikhail Tal: 'is even worse.'}) 48... Rxf3 49. Rh5 {Mikhail Tal: 'This creates the most serious problems for Black.' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Bulletin: 'Mikhail Tal: 'This creates the most serious problems for Black.'''} Rxf4 50. Rg5+ Kh3 51. Ke3 Rf1 52. Ke2 {Mikhail Tal: 'Black's task is no longer complicated.' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Bulletin: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Black's task is no longer complicated.'''} ({Mikhail Tal: 'The main variation would be'} 52. Rg6 c5 53. Rc6 Kg3 54. Rg6+ Kh4 55. Rc6 f4+ {Mikhail Tal: '!'} 56. Ke4 (56. Ke2 Rc1 57. Kf3 Kg5) 56... Kg5 $1 57. Rxc5+ Kg4 $19 {Mikhail Tal: 'and before us is a position which is already theoretically decided.'}) 52... Kh4 $1 {Mikhail Tal: 'This wins an important tempo which strengthens Black's position. A phase of purely technical play follows, for which no further commentary is necessary.' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Bulletin: '!' Bulletin: 'Mikhail Tal: 'This wins an important tempo which strengthens Black's position. A phase of purely technical play follows, for which no further commentary is necessary.'''} 53. Rg6 Rc1 54. Kf3 Rc4 55. Ke3 c5 56. Kf3 Rg4 57. Rc6 c4 58. Rc5 Kg5 {'Black prepares f4 Bulletin: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Black prepares f4''''} 59. Rc6 Re4 60. Rc8 (60. Rc5 {(Komodo 9 64-bit (20s)) doesn't improve anything} Kf6 61. Kf2 Ke6 $19) 60... Kf6 61. Rc5 Ke6 62. Kg2 (62. Ra5 {(Komodo 9 64-bit (20s)) there is nothing better in the position} Re5 63. Ra7 $19) 62... f4 63. Kf3 Rd4 64. Rc7 Kd5 65. Rc8 Rd3+ 66. Kxf4 c3 67. Rc7 Kd4 68. Rc8 Rd2 69. Rd8+ {Komodo 9 64-bit (20s)} Kc4 70. Rc8+ Kd3 71. Rd8+ Ke2 72. Re8+ Kd1 73. Rh8 c2 74. Rh1+ Ke2 75. Ke4 Rd8 76. Ke5 Rd1 77. Rh2+ Kd3 78. Rh3+ Kc4 79. Rh6 Kb5 80. Rh8 c1=Q 81. Rb8+ Ka6 82. Ra8+ Kb7 83. Ra4 Qg5+ 84. Ke4 Re1+ 85. Kd3 Qe3+ 86. Kc4 Rc1+ 87. Kd5 Rd1+ 88. Kc4 Rd4+ 89. Kc5 Qe5# {Bulletin: '0-1 (89) Ivkov,B-Tal,M 40: Bled 1961 Life and Games of Tal [Mikhail Tal]'} 0-1

