{Unsurprisingly Tal, emaciated yet full of energy, featured in many players' memories about the tournament. ("He was a walking god," said Tibor Karolyi jr. , and the admiration for him among ordinary Estonians was remarkable. Though when he was described as a living legend he corrected it and said "a barely-living legend!") Kalle Kiik, a Tartu University student competing in his first big tournament, was at the tail of the field when he faced Tal in the tenth round. Yet the youngster outplayed the legend until in mutual time trouble disaster struck. Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Unsurprisingly Tal, emaciated yet full of energy, featured in many players' memories about the tournament. ("He was a walking god," said Tibor Karolyi jr. , and the admiration for him among ordinary Estonians was remarkable. Though when he was described as a living legend he corrected it and said "a barely-living legend!") Kalle Kiik, a Tartu University student competing in his first big tournament, was at the tail of the field when he faced Tal in the tenth round. Yet the youngster outplayed the legend until in mutual time trouble disaster struck.' ChessCalisthenics: 'B82: Sicilian Scheveningen: 6 f4'' Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Unsurprisingly Tal, emaciated yet full of energy, featured in many players' memories about the tournament. ("He was a walking god," said Tibor Karolyi jr. , and the admiration for him among ordinary Estonians was remarkable. Though when he was described as a living legend he corrected it and said "a barely-living legend!") Kalle Kiik, a Tartu University student competing in his first big tournament, was at the tail of the field when he faced Tal in the tenth round. Yet the youngster outplayed the legend until in mutual time trouble disaster struck.''} 1. e4 {Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian'} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. f4 e6 7. a4 $5 (7. Qf3 {Glek,Igor 2395 - Itkis,Boris 2300, USSR 1985 - 39/  (287) Kiik,K: '(Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian) G