Ian: ' Rfb1+-''}) 32... bxc6 33. Ne7+ Rdxe7 34. dxe7 Rxe7 $2 (34... Bf6 35. Rxc6 Qd7 36. Rc7 Qb5 37. Rc8 Qd7 38. Rxe8+ Qxe8 39. Rxf6 gxf6 40. Qc7 { Qd8+- Kiik,K: ' d8+- Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: ' Qd8+-''}) (34... Qe6 35. Qxe6 fxe6 36. Rxc6 Bf6 37. Rxe6 Kf7 38. Rxa6 (38. Rfe1 Rxe7 39. Rxe7+ Bxe7 40. Ra1 h5 $1 41. Rxa6 g6 $11) 38... Rxe7 $16 {Hermlin,Aarne,  Kiik,Kalle Kiik,K: 'Hermlin,  Kiik,K Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Hermlin,Aarne,  Kiik,Kalle' Hermlin,  Kiik,K'}) 35. Rxc6 Qd7 {Diagram [#] Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Diagram [#]''} 36. Rxf7 $4 ({Instead, White should win after Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Instead, White should win after''} 36. Rc8+ {Kiik,K: 'ChessCalisthenics: '''} Re8 37. Rxe8+ Qxe8 38. Re1 $18 {winning the bishop soon. Unfortunately, Kiik saw a different combination and played a losing rook move. Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'winning the bishop soon. Unfortunately, Kiik saw a different combination and played a losing rook move.'' Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'winning the bishop soon. Unfortunately, Kiik saw a different combination and played a losing rook move.''}) 36... Qxc6 $1 {A really strong rejoinder. Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'A really strong rejoinder.''} 37. Rxg7+ $4 {So, Kiik decided to pick up an extra pawn, only to discover that after Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'So, Kiik decided to pick up an extra pawn, only to discover that after'' Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'So, Kiik decided to pick up an extra pawn, only to discover that after''} ({Now Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Now''} 37. Qxc6 $11 {and Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'and''} Kxf7 {Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian'} 38. Qxa6 $11 {is only a draw.}) 37... Kxg7 38. Qxc6 {Diagram [#] Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Diagram [#]''} Rc7 $1 {it is White who had to resign. The evening after the tournament, Kiik's second Aarne Hermlin brought Kiik to meet his old friend Tal in Tal's hotel room. After greetings in Russian, Tal said to Kiik: "You could have beaten me." Then, after a long pause, he added: "But you didn't." Kiik says he has never forgotten the message in Tal's words, suggesting to him that he did not fight hard enough until the very last move. Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: '!' Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'it is White who had to resign. The evening after the tournament, Kiik's second Aarne Hermlin brought Kiik to meet his old friend Tal in Tal's hotel room. After greetings in Russian, Tal said to Kiik: "You could have beaten me." Then, after a long pause, he added: "But you didn't." Kiik says he has never forgotten the message in Tal's words, suggesting to him that he did not fight hard enough until the very last move.'' Kiik,K: 'Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: '!' Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'it is White who had to resign. The evening after the tournament, Kiik's second Aarne Hermlin brought Kiik to meet his old friend Tal in Tal's hotel room. After greetings in Russian, Tal said to Kiik: "You could have beaten me." Then, after a long pause, he added: "But you didn't." Kiik says he has never forgotten the message in Tal's words, suggesting to him that he did not fight hard enough until the very last move.''} 39. Qxc7+ Bxc7 $19 {0-1 (39) Kiik,K-Tal,M Tallinn 39/287 1985 CI1-130 [Kiik,K]} 0-1

