{GM Mihail Marin: 'Another typical situation with the same endgame structure features knights on both sides (instead of knight versus bishop) with or without rooks on board. In the following game another World champion (true, former already) found himself in big trouble.'} 1. d4 {GM Mihail Marin} Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. g3 d5 4. Bg2 Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. c4 dxc4 7. Qc2 a6 8. Qxc4 b5 9. Qc2 Bb7 10. Bg5 Nbd7 11. Nbd2 Rc8 12. Bxf6 Nxf6 13. Nb3 Be4 14. Qc3 Nd5 15. Qd2 c5 16. Nxc5 Bxc5 17. dxc5 Rxc5 18. Rac1 Rxc1 19. Rxc1 {GM Mihail Marin: '[#]'} Nf6 $6 {GM Mihail Marin: 'This move leads to a very pleasant ending for White. The game is, however, suggestive of Black's defensive resources.' This move leads to a very pleasant ending for White. The game is, however, suggestive for Black's defensive resources. Dieser Zug führt zu einem sehr angenehmen Endspiel für Weiß. Die Partie ist jedoch lehrreich, weil sie die Verteidigungsressourcen von Schwarz zeigt.} 20. Qxd8 Rxd8 21. Ne5 Bxg2 22. Kxg2 Ne8 $1 {GM Mihail Marin: '!?' GM Mihail Marin: 'Facing a difficult position, Tal starts defending very accurately. The knight seems passive on e8, of course, but it serves the concrete purpose of defending the crucial c7 and d6 squares, thus preventing the penetration of the white rook.' Facing a difficult position, Tal starts defending very accurately. The knight seems passive on e8, of course, but it serves the concrete purpose of defending the crucial c7 and d6 squares, thus preventing the penetration of the white rook. In dieser schwierigen Situation beginnt Tal, sich sehr genau zu verteidigen. Der Springer scheint auf e8 passiv zu stehen, aber er muß die wichtigen Felder c7 und d6 verteidigen, damit der weiße Turm nicht in die Stellung eindringen kann.} 23. Nd3 (23. Rc6 {would allow sufficient counterplay with würde ausreichendes Gegenspiel erlauben, mit} Rd2) 23... Kf8 {GM Mihail Marin: 'The next emergency is to bring the king to the center. Black has to compensate by a material superiority the better coordination of the white army.' The next emergency is to bring the king to the centre. Black has to compensate by a material superiority the better coordination of the white army. Jetzt ist wichtig, den König ins Zentrum zu bringen. Schwarz muß durch eine zeitweise materielle Überlegenheit die bessere Koordination der weißen Figuren kompensieren.} 24. Rc6 Rd6 25. Rc8 Ke7 {GM Mihail Marin: '[#]'} 26. Rb8 $1 {GM Mihail Marin: 'The b-line offers the best mobility to the rook.' The b-line offers the best mobility to the rook. Die b-Linie bietet dem Turm die besten Chancen auf aktives Spiel.} ({GM Mihail Marin: 'For instance, after' For instance, after Z.B., nach} 26. Ra8 Nc7 {GM Mihail Marin: 'the rook would be quite restricted in its actions.' the rook would be quite restricted in its actions. würde der Turm in seine Bewegungsfreiheit sehr eingeschränkt sein.}) 26... Nc7 ({GM Mihail Marin: 'The first example of White's superior coordination is' A first example of White's superior coordination is Ein erstes Beispiel des hervorragenden Zusammenspiels der weißen Figuren ist:} 26... Kd7 $2 27. Ne5+ Ke7 28. Rb7+ $16 Kf6 $6 29. f4 $1 $18) 27. f4 {GM Mihail Marin: 'Using this moment of "respiro", White wins space in the center.' Using this moment of "respiro", White wijs space in the centre. Weiß gewinnt Raum im Zentrum.} Rd8 28. Rb7 $1 (28. Rb6 {GM Mihail Marin: 'would lead nowhere:' would lead nowhere: würde zu nichts führen:} Rd6 $1) 28... Kd7 29. Rb6 {GM Mihail Marin: 'It is remarkable how invulnerable the white rook feels, although optically it is surrounded by enemy forces.' It is remarkable how invulnerable the white rook feels, although optically it is surrounded by enemy forces. Bemerkenswert ist, wie unverletzbar der weiße Turm ist, obwohl er von den gegnerischen Streitkräften umzingelt ist.} Kc8 {GM Mihail Marin: 'Tal prepares the activation of the rook.' Tal prepares the activation of the rook. Tal bereitet die Aktivierung des Turmes vor.} ({GM Mihail Marin: 'Black has to be very careful. White's domination can irrump from one moment to another into tactical fireworks:' Black has to be very careful. White's domination can irrump from one moment to another into tactical fireworks: Schwarz muß sehr sorgfältig sein. Die Überlegenheit von Weiß kann sich von einem Augenblick zum nächsten in einem taktischen Feuerwerk entladen:} 29... a5 $6 30. Ne5+ Kc8 31. Nc6 Rd6 (31... Rd2 $2 {GM Mihail Marin: 'loses the rook to'} 32. Rb8+ Kd7 33. Rd8+ $18) 32. Rb8+ Kd7 33. Ne5+ Ke7 34. Rb7 {GM Mihail Marin: 'and Black loses material for instance'} Kd8 35. Nxf7+ $18) 30. Kf3 {GM Mihail Marin: '[#]'} ({Better chances of maintaining the advantage would have offered Bessere Chancen, den Vorteil zu behalten würde} 30. b4 {blocking the queenside pawns. Black's best tentative of counterplay would have been bieten, mit der Blockade der Damenflügelbauern. Der beste Versuch von Schwarz, Gegenspiel zu erlangen, wäre} Rd4 31. a3 Rc4 32. Nc5 Rc3 ({possibly better would be wahrscheinlich würde besser sein:} 32... a5 33. Nb7 $1 Rc2 $8 34. bxa5 Rxe2+ 35. Kh3 {when in connection with the threats d6xf7 or a6-a7, White retains the initiative. und in Verbindung mit den Drohungen d6xf7 oder a6-a7 bleibt die Initiative bei Weiß.}) 33. Nxa6 Rxa3 (33... Nxa6 34. Rxa6 Kb7 35. Ra5 Kb6 36. Ra8 $16 {g8 g8}) 34. Rb8+ (34. Nxc7 Kxc7 35. Rxb5 {would avoid any risk, but would also reduce the winning chances. würde jedes Risiko vermeiden, aber auch die Gewinnchancen verringern.}) 34... Kd7 35. Nc5+ Kc6 36. Rf8 Rb3 37. Nd3 $1 f5 38. Rf7 {and the h-pawn will be at least as dangerous as b5. und der h-Bauer wird letztendlich genauso gefährlich wie der b5 sein.}) 30... a5 $5 {GM Mihail Marin: 'Black cannot wait passively until White builds up a massive space advantage with g4-g5.'} 31. b3 {GM Mihail Marin: 'preventing 31...a4, which would allow Black to defend both his queenside pawns.' preventing 31...a4, which would allow Black to defend both his queen side pawns. verhindert 31...a4, womit Schwarz seine beiden Damenflügelbauern decken könnte.} Rd5 32. Ne5 {GM Mihail Marin: 'This active continuation should have offered White a large advantage after Black's inaccurate defense.'} ({GM Mihail Marin: 'There was nothing wrong with the neutral'} 32. g4 $5) 32... f6 33. Nc6 {[%cal Yc6e7,Ye7d5,Rc6a5]} Rd6 {GM Mihail Marin: '?!'} (33... Rh5 {(GM Mihail Marin) offered better chances for successful defense.} 34. Nxa5 (34. h4 b4 $11 {allows Black consolidating.}) 34... Rxh2 35. Nc6 Rh5 {True, White's position remains more pleasant, but at least Black would have had exchanged one of his weak pawns.} 36. Na7+ Kd7 37. Rb7 Kd6 38. b4 {and Black keeps being tied up to the defense of the b5-pawn with his pieces enjoying a narrow mobility.}) {GM Mihail Marin: '[#]'} 34. Na7+ $6 {GM Mihail Marin: 'Having reached a maximum of activity, Larsen should have transformed it in some concrete advantage, such as a small material gain. He might have forgotten that this kind of domination with an inferior number of pieces tend to evaporate.' Having reached a maximum of activity, Larsen should have transformed it in some concrete advantage, such as a small material gain. He might have forgotten that this kind of domination with an inferior number of pieces tend to evaporate. Larsen hat die größtmögliche Aktivität erreicht und sollte sie in einen konkreten Vorteil umwandeln, wie z.B. einen kleinen Materialgewinn. Vielleicht hat er unterschätzt, dass sich diese Art von Vorteil mit wenigen Figuren auflösen kann.} (34. Rb8+ $1 Kd7 35. Nxa5 {GM Mihail Marin: 'when' when wenn} Rd2 36. a4 Ra2 {GM Mihail Marin: 'would fail to' would fail to würde verlieren wegen} 37. Nb7 $1 $16 {GM Mihail Marin: 'indirectly defending a4.'}) 34... Kd7 35. Rb7 Rd5 {GM Mihail Marin: '!'} ({Larsen might have underestimated this move. If} 35... b4 {GM Mihail Marin} 36. Nb5 Rc6 37. Ra7 {Wite soon wins the a5-pawn. with some practical chances to convert it.}) {GM Mihail Marin: '[#]'} 36. a4 {GM Mihail Marin: '?!'} ({This leads to an obvious draw. White would have retained the long-term control with} 36. a3 $1 {(GM Mihail Marin) immobilizing both black queenside pawns.}) 36... bxa4 37. bxa4 Kd8 38. e3 Rc5 39. Nb5 Kc8 ({GM Mihail Marin: 'Black could have already forced a draw with' Black could have already forced a draw with Schwarz hätte schon ein forciertes Remis haben können mit} 39... Nxb5 40. axb5 Rc7 41. Rb8+ Rc8 $11) 40. Nd6+ Kd7 41. Ne4 Rc4 42. Ra7 f5 ({Tricks such as Fallen wie} 42... Rxa4 $4 43. Nc5+ {will not prevent Black from equalizing the position completely. hindern Schwarz nicht daran, die Stellung vollständig auszugleichen.}) 43. Nd2 Rxa4 44. Nb3 Ra2 45. h4 a4 46. Rxa4 $1 1/2-1/2

