1. d4 {ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena'} Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 O-O 5. Nf3 d6 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5 Ne7 9. Ne1 Nd7 10. f3 f5 11. g4 h5 $6 {ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: '?!''} 12. g5 (12. h3 {ChessBase} hxg4 13. hxg4 f4 14. Ng2 $13) 12... h4 {[%csl Rg5][%cal Yf5f4] Against anything else White plays 13.h4 and Black's kingside play is over. His minor pieces have no squares and the only way to do anything is ...h8, ...g8, ...f7, ...f8-e7 and a sacrifice on g5; clearly impossible. Now Black wants to play ...f4 as well, and win the g5; but this is too slow.  ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: 'Against anything else White plays 13.h4 and Black's kingside play is over. His minor pieces have no squares and the only way to do anything is ...h8, ...g8, ...f7, ...f8-e7 and a sacrifice on g5; clearly impossible. Now Black wants to play ...f4 as well, and win the g5; but this is too slow. ''} 13. Nd3 f4 (13... Kf7 {[%cal Ye7g8] ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena'} 14. c5 $1 f4 (14... dxc5 $2 15. Qb3 Ke8 16. f4 $1 $40 {begins to look like GM-Amateur; Black will soon be crushed.}) 15. Qb3 b6 16. cxd6 cxd6 17. Qa3 $14 {Sanguinetti-Szmetan, Argentina 1974. White is well ahead in his attack.}) (13... c6 {ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena' does not work in this instance. The kingside is securely blocked for now, so White can focus his attention on the queenside.} 14. Kh1 cxd5 (14... b5 15. Nb4 $16) 15. cxd5 a6 16. Be3 $16) 14. Kh1 {ChessBase: '!' '!' '!'} (14. Qe1 {ChessBase} Kf7 15. Kh1 Rh8 16. Rg1 Nf8 17. c5 Bd7 18. b3 Rh5 $36 {0-1 (56) Wade,R-Reshevsky,S Buenos Aires 1960}) 14... Kf7 $6 {[%csl Rg5][%cal Ye7g8,Yd8g5] ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: '?!'' Black must clear the g8-square for his e7 to move there, so that the  attacks the g5, but... ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: 'Black must clear the g8-square for his e7 to move there, so that the  attacks the g5, but...''} (14... a5 {ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena'} 15. Bd2 Kf7 (15... b6 16. Be1 $16 {[%cal Ye1f2,Ya2a3,Yb2b4,Yc4c5] is similar}) 16. Be1 Rh8 17. Bf2 b6 18. a3 Ba6 19. Ne1 $16 {[%cal Yb2b4] and White's play proceeds unhindered.}) 15. c5 Rh8 {The captures on c5 both allow White too much play: ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: 'The captures on c5 both allow White too much play:''} (15... Nxc5 {ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena'} 16. Nxc5 dxc5 17. Qb3 Ke8 18. Qb5+ Kf7 19. Qxc5 $14 {Markos}) (15... dxc5 {ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena'} 16. Qb3 Ke8 17. Qa4 $44 {Markos; in both cases White's compensation is very good.}) 16. Qb3 {ChessBase: '' '' ''} ({The most forceful continuation here was ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: 'The most forceful continuation here was''} 16. cxd6 $1 {ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: '!''} cxd6 17. Nb5 Nb6 {ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena'} (17... Qb6 $6 {ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena'} 18. Qa4 a6 19. Qa3 $16 {Markos}) (17... Nf8 {ChessBase} 18. Qb3 $18) {and now White has the powerful typical sac} 18. Nxf4 $1 exf4 19. Bxf4 $16 {[%csl Rd6] when Black's pieces are totally uncoordinated, for example} Kg8 20. Nxd6 Kh7 21. Qd2 Rf8 22. Rac1 Bxb2 23. Qxb2 Rxf4 24. Qe5 Rf8 25. f4 $40 {with a powerful attack.}) (16. Nb5 {ChessBase} Nxc5 17. Nxc5 dxc5 18. b4 $1 $16 {Tal}) 16... b6 17. cxd6 cxd6 18. Qa3 Nc5 19. Nxc5 bxc5 20. b4 $14 {ChessBase: '' '' '' ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: '''} cxb4 21. Qxb4 {Black has been thrown on to the defensive. ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: 'Black has been thrown on to the defensive.''} Bh3 22. Rg1 Rb8 23. Nb5 Nc8 24. Ba3 Bf8 {ChessBase: '[#]'} 25. Qc4 {ChessBase: '?' '?' '?'} (25. Rac1 {ChessBase} a6) (25. Qc3 $1 $16 {ChessBase} Be7 26. Nc7 $16) 25... Be7 26. Qc7 (26. Nc7 {ChessBase} Nb6 27. Qc2 Rc8 $11) 26... Qxc7 27. Nxc7 Rh5 28. Bf1 Bxf1 (28... Bd7 {ChessBase} 29. Ne6 Nb6 (29... Bxe6 30. dxe6+ Kxe6 31. Bh3+ $16) 30. Rc1 Rhh8 31. Ba6 Na8 $11) 29. Rgxf1 Rxg5 30. Ne6 Rh5 31. Rac1 Kf6 (31... h3 {ChessBase}) 32. Rc7 Rh8 33. Rfc1 {The difference in coordination is evident. ChessBase: 'Dembo,Yelena: 'The difference in coordination is evident.''} (33. h3 {ChessBase} Nb6 34. Nxf4 (34. Rx