1. c4 c5 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. e3 Nc6 5. Ne2 d6 6. Nbc3 Bd7 7. b3 (7. O-O Qc8 $5) (7. d4 $5) 7... a6 8. Bb2 b5 9. d3 Rb8 10. Qd2 Qa5 ({Nigel Davies: 'The natural move was''The natural move was Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: 'The natural move was'''} 10... Nf6 $5 {Nigel Davies: 'though Tal might not have liked''though Tal might not have liked Larsen,Bent: '!?' Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: 'though Tal might not have liked'''} 11. Nd5 {.}) 11. O-O Nf6 12. Rad1 e6 $6 {Nigel Davies: 'This seriously weakens the dark squares and allows Larsen a powerful reply.''This seriously weakens the dark squares and allows Larsen a powerful reply. Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: 'This seriously weakens the dark squares and allows Larsen a powerful reply.'''} (12... O-O {Nigel Davies: 'when White has an interesting line in''when White has an interesting line in Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: 'when White has an interesting line in'''} 13. Nd5 $14 (13. Bxc6 $6 {Nigel Davies: '!?' '!?''Larsen,Bent: '?!' Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: '!?'''} Bxc6 14. Nd5 Qd8 15. Nxf6+ Bxf6 16. Bxf6 exf6 17. e4 f5 $1 {Nigel Davies: 'Larsen,Bent: '!''} 18. exf5 Qf6 19. Qf4 {, which seems to be a bit better for him.})) 13. d4 O-O (13... bxc4 14. dxc5 d5 (14... Qxc5 15. Na4) 15. e4) 14. dxc5 (14. d5 $1 {Nigel Davies: 'is also worth considering here, for example Larsen,Bent: '!''} exd5 15. Nxd5 Qxd2 (15... Nxd5 16. Bxg7 Kxg7 17. Qb2+ f6 18. Rxd5 {is also very good}) 16. Rxd2 Ne8 17. Bxg7 Kxg7 18. Rc1 {gives White the better endgame.}) 14... dxc5 15. cxb5 axb5 16. a4 {Nigel Davies: 'This leads to the break up the duo of pawns on b5 and c5 and opens the b2-h8 diagonal.''This leads to the break up the duo of pawns on b5 and c5 and opens the b2-h8 diagonal. Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: 'This leads to the break up the duo of pawns on b5 and c5 and opens the b2-h8 diagonal.'''} bxa4 17. Nxa4 Nb4 $1 18. Be5 ({Nigel Davies: 'And not''And not Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: 'And not'''} 18. Bxf6 $2 Bxf6 19. Qxd7 {Nigel Davies: 'because of''because of Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: 'because of'''} Rfd8 20. Nxc5 (20. Nb6 {is necessary, but better for Black after he takes it with his queen}) 20... Qxc5 21. Qa4 Rxd1 22. Rxd1 Qc2 $19 {Nigel Davies: 'Larsen,Bent: '-+''} 23. Re1 Qd2 24. Kf1 Nd3 25. Rb1 Qc2 {winning material.}) 18... Rbd8 ({In his brilliant youth Tal might well have played} 18... Bxa4 $1 {after which} 19. Bxb8 Bxb3 20. Ra1 Ne4 21. Rxa5 Nxd2 22. Bd6 Re8 23. Bxc5 Nd3 24. Nc1 Nxc5 25. Rxc5 Nxf1 26. Nxb3 Rb8 27. Bxf1 Rxb3 {sees Black thread his way through the complications to equality.}) 19. Qb2 Bxa4 20. Rxd8 Rxd8 21. bxa4 $14 Ne8 ({After} 21... Nd3 22. Qc3 Qxc3 23. Bxc3 Nd5 24. Bxg7 Kxg7 25. Ra1 {White is better because of the passed a-pawn. But this might have been better than the game.}) 22. Bxg7 Nxg7 23. Nc3 Nd3 24. Qc2 Nb4 $138 {Nigel Davies: 'A sub optimal move in time trouble.''A sub optimal move in time trouble. Larsen,Bent: '' Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: 'A sub optimal move in time trouble.'''} 25. Qe4 $6 ({White in turn should probably have played the sensible} 25. Qb3 {.}) 25... Nd3 26. Qc4 Ne5 27. Qb3 c4 28. Qc2 f5 $2 {Nigel Davies: '?!' '?!''Larsen,Bent: '?' Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: '?!'''} (28... Nf5 {would have been much sounder, the text weakens Black's kingside.}) 29. Rb1 Rd3 30. Rc1 $1 Ne8 31. Qb2 Nd6 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'Larsen,Bent: '?''} 32. Ne2 Rb3 33. Qd4 Rd3 {Nigel Davies: '?!' '?!''Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: '?!'''} (33... Ndf7 {was better.}) 34. Qa1 Rd2 $2 {Nigel Davies: 'Larsen,Bent: '?''} 35. Nd4 $1 $18 {Nigel Davies: '!' '!''Larsen,Bent: '+-!' Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: '!'''} Nd3 {Nigel Davies: '?' '?''Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: '?'''} ({And here Black should play} 35... Kf7 {.}) 36. Nc6 Qc7 (36... Nxc1 37. Qxc1 $1 {Nigel Davies: 'makes it impossible for Black to defend his rook.''makes it impossible for Black to defend his rook. Larsen,Bent: 'Nigel Davies: 'makes it impossible for Black to defend his rook.'''}) 37. Rb1 Rxf2 38. Rb8+ Kf7 39. Nd8+ Ke8 40. Bc6+ 