{Leitao,Rafael: 'Not even the great Mihail Tal escaped against the young Mecking. I quite like how my childhood idol managed to outplay the legendary World Champion in an equal endgame.'} 1. e4 {Leitao,Rafael} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 {Leitao,Rafael: 'As I mentioned before, the Brazilian was a strong theoretician and was not afraid to go for the main lines.'} e6 7. f4 Qb6 8. Qd2 Qxb2 9. Nb3 Qa3 10. Bxf6 gxf6 11. Be2 Nc6 (11... h5 12. O-O Nc6) 12. O-O (12. Bh5 Na5 13. f5 $13) 12... h5 13. Nb1 (13. Kh1) 13... Qb4 $5 {!?} (13... Qb2 $6 {?!} 14. a3 (14. a4)) (13... Qa4) 14. Qe3 d5 (14... f5 15. exf5 Ne7 $13) 15. exd5 Ne7 {Leitao,Rafael: 'Even back then the theory of the Poisoned Pawn Variation was going very deep.'} 16. Nc3 {!} (16. c4 $2 {?!} Nf5 17. Qf2 a5 $17 18. N1d2 a4 19. a3 Qc3 20. Rfc1 Qe3 $15) ({and} 16. dxe6 {(Leitao,Rafael) are also possible.}) 16... Nf5 17. Qd3 Qb6+ 18. Rf2 $1 {!} (18. Kh1 {?!} h4 19. Bg4 Ne3 20. Na4 Qa7) 18... Qe3 (18... Bd6 {Leitao,Rafael !?} 19. Qd2 (19. Ne4 Bxf4 $13) 19... Qe3 20. Qxe3 $14) 19. Ne4 $1 {!} Qxd3 (19... Be7 {!?}) 20. Bxd3 {Leitao,Rafael: ' After so much fireworks we arrive to an endgame that is close to equality.'} Be7 21. Re1 $14 {! 'with the idea' 22.Nf6} Kf8 22. dxe6 Bxe6 {!?} (22... fxe6 {?!} 23. Nec5 Nd4 (23... Kf7 {Leitao,Rafael} 24. Bc4 (24. Rfe2 {?!} Nd4 {!}) 24... b5 (24... Nd4 25. f5 $18 {!}) 25. Bxe6+ Bxe6 26. Nxe6 $11 {''}) 24. Bc4 $18) 23. Nec5 Nd4 {Leitao,Rafael: '!'} 24. Nxe6+ Nxe6 25. Bf5 Nc7 {Leitao,Rafael: 'Diagram [#]'} (25... Rd8 {Leitao,Rafael} 26. Bxe6 fxe6 27. Rxe6 Rd1+ 28. Rf1 Rd7 $11 {/}) (25... Ng7 {!?} 26. Be4 Rb8 27. Rd1 Ne6) 26. Rd1 {Leitao,Rafael: '!'} Nb5 $1 {!} (26... Rd8 27. Rxd8+ Bxd8 28. Rd2 Ne6 29. Rd7 b5 30. Bxe6 Bb6+ 31. Kf1 fxe6 32. g3 $18 {!}) 27. Rd7 Rd8 $16 28. c4 $6 {!?} (28. Rfd2 Rxd7 29. Rxd7 Nd6 30. Bh3 Ke8 $16 {''}) (28. Rxb7 {?} Nd6) 28... Nd6 29. Rxd8+ Bxd8 30. Bd3 b6 31. Rd2 (31. c5 $6 {!?} bxc5 32. Rc2 (32. Nxc5 a5 33. Rb2)) 31... Bc7 32. Kf2 Kg7 33. Kf3 Re8 $1 {!} 34. Re2 $2 $138 (34. Nd4 $16 {!?}) (34. g3 {!?}) 34... Rd8 35. Rd2 (35. Re7 Ne8 {!} (35... Bb8 36. c5 {!}) 36. Re3) 35... Nb7 {?!} 36. Be4 Rxd2 {?} (36... Nd6) 37. Nxd2 Nc5 38. h4 $1 {Leitao,Rafael: 'Fixing the weakness on h5. A very well played game until now. One slip and Black is in grave danger.' !} Bd6 $4 {Leitao,Rafael: '?!' Leitao,Rafael: 'Diagram [#]'} (38... Ne6 {Leitao,Rafael: 'with a probable draw. If White plays g3 it is no longer possible to execute the manoeuvre that occurred in the game.' %03'better is'} 39. g3 Bd6 $16) 39. Nf1 {Leitao,Rafael: '!' Leitao,Rafael: 'A nice move that is made even stronger by the unfortunate position of the bishop on d6. The knight is heading to g3.'} Bc7 (39... Ne6 {Leitao,Rafael} 40. Ng3 $1) 40. Ng3 Kh6 41. Nf5+ Kh7 42. Ng3+ {Leitao,Rafael: 'Why almost all great players like to repeat moves in winning technical positions? Surely this is not a coincidence.'} Kh6 43. Bc2 $1 {!} Ne6 44. Nf5+ Kh7 45. g3 {Leitao,Rafael: 'The red carpet is prepared for the White's king walk.'} Ng7 $8 (45... Nc5 {Leitao,Rafael} 46. Ke3 $18) (45... Kg8 46. Ne7+ Kf8 47. Nd5 Bd8 48. Ke4 Nc5+ 49. Kf5 (49. Kd4) 49... Nb7 {!}) 46. Ne7+ Kh8 (46... Kh6 $2 {Leitao,Rafael} 47. Ng8# {#}) 47. Nd5 $1 {!} Bd8 48. Ke4 $18 Ne6 (48... Kg8 {!?}) 49. Bd1 (49. Nb4 $18 {Leitao,Rafael}) 49... Ng7 (49... Nc5+ {Leitao,Rafael} 50. Ke3 $18) 50. Nb4 $1 a5 51. Nd5 Kg8 52. Nc3 Kf8 53. Bc2 {Leitao,Rafael: '!' Leitao,Rafael: 'A precise prophylactic move.'} (53. Kd5 {Leitao,Rafael} Nf5) 53... Ke7 54. Kd5 Kd7 55. Ba4+ Ke7 (55... Kc7 {Leitao,Rafael} 56. Nb5+ $18 {'with the idea' 57.Nd6}) 56. Bc2 Kd7 57. Ba4+ Ke7 58. Kc6 Nf5 59. Nd5+ Ke6 60. Nxb6 Nd4+ (60... Nxg3 61. c5 { b3+-} f5 (61... Ne4 62. f5+ {!} Kxf5 63. Bc2 $18) 62. Bb3+ Ke7 63. Nc8+ Kf8 64. Kd7 $18) 61. Kb7 Kd6 62. Nd7 Ne6 63. Kc8 Be7 64. Bd1 {Leitao,Rafael: 'A truly great technical game! RR This game is published in Chess Informant 19/481'} 1-0

