{[%mdl 8192] B86: Sicilian Scheveningen/Najdorf: 6 Bc4, without early ...b5} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. Bc4 Be7 7. Bb3 O-O 8. f4 Na6 9. Qf3 Nc5 10. Be3 d5 11. exd5 exd5 12. O-O Re8 13. h3 Nce4 14. Nxe4 dxe4 15. Qe2 Nd5 {last book move} 16. Rad1 Nxe3 17. Qxe3 {Black has the pair of bishops} Bc5 18. f5 Qf6 19. Kh1 Bd7 20. Qc3 Bd6 21. Ne6 Be5 {Black threatens to win material: Be5xc3} 22. Qe3 Re7 23. Nc5 Qb6 24. Qg5 {White threatens to win material: Qg5xe7} Bf6 25. Nxd7 Rxd7 {Opposite coloured bishops appeared} 26. Qf4 {White threatens to win material: Qf4xe4} Re7 {[%cal Ye4e3] Black prepares the advance e3} 27. Rfe1 e3 {Is this a dangerous pawn?} 28. c3 {Prevents intrusion on d4} h5 29. Re2 Rae8 30. Qd6 Qb5 {Black threatens to win material: Qb5xe2} 31. Qd3 {White threatens to win material: Qd3xb5} Qe5 32. Rf1 a6 33. Rf3 b5 34. g3 {Controls h4} Qc5 35. a4 Qb6 36. Qc2 $2 (36. axb5 $142 axb5 37. Bd5 $17) 36... Qb7 37. Kg2 Rd8 38. axb5 axb5 39. Qc1 Bg5 40. h4 Rd2 (40... Bh6 $142 {it becomes clear that Black will call all the shots} 41. f6 Red7 42. fxg7 Rd2 43. Bxf7+ Kxg7 44. Bxh5 Rxe2+ 45. Kh3 Rf8 $19) 41. Qf1 Rxe2+ (41... Rxe2+ 42. Qxe2 Bh6 $19) 0-1

