er Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov'' ! 'with the idea' 30.efQ Kf8 31.Re8# 'with the idea' 30.h7$18} Rb8 (29... Rfc8 $5 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) deserves attention:} 30. Nxc8 Bc6 $1 {Krasenkow,Michal: ''} 31. Nd6 Kh7 32. e8=Q Bxe8 33. Nxe8 Kxh6 34. Nxf6 d4 $132 {with good counter chances}) 30. Nxb7 Rcc8 (30... Re8 {(Knaak,Rainer) Polugaevsky,Lev} 31. Nd6 Rxe7 32. Rxe7 Ne3+ 33. Kh2 Ng4+ 34. Kg3 Nxh6 35. Rxa7 $14 {with only a slight edge for White in the game Naumkin - Nevanlinna, Jyvaskyla 1993. Krasenkow,Michal: '1/2 (58) Naumkin,I (2450)-Nevanlinna,R (2290) Jyvaskyla 1993'}) 31. Nd6 Re8) 27... Rc6 {Krasenkow,Michal: '!' Krasenkow,Michal: '!' Krasenkow,Michal: '!' Belov: '!' '!' Knaak,Rainer: 'Oder'} (27... Rb4 28. a3 $18 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-' '+-'' ''} Rb5 {Knaak,Rainer} 29. Nd6 Nc4 30. Nxb5 Nxd2 31. e7 Re8 32. Nc7 Bc6 33. Re6 Bd7 34. Nxe8 Bxe8 35. Rxf6 Bf7 36. h6 {usw.}) ({Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Polugaevsky gave'''} 27... Na4 $5 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'as the most stubborn continuation. White would have secured winning chances by'''} 28. e7 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: '?!'''} (28. Nd6 $1 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) R.Scherbakov !} Bc6 29. e7) 28... Re8 (28... Kxf7 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) R.Scherbakov} 29. exf8=Q+ Kxf8 30. Rde2 Re4 $1) 29. Nd6 Bc6 30. Nxc4 (30. Nxe8 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) R.Scherbakov} Bxe8 31. Rxd5 {but Black was still fighting after} Kf7) (30. Re3 $5 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) R.Scherbakov}) 30... dxc4 31. Rd6 $16) 28. Rxb2 Re8 $2 {Krasenkow,Michal: '?!' Krasenkow,Michal: '?!' Krasenkow,Michal: '?!' Belov: '?!' '?!'} ({Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'In case of'''} 28... Bc8 $1 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!' '!' Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'White had a pleasant choice:''' Krasenkow,Michal: '' Krasenkow,Michal: 'I.Belov' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!' '!' Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'White had a pleasant choice:''' Krasenkow,Michal: '' Krasenkow,Michal: 'I.Belov' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!' '!' Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'White had a pleasant choice:''' Krasenkow,Michal: '' Krasenkow,Michal: 'I.Belov' Belov: '' '' Knaak,Rainer: 'war notwendig und von einfachem Gewinn kann dann keine Rede sein.'} 29. Nh6+ $1 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!' '!' Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: '!?'''} (29. e7 Re8 30. Nd8 $16 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: ''' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '' '''} Rc7 {Knaak,Rainer Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov''} 31. Rd2 Rcxe7 32. Rxe7 Rxe7 33. Rxd5 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '''}) 29... Kh7 30. Nf5 Rxe6 31. Rc1 $16 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: ''' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '' '' Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'and so on.''' Knaak,Rainer: 'und Schwarz hat viel bessere Verteidigungschancen als in der Partie.'}) (28... Kg7 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) (R.Scherbakov) was losing to} 29. e7 $18 {followed by Nf7-d8. 'with the idea' 30.Nd8$18}) 29. Nh6+ $1 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!' '!' Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Shifting the knight to the dominating position on f5.'''} ({The pawn on e6 could not be saved anyway:} 29. Rbe2 $6 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) R.Scherbakov} Bc8) 29... Kh7 30. Nf5 Rexe6 31. Rxe6 Rxe6 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Black has restored the material balance but it won't make his life easier.'''} 32. Rc2 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: '!'''} Rc6 ({After} 32... Bc6 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) (R.Scherbakov) White would simply improve by} 33. g4 a5 34. f3 {etc.}) 33. Re2 $18 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-' '+-' Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Securing a decisive invasion. White's powerful rook on the 7th rank, combined with no less a powerful knight on f6 and strong h5-passer give Black no chance to survive.'''} Bc8 ({Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Or'''} 33... Rc7 34. Re6 $18 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-' '+-''} Bc8 {Knaak,Rainer Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov''} 35. Rxf6 Bxf5 36. Rxf5 $18) 34. Re7+ Kh8 35. Nh4 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'With a simple idea to give checkmate by 36. Ng6 Kg8 37.h6 and 38.Rg7X''' ! 'with the idea' 36.Ng6 Kg8 37.h6} f5 36. Ng6+ Kg8 37. Rxa7 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Black resigned. Wonderful play by Lev Polugaevsky!'''} 1-0

