fxe4 18. Nxe4 $11 {'with the idea' Nc3} Bc4 19. Re1 b6 $15) 18. Qc2 (18. e5 {?} Qd4+ $17) (18. exf5 {!?} Qd4+ 19. Kh1 Bxf5 20. Ne4 Rbe8 21. Qxd4 Bxd4 22. Nc3 $15) 18... Qh4 {!} (18... Qd4+ {!?} 19. Kh1 Rbd8) 19. Nb3 {?!} (19. Nc4 fxe4 20. Bxe4 Ng5 $1 {!} (20... Bd4+ {!} 21. Kh2 Ng5 $19 {!}) 21. fxg5 (21. Be3) 21... Rxf1+ 22. Kxf1 Rf8+ 23. Kg1 Qe1+ 24. Kh2 Rf1 $19 {Tal}) (19. Be2 fxe4 20. Nxe4 Bd4+ 21. Kh2 Rbe8 $17) (19. exf5 Bd4+ 20. Kh1 Bxf5 21. Be4) 19... fxe4 (19... c4 {!?}) 20. Bxe4 {Raetsky/Chetverik: 'Maybe White was counting on a consolidating move like ...b7-b6 or a knight move like ...Nd6, eyeing the d4-square via f5. However, Tal treated this position more dynamically.' %08DA} Ng5 $1 $19 {Raetsky/Chetverik: '!!' ! 'with the idea' 21... Nh3; |21... Ne4} 21. fxg5 {Raetsky/Chetverik: '?'} (21. Bf3 Nxf3+ 22. Rxf3 c4 $1 {prepares ...Bd4+ and ...Bd5 with a crushing attack.}) ({Much better was} 21. Ra3 $1 {. The knight on b3 is supported and the rook is developed into the game via the third rank. After !} Nxe4 22. Qxe4 Qe7 {Black has the bishop pair in an open position, but his advantage is not yet alarming. After the move in the game White just loses.} 23. Re1 $17) 21... Rxf1+ 22. Kxf1 Rf8+ 23. Bf3 (23. Bf4 Qxf4+ 24. Bf3 Qe3 $19) 23... Bc4+ {Z0} ({Raetsky/Chetverik: 'White resigned as he is mated after'} 23... Bc4+ 24. Kg1 Qe1+ 25. Kh2 Be5+ {Raetsky/Chetverik: 'etc.'}) ({Kg1} 23... Qe1+ $19 {Kh2 Be5+}) 0-1

