{[%mdl 64] C93: Closed Ruy Lopez: Smyslov Variation} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 h6 10. d4 Re8 11. Nbd2 Bf8 12. Nf1 Bb7 13. Ng3 Na5 14. Bc2 Nc4 15. Bd3 Nb6 16. Bd2 c5 17. d5 Bc8 18. Nh2 Na4 19. Rb1 Bd7 20. b3 Nb6 21. c4 Rb8 22. f4 bxc4 23. bxc4 {last book move.} Na4 24. Qc2 exf4 25. Bxf4 Rb4 26. Bd2 Qc7 27. Bxb4 cxb4 {White wins the exchange} 28. Rf1 Be7 29. Kh1 a5 30. Qd2 Nc5 {A sound move} 31. Bc2 Bd8 {[%cal Rc5e4,Re8e4,Rf6e4,Gc2e4,Gg3e4] The pressure on the backward pawn e4 grows} 32. Rbe1 Bc8 33. Nf3 Nfd7 34. e5 $1 {forging ahead of the opponent} Nxe5 (34... dxe5 35. Qf2 {Combination}) (34... Nxe5 35. Nxe5 dxe5 (35... Rxe5 36. Qf2 {Combination}) 36. d6 {Passed pawn}) (34... Z0 $140 35. exd6 {Threat} Qxd6 36. Rxe8+ {Discovered attack}) 35. Qf4 Re7 (35... Ncd7 36. Nf5 Nf6 37. Nxh6+ gxh6 38. Qxh6 Qxc4 39. Qg5+ Kf8 40. Nxe5 Qxc2 41. Rc1 $18) 36. Nd4 (36. Nh5 $142 $5 Ned3 37. Qg3 f5 38. Rxe7 Qxe7 39. Bxd3 Nxd3 $18) 36... Ned3 37. Bxd3 Nxd3 38. Rxe7 $1 {Decoy: e7} Qxe7 (38... Qxe7 39. Ndf5 {Decoy Double attack}) (38... Bxe7 39. Qxf7+ Kh7 (39... Kh8 40. Nh5 {Combination}) 40. Nh5 {Combination}) (38... Z0 $140 39. Qxf7+ {Mate threat}) 39. Qe4 Ne5 40. Nc6 Nxc6 41. dxc6 Qe5 42. Qxe5 dxe5 43. Rd1 Bc7 44. Ne4 Kf8 45. Nd6 Bxd6 46. Rxd6 Ke7 47. Rd5 a4 48. c7 b3 49. axb3 axb3 50. Rxe5+ Kd6 51. Rb5 Kxc7 52. Rxb3 Kc6 53. c5 $1 {Skewer: c8, b3-c3} Be6 (53... Kxc5 54. Rc3+ {Skewer}) 54. Rc3 Bd5 55. Kg1 f5 56. Ra3 Kb7 57. Rg3 g5 58. Re3 Kc6 59. Re7 Kxc5 60. Rh7 g4 61. hxg4 (61. h4 $5 {and White can already relax} Kd6 62. Rxh6+ Ke5 $18) 61... fxg4 62. Rxh6 Bb7 63. Rg6 (63. Rg6 Kd5 64. Rxg4 $18) 1-0

