1. e4 {Ftacnik,L} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Qg4 cxd4 8. Bd3 $1 Qa5 $1 9. Ne2 Ng6 10. h4 $6 (10. Bd2 $5 dxc3 (10... Nxe5 $2 11. Qxg7 Nxd3+ 12. cxd3 Rf8 13. cxd4 Qd8 14. Bb4 Nd7 15. Bxf8 $16) 11. Bxc3 $44 {(Keres)} Qc7 (11... Qb6 12. Bd4) 12. O-O Nc6 13. f4 Bd7 14. Ng3) (10. O-O $142 dxc3 11. h4 (11. f4 Nc6 12. Rb1) 11... Nc6 12. f4 (12. h5 $6 Ncxe5 $1 13. Qg3 Nxd3 14. cxd3 Bd7 $1 (14... Ne7 $142 15. Qxg7 Rg8 16. Qxh7 e5) 15. hxg6 hxg6 $15 16. Bf4 $132) 12... h5 13. Qg3 Nce7 14. Nd4 $44 Bd7) (10. f4) 10... Nc6 11. h5 Ncxe5 $132 12. Qxd4 $6 (12. Qg3 Nxd3+ 13. cxd3 Ne7 14. Qxg7 Rg8 15. Qxh7 $6 (15. Qxd4 Bd7 16. Kf1 Nf5 $17) 15... e5 $1 16. h6 $2 Bf5 17. Qxg8+ Nxg8 18. h7 Bxh7 19. Rxh7 dxc3 {Bronstein}) 12... Nxd3+ 13. cxd3 e5 $17 {Keres} 14. Qe3 d4 15. Qg3 Ne7 16. Qxg7 Rg8 17. Qf6 (17. Qxh7 Be6 18. h6 Rc8 $2 19. Qxg8+ Nxg8 20. h7 $18 {Vainstein}) 17... dxc3 {"Der Bauerngewinn ist in dieser Stellung unwesentlich, jedoch versperrt der Bc3 die c-Linie und schrankt die Entwicklungsmoglichkeit del Lc1 ein." (Slotnik 82)} (17... Rxg2 $2 18. Bg5 $1 Ng8 19. Qg7 $16 {(Bronstein)}) 18. O-O Qc7 19. d4 $1 {"Brilliantly played. After the exchange of the last central pawns, the black king will be stripped naked, and his life now is not valued very highly." (Vainstein 76)} (19. Ng3 Nd5 $1 $17 {(Bronstein)}) 19... Bg4 20. f3 Nd5 21. Qh4 {For Tal, the exchange of Queens was out of the question.} (21. Qxe5+ Qxe5 22. dxe5 Bxh5 $15 {(Bronstein)}) 21... Be6 22. dxe5 Qxe5 23. Re1 Rc8 $1 {"Der Turm soll auf der vierten Reihe vor allem die Felder d4 und f4 kontrollieren." (Bronstein)} 24. Rb1 $1 (24. Nd4 Qg3 $1 25. Qxg3 Rxg3) (24. Nf4 Qd4+ 25. Kh1 Rc6 {(Vainstein 76)}) 24... b6 25. Rb5 a6 26. Rb3 Qg7 $1 (26... Ne3 $2 27. Nf4 $1 $16 {(Bronstein)}) (26... b5 $3 27. Nd4 Qg7 28. Re2 Rc4 29. Nxe6 fxe6 30. Rxe6+ Kd7 31. Qh3 Qxg2+ 32. Qxg2 Rxg2+ 33. Kxg2 Kxe6 $19 {(Vainstein 76)}) 27. Qf2 Rc4 28. h6 Qf6 $6 (28... Qg6 $1 $17 {(Bronstein)}) 29. Nxc3 $1 {"Mit diesem Springeropfer versucht Tal neue Drohungen zu schaffen." (Slotnik 82)} Nxc3 30. Rxb6 {"Tal has eliminated the c3 pawn and opened the maximum number of files and ranks, but this would still be endurable, except that he has also opened the black-squared diagonals, and the black king has to fear for its life." (BSV)} Qd8 $1 31. Rxa6 Rg6 {"Bronstein takes an heroic decision -- to transfer his king to f6, closer to his pieces, so that they should be in direct contact with the king, allowing it to exercise its right to self-defense." (Vainstein 76)} (31... Nd1 $2 32. Qe2 $1 Rxc1 33. Rxe6+ $1 Kd7 34. Re4 $1 $40 {(Bronstein)}) 32. Qb2 Ke7 $1 {"Es klingt sicher seltsam, aber fur den Konig ist f6 das sicherste Feld; dorthin strebt der schwarze Monarch!" (Bronstein)} 33. Ra7+ Kf6 34. Re4 $6 {"Eine entscheidende Verrechnung, die nur erklarlich ist durch die vielen Varianten, die nachzuprufen waren. Nach 34 Le3! hatte Schwarz sehr aufpassen mussen, um den zahlreichen weissen Kombinationen zu begegnen." (Bronstein)} (34. Be3 $142 $1 Qd3 {(Bronstein)} 35. Qb8 $1 Nd5 $1 (35... Rc8 36. Qf4+) (35... Ne2+ 36. Rxe2) 36. Qh8+ Kf5 {(Vainstein 76, Slotnik 82)}) 34... Qd1+ $1 35. Kh2 Rxe4 36. Qxc3+ (36. fxe4 Qh5+ 37. Kg1 Qc5+ $19 {(Bronstein)}) 36... Re5 $1 (36... Qd4 37. Qxd4+ Rxd4 38. Bb2 Rxh6+ 39. Kg1 Rhh4 40. Ra4 Ke5 41. g3) 37. Bf4 (37. Ra5 Qd6 (37... Qe2 $1) 38. Bf4 Bd5 39. Ra6 $1 Rxh6+ 40. Kg1 Qxa6 41. Qxe5+ Kg6 42. Qg5#) (37. f4 Rxh6+ $1 38. Kg3 Qg4+ 39. Kf2 Qe2+ $19 {(Bronstein)}) 37... Qe2 $1 38. Bxe5+ Qxe5+ 39. Qxe5+ Kxe5 40. Ra5+ Kd4 41. Rh5 Bd5 42. Kh3 f5 (42... f5 43. Kh2 Ke3 $1 44. Rxf5 Kf2 $1 {(Bronstein)}) 0-1

