1. e4 {Marin,Mihail Marin,Mihail 1) Tal in Shakhmatyi (Riga) 1963. Reprinted and translated in 2)Kirillov: Michail Tal. Sein Lebenswerk 1962-1973.Chessgate. 2004. S. Band2,S.27-28} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 h6 10. d4 Re8 11. Nbd2 Bf8 12. Nf1 Bd7 13. Ng3 Na5 14. Bc2 c5 15. b3 g6 ({Marin,Mihail: 'The move order relevant for our discussion is'} 15... Nc6 16. d5 {Marin,Mihail} Ne7 17. Be3 {and now 17...g6 would transpose to the game. Another neutral and not really accurate move is} Qc8 18. Qd2 Kh8 19. a4 Nfg8 20. axb5 axb5 21. Rxa8 Qxa8 {The lack of coordination reigning in Black's camp allows the same combination as in the main game, but in an even more favourable form.} 22. Bxc5 dxc5 23. Nxe5 Nf6 24. Nxf7+ Kg8 25. Nd6 Rb8 26. c4 $16 {Jansa,V-Geller,E/Budapest 1970/EXT 2009 (1-0, 83). White has three pawns for a knight and a crushing space advantage.}) 16. Be3 Nc6 17. d5 Ne7 18. Qd2 Kh7 {[#]} 19. Bxc5 $5 {Marin,Mihail: 'This is thematic, very nice, but not necessary.'} (19. a4) (19. c4) ({Since Black has deprived his own knight of the g6-square, the plan based on} 19. Nh2 {Marin,Mihail} Bg7 20. f4 {is very dangerous. Black will have problems maintaining the control of the e5-square.} exf4 21. Bxf4 c4 22. Nf3 Bc8 23. Kh1 Neg8 24. bxc4 bxc4 25. Rab1 $16 {Sigurjonsson,G-Smejkal,J/Raach 1969/EXT 2001 (1-0, 54)}) 19... dxc5 20. Nxe5 Nc8 21. f4 (21. Nxf7 Qe7 22. Ng5+ hxg5 23. e5 Nxd5 24. Qxd5 Nb6 $11) 21... Qe7 22. c4 {Marin,Mihail: 'White has fantastic compensation for the sacrificed piece. All that Black can dream of is to return the piece for two pawns, but that is not easy to achieve.'} Bg7 (22... Nb6) 23. Nf3 (23. Rad1 $1 {Tal} Nd6 (23... Nb6 {Marin,Mihail} 24. Qa5 $44) 24. Bd3) 23... bxc4 (23... Nh5 24. Nxh5 Bxa1 25. e5 $18 {Tal}) 24. bxc4 {Marin,Mihail: '?!' '?!'} (24. e5 $1 {Marin,Mihail} c3 25. Qd1 Ng8 26. d6 $40) 24... Nd6 25. e5 ({Marin,Mihail: 'He may have missed that'} 25. Bd3 {Marin,Mihail: 'allows'} Nfxe4 {Tal Marin,Mihail: '!' '!'} 26. Bxe4 Bxa1 27. Bxg6+ {Marin,Mihail} fxg6 28. Rxe7+ Rxe7 29. Qa5 Rc8 $15) 25... Nxc4 26. Qc3 (26. Qd3 Nb2) 26... Bb5 (26... Nb6) (26... Nxe5 $1 $15 {Marin,Mihail}) 27. Rad1 {Marin,Mihail: '' ''} Rad8 28. d6 Nxd6 29. exd6 Qb7 (29... Qf8 $142 30. Qxc5 {Tal} Rxe1+ 31. Rxe1 Rc8 32. Qf2 Qxd6 $11) 30. Ne5 {[#]} (30. f5) 30... Nd7 $2 (30... Nd5 31. Qf3 Rxd6 32. Kh2 $14) 31. Nh5 $18 Bh8 32. Qg3 Nxe5 33. fxe5 Qd7 {[#]} 34. Nf4 $18 Bxe5 35. Bxg6+ Kh8 36. Bxf7 Bd4+ 37. Rxd4 Rxe1+ 38. Qxe1 Qxf7 39. Qe5+ Qg7 40. Qxc5 Bc6 41. Rd2 1-0

