{[%mdl 64] C47: Scotch Four Knights and Four Knights with 4 g3} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. d4 exd4 5. Nd5 Nb4 6. Nxd4 Nxe4 7. Nf5 c6 8. Nxb4 Bxb4+ 9. c3 Qf6 10. Qf3 Nxc3 11. a3 Ba5 {last book move. Black's piece can't move: c8} 12. Bd2 d5 13. Ng3 Qe6+ 14. Qe3 d4 15. Qxe6+ Bxe6 16. f3 {Secures e4+g4} O-O-O 17. Kf2 Bb6 (17... Rhe8 $142 $5 18. bxc3 dxc3 $19) 18. bxc3 $15 dxc3+ 19. Be3 Bxe3+ 20. Kxe3 {White wins a piece} Rhe8 21. Ne4 {White threatens to win material: Ne4xc3} Bd5 22. g4 Bxe4 23. fxe4 Rd5 24. Rc1 g6 25. Bg2 f5 26. gxf5 gxf5 27. Rhf1 fxe4 28. Rxc3 {White wins a piece} Rh5 {Black threatens to win material: Rh5xh2} 29. Rh1 Rh4 30. Rc4 {[%cal Rc4e4,Re3e4,Rg2e4,Ge8e4,Gh4e4] The pressure on the isolated pawn grows. White threatens to win material: Rc4xe4} Kc7 31. Rxe4 Rexe4+ 32. Bxe4 {White wins a piece} Rh3+ 33. Bf3 c5 34. Rg1 b5 35. Rg7+ Kb6 {Black has a cramped position} 36. Rb7+ Ka6 37. Rb8 Rxh2 38. Be2 {White threatens to win material: Be2xb5} Rh3+ 39. Ke4 c4 {This push gains space} 40. a4 {Deflection: c4} Rh4+ (40... bxa4 41. Rb4 {Decoy Double attack} (41. Bxc4+ {Deflection})) (40... Z0 $140 41. axb5+ {Wins material}) 1-0

