{[%mdl 8256] B93: Sicilian Najdorf: 6 f4} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. f4 e5 7. Nf3 Nbd7 8. Bd3 Be7 9. O-O O-O 10. Kh1 b5 11. a3 Qc7 12. fxe5 dxe5 13. Nh4 Nc5 14. Bg5 Qd8 15. Nf5 Bxf5 16. Rxf5 Nfd7 17. Bxe7 Qxe7 18. Nd5 Qd6 19. Qg4 {last book move} g6 20. Raf1 f6 21. h4 (21. R5f3 $142 $5 $14 {must be considered}) 21... Kh8 $15 22. R5f3 $2 (22. R5f2 $142 $5 $15 {would keep White alive}) 22... f5 $1 $17 {Deflection: d5} 23. exf5 (23. exf5 Qxd5 {Deflection}) (23. Z0 $140 fxg4 {Wins material}) 23... Qxd5 24. fxg6 Rxf3 25. g7+ Kg8 26. Bxh7+ $4 {terrible, but the game is lost in any case} (26. Rxf3 e4 27. Rf5 Nxd3 28. cxd3 Qxd3 29. Rf4 $19) 26... Kxh7 27. Rxf3 Ne4 (27... Qe6 $142 $5 {makes it even easier for Black} 28. Qh5+ Qh6 29. Rf8 Rxf8 30. gxf8=N+ Nxf8 31. Qxe5 Qxh4+ 32. Kg1 $19) 28. h5 Ndf6 (28... Kg8 $142 {makes sure everything is clear} 29. h6 Nef6 $19) 29. Qg6+ Kg8 30. h6 Ra7 31. Kh2 Re7 $4 {overlooking an easy win} (31... Qd2 $142 {with excellent chances for Black} 32. h7+ Nxh7 33. Qxe4 Qd6 $19) 32. Rh3 $18 Nh7 33. Rd3 Qa8 (33... Qxd3 {hoping against hope} 34. cxd3 Nef6 $18) 34. Qxe4 $1 {Deflection: g8} Qxe4 (34... Qxe4 35. Rd8+ {Deflection}) (34... Z0 $140 35. Qxa8+ {Mate threat}) 35. Rd8+ Kf7 36. g8=Q+ Kf6 37. Rd6+ Kf5 38. Qg6+ Kf4 39. g3+ Ke3 40. Rd3+ Qxd3 1-0

