1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d6 9. h3 h6 10. d4 Re8 11. Nbd2 Bf8 12. Nf1 Bd7 13. Ng3 Na5 14. Bc2 Nc4 15. Nh2 c5 16. b3 Nb6 17. f4 cxd4 18. cxd4 Qc8 $5 {This is an interesting move, keeping an eye on both enemy wings.} 19. Re2 (19. Nf3 {can be met by the surprising sacrifice} Bxh3 (19... exf4 {Tal,M} 20. Bxf4 Bxh3 $1 21. gxh3 Qxh3 $13) 20. gxh3 (20. fxe5 dxe5 21. gxh3 Qxh3) 20... Qxh3 21. Nf1 Rac8 $5 {[%cal Gc8c2]} 22. Bd3 exf4 23. Bxf4 Qg4+ 24. Bg3 Nxe4 25. N3h2 Qxd1 26. Raxd1 Nxg3 27. Nxg3 Rxe1+ 28. Rxe1 g6 {Acosta,A-Geller,E (2590)/Bogota 1978/EXT 98 (0-1, 70)}) 19... Qc3 (19... exd4 {Tal,M} 20. Bb2 $14) 20. Be3 exd4 $6 {This move is based on some very nice tactical nuances, but, taking into account Tal's recommended improvement on the 22nd move, it may be not the strongest.} (20... exf4 21. Bxf4 g5 {This move leads to chronic kingside weaknesses, but Black's piece activity and the relative vulnerability of the white centre seem to compensate for this drawback.} 22. Be3 Nfd5 (22... Nbd5 23. Nhf1 Nxe3 24. Nxe3 Rac8 25. Rc1 Kh8 $13) 23. Nhf1 (23. exd5 Rxe3 24. Ne4 Rxe4 25. Bxe4 Bg7 $44 {[%csl Gd4,Gd5][%cal Gf7f5]}) 23... Bg7 $5 (23... Nb4 24. Bf2 $1 {Tal}) 24. Bf2 (24. exd5 Rxe3 25. Nxe3 Bxd4 $36) 24... Nf4 {The activity of this knight is an important achievement for Black.} 25. Rd2 Rac8 26. Rc1 Kh8 27. Ne3 d5 28. e5 f6 $13) 21. Bf2 (21. Qxd4 {Tal,M} Nbd5 $1 22. Rf1 (22. exd5 Rxe3 $1) 22... Rac8 $1) 21... Rac8 22. Nf3 (22. Bd3 $1 {Tal,M} Qc7 (22... Nc4 $2 23. Rc2 Nb2 24. Rxc3 Rxc3 25. Qd2 $1 $16) 23. Nf3 g6 24. Bxd4 Bg7 $14) 22... Nbd5 23. Bxd4 (23. exd5 $2 {Tal,M} Rxe2 24. Nxe2 Qxc2) 23... Qc7 24. Qd2 Qxc2 $1 25. Qxc2 Rxc2 26. Rxc2 Nxe4 27. Nxe4 Rxe4 28. Rd1 Nxf4 29. Rc7 Be6 30. Bf2 a5 $1 31. Kf1 a4 32. Rd4 Rxd4 33. Nxd4 axb3 34. axb3 Bd5 35. Bg3 Ne6 (35... Bxg2+ $6 {Tal,M} 36. Kg1 Nd5 37. Rc8 Bxh3 38. Rd8 Nf6 39. Bxd6 Nd7 40. Nxb5 g6 41. b4 $16) 36. Nxe6 fxe6 37. Rd7 1/2-1/2

