1. c4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. e4 e5 5. dxe5 dxe5 6. Qxd8+ Kxd8 7. f4 Nd7 8. Nf3 c6 9. Be2 ({One more possibility is} 9. fxe5 $5 Nxe5 10. Bf4 Nxf3+ ({Another kind of pawn structure arises after} 10... f6 $5 11. O-O-O+ ({White is also slightly better after} 11. Be2 Nh6 12. Rd1+ Ke8 13. O-O Nhf7 14. Na4 Ke7 15. Bg3 (15. Nc5 $5 b6 16. Nd3 $14) 15... b6 16. c5 b5 17. Nc3 Be6 18. Nd4 $14 {½-½ Knaak,R (2515)-Middendorf,F (2250)/Muenster 1991/EXT 1997 (85)}) 11... Ke8 12. Be2 $6 ({A better move is} 12. Kb1 $1 $14) 12... Bh6 $1 13. Bxh6 Nxh6 14. Nxe5 fxe5 15. b4 Ke7 16. c5 Be6 17. a3 Rad8 $11 {½-½ Olafsson,H (2555)-Ljubojevic,L (2620)/Reykjavik 1987/CBM 002 (24)}) 11. gxf3 Be6 (11... Ke7 12. c5 Be6 13. Bd6+ Ke8 14. O-O-O Nf6 15. Kc2 Nd7 16. f4 f5 17. Bd3 $14 {½-½ Lautier,J (2632)-Hauchard,A (2513)/Paris 2000/CBM 077 (49)}) 12. O-O-O+ Ke8 13. Kc2 Nf6 14. b3 $14 {½-½ Donner,J (2500)-Ivkov,B (2560)/Wijk aan Zee 1972/MCD (19)}) ({or} 9. Be3 $5 exf4 10. Bxf4 Nh6 11. h3 f6 12. O-O-O Nf7 13. h4 Bh6 14. Bxh6 Nxh6 15. e5 fxe5 16. h5 Nf7 17. hxg6 hxg6 18. Rxh8+ Nxh8 19. Nxe5 $14 {½-½ Atalik,E (2481)-Fominykh,M (2253)/Moscow 2012/CBM 146 Extra (68)}) ({Interesting is} 9. g3 $5 Ngf6 10. Bh3 Re8 11. O-O h6 12. fxe5 Nxe5 13. Bxc8 Rxc8 14. Nxe5 Rxe5 15. Be3 Re6 16. Rf3 Ke8 17. Raf1 Rc7 18. Bd4 $14 {1-0 Vaisser,A (2530)-Ivkov,B (2470)/Belgrade 1988/CBM 010 (43)}) 9... f6 $5 ({Also possible is} 9... Ke8 10. O-O Ne7 11. Bd2 exf4 12. Bxf4 Nc5 13. Rac1 (13. Be3 {is better:} Ne6 14. Rad1 $14) 13... Bg4 14. b4 Bxf3 15. gxf3 Ne6 16. Be3 g5 17. Rfd1 Ng6 18. Na4 b6 $11 {1-0 Tal,M (2620)-Klaric,Z (2405)/Sochi 1977/EXT 1999 (48)}) 10. O-O ({The position is equal after} 10. fxe5 Nxe5 11. Nxe5 fxe5 12. Bg5+ Ke8 13. O-O-O Bf6 14. h4 Be7 15. Rd2 Be6 16. Rhd1 Nf6 17. c5 Rf8 $11 {0-1 Miles,A (2505)-Kagan,S (2460)/Hastings 1976/EXT 1999 (53)}) 10... Nh6 ({White preserves a more active position after} 10... Ke8 11. Rb1 Nh6 12. fxe5 Nxe5 13. Nxe5 fxe5 14. b4 Rf8 15. Rd1 Nf7 16. b5 Nd8 17. bxc6 bxc6 18. Be3 $14 {½-½ San Segundo Carrillo,P (2516)-Rogers,I (2593)/Mallorca 2004/CBM 104 (43)}) 11. fxe5 Nxe5 12. Nxe5 fxe5 13. Be3 ({White can try} 13. Bg5+ $5 Ke8 14. Rad1 Nf7 15. Be3 Bf8 16. c5 Be7 $2 (16... Bh6) 17. Nb5 $1 cxb5 18. Bxb5+ Kf8 19. Bh6+ $18 {1-0 Ivkov,B (2525)-Kagan,S (2445)/Rio de Janeiro 1979/IZT}) (13. b4 $5 {is interesting:} Be6 14. b5 Nf7 15. Bg4 Bxg4 16. Rxf7 Bf8 17. Bg5+ Kc8 18. Be7 Bh6 19. Bd6 Be3+ 20. Kh1 Bb6 21. c5 Ba5 22. Bxe5 $16 {1-0 Crouch,C (2410)-Norwood,D (2535)/England 1998/EXT 2000 (31)}) 13... Ke8 14. Rad1 (14. h3 {is too slow:} Nf7 15. b4 Nd8 16. b5 Ne6 17. bxc6 bxc6 18. Rab1 Rf8 19. Rfc1 Nd4 $11 {½-½ Garcia,R-Najdorf,M/Buenos Aires 1965/MCD (37)}) 14... Rf8 15. Rfe1 Nf7 16. b4 $14 Bh6 17. Bf2 Bg5 18. b5 Be7 19. c5 Ng5 20. Be3 Ne6 21. bxc6 bxc6 $11 22. Nd5 $5 cxd5 23. exd5 Bxc5 24. Bb5+ Ke7 25. dxe6 Bxe3+ 26. Rxe3 Bxe6 27. Rxe5 Kf6 28. Re2 Rab8 29. a4 Rb6 30. h3 h5 31. Bd7 Rd8 32. a5 Ra6 33. Rf1+ Bf5 1/2-1/2

