1. e4 {1)Tal in Shakmaty v SSSR 1956. 2) Tal:The life and Games of M Tal. Soon after the soviet Championship, I had my first trip abroad. With the USSR Student Team I set off the World Championship in Sweden. There were a great number of new, colourful impressions, plus the the special character of the "little olympiad" everyone was young good-humoured, and got on well together. (The life and Games of M Tal)} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d6 9. h3 Na5 (9... Nb8 $5 {Une idée intéressante du maitre soviétique Borisenko} 10. a4 Bb7 11. d3 Nbd7 12. Bc2 Re8 13. Nbd2 Bf8 14. Nf1 c5 $132 {0-1 Milic,B-Spassky,B WchT U26 2nd 1955 (1)}) 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Qc7 12. Nbd2 Bd7 13. Nf1 Rfe8 14. Ne3 g6 {Tal: Ivkov knew the game Boleslavsky-Kholmov (14...Bf8).} (14... Bf8 15. b4 cxd4 16. cxd4 Nc6 17. Bb2 Qd8 18. a3 exd4 19. Nxd4 Nxe4 20. Nd5 Qh4 21. Rxe4 Rxe4 22. Nf3 {1-0 (22) Boleslavsky,I-Kholmov,R Leningrad (Russia) 1956 URS-ch [GJ17Datum]}) 15. b4 $1 {Tal} cxb4 16. cxb4 Nc4 17. Nxc4 bxc4 18. Re3 $5 {[%csl Ra6,Re5][%cal Ge3a3,Ga3a5] Début d'un plan curieux mais astucieux avec pression indirecte sur le "e5" qui va forcer les Noirs à abandonner le centre par la prise ed4} Bf8 (18... c3 19. Rb1 {[%csl Rc3][%cal Gb1b3] Tal} Rac8 20. Rb3 Qb7 21. Rbxc3 Rxc3 22. Rxc3 Nxe4) (18... Rad8 $5 19. Bb2 (19. Bd2 exd4 20. Nxd4 d5 $132) 19... d5 $132) (18... Rab8 $142 {Tal} 19. Bd2 exd4 20. Nxd4 d5 21. e5 Ne4 22. Bxe4 dxe4 23. Rxe4 Bxb4 24. Bf4 $36 {Tal}) 19. Bb2 $1 {[%csl Gb2,Re5][%cal Gd4e5]} Bh6 $6 {[%csl Rf6,Rg8]} (19... Bg7 $142 {[%csl Re3] Aurait évité le thème tactique des Blancs après le coup d4}) 20. Ra3 {[%csl Re5][%cal Gd4e5,Gd6e5,Ga3a5] Menace la prise de5} Qb7 $2 {[#] Tal: Starting a combination which failed.} (20... a5 $132) 21. dxe5 Qxb4 22. Qd4 $1 $18 {[%csl Rf6,Rg8] Tal: Ivkov missed this winning move.} (22. Rb1 dxe5 23. Bc1 Qf8 24. Bxh6 Qxh6 25. Rb6 Re6 $11 {This is the variation Ivkov had calculated.}) 22... Nh5 (22... Rab8 23. Rb1 dxe5 24. Nxe5 Qd2 25. Nxd7 $18 {Tal}) (22... Reb8 23. Rb1 Ne8 24. exd6 Bg7 25. e5 Nxd6 26. Bc1 $18 {Tal}) 23. exd6 (23. e6 $1 Bg7 24. exf7+ Kxf7 25. Ng5+ Kg8 26. Qd5+) 23... Bg7 24. e5 Bc6 $2 (24... Nf4 {[%cal Gf4e6]}) 25. Re3 $18 Bxf3 26. Bc3 Qb5 27. gxf3 Rad8 28. f4 Re6 29. Rb1 Qc6 30. Rb6 Qc8 31. Bd1 Bh6 32. Bxh5 gxh5 33. f5 1-0

