1. e4 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: 'Nunn, Harding'} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. Rxe5 c6 12. d4 Bd6 13. Re1 Qh4 14. g3 Qh3 15. Be3 Bg4 16. Qd3 Rae8 17. Nd2 Re6 18. a4 f5 (18... Qh5 19. axb5 axb5) 19. Qf1 Qh5 20. f4 bxa4 21. Rxa4 g5 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: '"The old main line, now more or less refuted" - Nunn, 1989. NB: We use the term 'Old Main Line' to describe the whole complex of variations arising from 21 Rxa4.'} 22. Rxa6 gxf4 $5 (22... Kh8) 23. Bxf4 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: 'Tal found the right move back in 1975 but not the follow-up which took another decade to emerge. Part of the reason was no doubt the eminence of the players in this game which deterred searches for improvements?'} (23. Rxc6 fxe3 (23... fxg3 24. hxg3 Bxg3 25. Qg2 $16) 24. Bxd5 exd2 {This was later shown to be an error; 24...Kh8 seems satisfactory for Black.} 25. Rxe6 Kh8 26. Rexd6 $2 (26. Bb3 $1) 26... d1=Q {Pachman. Geller probably found some or all of this but Tal got his improvement in first.}) 23... Bxf4 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: 'Diagram #'} 24. Rxc6 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: '?!'} (24. Rxe6 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: '!'} Bxd2 25. Raxc6 (25. Bxd5 $1 {Survey: Tim Harding} cxd5 26. Qg2 {Nunn, 1989: "There are no visible improvements... so this must be considered the refutation of 21...g5". Hauptmann-Sieberg, corr 1989, continued:} f4 (26... Bf3 27. Qxd2 Be4 28. Rh6 Qf3 29. Qg5+ $18) (26... Bg5 27. Qxd5 $18) 27. Qxd2 fxg3 (27... Bxe6 {also loses (see examples in the database)}) 28. Rf6 $1 Re8 (28... Rxf6 29. Rxf6 gxh2+ 30. Qxh2 Qg5 31. Qb8+ {mates}) 29. hxg3 Re2 30. Qh6 Re1+ 31. Rf1 Rxf1+ 32. Kxf1 Qf5+ 33. Qf4 Qd3+ 34. Kg1 Qxa6 35. Qxg4+ Kf7 36. Qh5+ Kf8 37. Kf2 {1-0. Four subsequent games in the database confirmed this line wins for White.}) (25. Re5 $5) 25... f4 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: 'Yudovich, INF 20/322'}) 24... Be3+ 25. Rxe3 Rxe3 26. Bxd5+ Kh8 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: 'Threat ...f4'} 27. Qf4 Re1+ 28. Nf1 Bh3 29. Bc4 (29. Bg2 Bxg2 30. Kxg2 Rfe8 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: 'Yudovich'} (30... Re2+ 31. Kh1 $140 Qh3 32. Qf3 Rxb2 {Wade})) 29... Qd1 (29... Rfe8 30. Rh6 {Yudovich, INF20; Nunn; Harding: 'Yudovich'}) 30. d5 $1 (30. Rh6 Bxf1 31. Bxf1 Rfe8 32. Rf6 Rxf1+ 33. Qxf1 Re1 34. Rxf5 {should also be a draw - Nunn, 1989}) (30. Qf2 Rfe8 {threat ...Rxf1+ Yudovich}) 30... Bxf1 31. Bxf1 Qxd5 1/2-1/2

