eny: 'Stohl, Igor'} 14. Nxc6 bxc6 15. Qc3 Qa4 16. Bc4 Nxe5 (16... Nc5 17. Qd2 f6 18. exf6 $1 Nxe4 19. f7+ Kxf7 20. Qf4+ Ke8 21. Qxe4 Bc5 22. Rd3 Bb6 23. Ra3 Qxa3 24. Qxc6+ {1-0,Ostrovjerhov-Koshelj/corr/1971/}) 17. O-O $1 $32 {} Nxc4 18. Nf6+ gxf6 19. Qxf6 $18) (13... Qa4 $5 {(Stohl) Postny,E} 14. Be2 $2 (14. Bb5 $1 axb5 15. O-O $44) 14... Nc6 15. Nxe6 fxe6 16. Nf6+ gxf6 17. exf6 Kd8 18. Be3 Kc7 19. O-O Bc5 20. Kh1 Bxe3 21. Rxe3 Nc5 22. c4 Qb4 23. Qc1 Bd7 24. Rg3 Raf8 {0-1 Velasquez Ojeda,C (2359)-Valenzuela Fuentealba,L (2418)/Santiago 2004/CBM 100}) 14. Kf2 Qa4 $2 {[#]} (14... h6 $15) (14... Nc6 {Stohl,Igor Stohl: 'Postny,E: '?'' Postny,Evgeny: '?' '?'} 15. Nxc6 bxc6 16. Nd6+ Bxd6 17. Qxd6 {Stohl: 'Postny,E: '+-' Postny,E: '1-0 Grabczewski,R-Matkowski,W/Warsaw 1957/EXT 2001 (21)'' Postny,Evgeny: '+-' '+-'} Nf6 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor'} 18. exf6 gxf6 19. Rd3 Qa5 20. Bxf6 Qf5+ 21. Rf3 {1-0, Grabczewski,R-Matkowski,W/Warsaw/ 1957/}) 15. Bb5 $6 {Stohl: 'Postny,E: '!'' Postny,Evgeny: '!' '!' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor: '?!'' Stohl,Igor: 'Tal rightly feels it's time to act and throws in a piece, but doesn't choose the right one. Correct was' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor: 'Tal rightly feels it's time to act and throws in a piece, but doesn't choose the right one. Correct was''} (15. Nxe6 $1 $18 {Stohl: '!' Postny,Evgeny: '!' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor'} fxe6 16. Nd6+ Bxd6 17. Qxd6 Rf8+ 18. Kg3 Nf6 {Stohl: '' Postny,Evgeny: ''} (18... Rf7 {Stohl,Igor: '?' Stohl: '?' Postny,Evgeny: '?'} 19. Qxe6+ Kf8 20. Bc4 $18) 19. exf6 $18 gxf6 {Stohl,Igor} 20. Be2 fxg5 (20... Nd7 21. Bh5+ Kd8 22. Be3 Rg8+ 23. Kh3 Rg6 24. Rc3 $1 Qe4 25. Rd1 $1 Qxg2+ 26. Kh4 Qe4+ 27. Bf4 $18) 21. Bh5+ Rf7 22. Bxf7+ Kxf7 23. Rf3+ Kg6 24. h4 $1 $18 {with a winning attack (Kasparov in My Great Predecessors 2 and 3).}) 15... axb5 16. Nxb5 f6 $17 {Stohl: 'Postny,E: ''' Postny,Evgeny: '' ''} 17. exf6 gxf6 $2 ({Postny,Evgeny: 'It looks like Black is fine after:'} 17... Qxe4 $15 {Stohl,Igor: '' Stohl: '' Postny,Evgeny: '!' '!' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor: '''} 18. fxg7 Bc5+ 19. Re3 {Stohl: 'Postny,E'} (19. Kg3 {Stohl,Igor Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor'} Rg8 {} 20. Re1 Nf6 $1 21. Bxf6 Rxg7+ $1 22. Bxg7 Qg6+ 23. Kf3 Qxg7 24. Qf4 Na6 $17 {is an even more fantastic line shown by Kasparov.}) 19... Qf5+ 20. Ke2 Qg4+ 21. Ke1 Ra1+ {Stohl: '!' Postny,Evgeny: '!' '!'} (21... Rg8 $2 {Stohl} 22. Nc7+ Kf7 23. Rf1+ Kg6 (23... Kxg7 24. Nxe6+ $18) 24. Qd3+ Kxg7 (24... Kxg5 25. Nxe6+ Kh6 26. Rh3+ $18) 25. Nxe6+ Kh8 26. Qc3+ Bd4 27. Nxd4 $18) 22. Kf2 Qf5+ 23. Ke2 Rg8 $17 24. Rxa1 Qg4+ 25. Ke1 Rxg7 $15 26. Nc7+ {Stohl} Kf7 $17) 18. Re1 $14 {Stohl,Igor: '!!' Stohl: '!!' Stohl: 'Postny,E: '!'' Postny,Evgeny: '!' '!' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor: '!!'' Stohl,Igor: 'A beautiful quiet move, now White again has a powerful attack' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor: 'A beautiful quiet move, now White again has a powerful attack''} Ra6 {[#]} (18... Nc6 19. Bxf6 Qxe4 20. Rxe4 Nxf6 21. Nc7+ $16) (18... fxg5 $2 {Stohl,Igor} 19. Nc7+ Kd8 {Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor'} (19... Kf7 {(Stohl) Postny,E} 20. Rf3+ $18) 20. Nxe6+ Ke8 21. Ng7+ $1 Kd8 22. Qxg5+ Kc7 23. Qf4+ $18) 19. Bxf6 $18 Nxf6 20. Nxf6+ Kf7 21. Rf3 {Stohl,Igor: '?' Stohl: '?' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor: '?'' Stohl,Igor: 'Very natural, but the computer within seconds points out the far stronger' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor: 'Very natural, but the computer within seconds points out the far stronger''} (21. Ne4 $1 {[%cal Rd2g5,Rb3f3,Rd2f4] (Stohl,Igor) f3, f4, g5. Postny,Evgeny: '(Stohl, Igor) f3, f4, g5. ' Here Black's  can't join the defence and he is helpless against all the threats.}) 21... Qh4+ 22. Kf1 e5 {Stohl,Igor: '!' Stohl: '!' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor: '!''} 23. Qd5+ Be6 (23... Kg6 {Stohl,Igor Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor'} 24. Ne8 $1 $40) 24. Nd7+ {Stohl: 'Postny,E: '!'' Postny,Evgeny: '!' '!'} Kg6 {Stohl,Igor: '?' Stohl: '?' Postny,Evgeny: 'Stohl, Igor: '?'' Stohl,Igor: 'The final mistake, necessary was' Postny,Ev