{Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'B17: Caro-Kann: Modern Line (4...Nd7) ''''} 1. e4 {Dolmatov Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Dolmatov''} c6 {Mikhail Tal: 'This well-tried defence, along with 1...e5, occupies the leading place in the Czechoslovakian Grandmaster's opening repertoire. In the majority of our previous encounters Filip had played 1...e5. Since, for several years now, much has been written about how Tal is unhappy against the Caro-Kann, my opponent no doubt decided to test the correctness of this opinion.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'This well-tried defence, along with 1...e5, occupies the leading place in the Czechoslovakian Grandmaster's opening repertoire. In the majority of our previous encounters Filip had played 1...e5. Since, for several years now, much has been written about how Tal is unhappy against the Caro-Kann, my opponent no doubt decided to test the correctness of this opinion.'''} 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 {Mikhail Tal: 'In recent events this order of moves has occurred in my games comparatively rarely.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'In recent events this order of moves has occurred in my games comparatively rarely.'''} dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. Nf3 ({Nowadays the variation} 5. Bc4 Ngf6 6. Ng5 {is more fashionable, but it is not known how long this fashion will last. In any case, the old continuation adopted by me in the present game has in no way been refuted over the past half-century.}) 5... Ngf6 6. Ng3 e6 7. Bd3 Be7 (7... c5 $5 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: '!?''} 8. O-O cxd4 9. Nxd4 Bc5 10. Nf3 O-O $10 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: '=''} 11. Qe2 Qc7 $11) 8. Qe2 c5 9. O-O {Mikhail Tal: 'With his 8th move White expressed his preparedness to castle queenside. A move later he thought better of it!' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'With his 8th move White expressed his preparedness to castle queenside. A move later he thought better of it!'''} O-O 10. Rd1 cxd4 ({Mikhail Tal: 'Probably' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Probably'''} 10... Qc7 {Mikhail Tal: 'was a little more accurate,' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'was a little more accurate,'''} {Mikhail Tal: 'I intended to play'} 11. c4 {Mikhail Tal: ', so as to provoke the exchange in the centre all the same, freeing White's pieces (on 11 c4,'} (11. Z0) ({after which} 11. Nf5 $2 {fails to} exf5 12. Qxe7 Re8 {.}) 11... Re8 (11... b6 {is bad because of} 12. d5 exd5 13. Qxe7 Re8 14. Bxh7+ $1 {).}) 12. dxc5 Nxc5 13. Bc2 Ncd7 14. Ne4 b6 15. Ba4 Rd8 $10 {Tal,M-Ciric,D/Budva/1967/ Inf 4/197/}) 11. Nxd4 Re8 12. b3 {Mikhail Tal: 'This bishop will be most actively placed on the long diagonal, taking into account the fact that White has chosen the enemy king as the object of his attack. It is not so easy for Black to complete the development of his pieces.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'This bishop will be most actively placed on the long diagonal, taking into account the fact that White has chosen the enemy king as the object of his attack. It is not so easy for Black to complete the development of his pieces.'''} Qb6 13. Bb2 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: ''} Nf8 ({Mikhail Tal: 'Black could have eliminated one of the bishops by'} 13... Nc5 $5 {Mikhail Tal: 'and the sharper'} 14. Bc4 (14. Z0) ({but both the quiet} 14. Nf3 Nxd3 15. Rxd3) 14... Bd7 (14... Na4 15. bxa4 $5 (15. Bb5 $2 Nxb2 16. Bxe8 Nxd1) 15... Qxb2 16. Nb5 { a-b1 Mikhail Tal: 'lead to a favourable position for White.'} Qb4 17. Nc7 $14) 15. Nf3 Bc6 16. Ne5 Bd5) 14. Nf3 {Mikhail Tal: 'The knight transfers itself to e5 where it is most threatening to the enemy king.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'The knight transfers itself to e5 where it is most threatening to the enemy king.'''} Bd7 15. Ne5 Rad8 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'last book move''''} 16. Ne4 {Mikhail Tal: 'Black has succeeded in almost completing the mobilisation of his forces.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Black has succeeded in almost completing the mobilisation of his forces.'''} (16. Nh5 {was very tempting here, against which Black's only move is} Bc8 {.} 17. Z0 ({But in the resulting position, I could not find a concrete way to exploit the activity of the white pieces. Nothing of importance is gained by} 17. Nxf6+ Bxf6 18. Nc4 Qc5 19. Bxf6 gxf6 {.}) ({I very much wanted to sacrifice a piece by} 17. Nxg7 $5 Kxg7 18. Ng4 {, but recollections restrained me! In a similar position I sacrificed a knight on g7 against Keres in the 1959 Peoples' Spartakiad. On that occasion, the sacrifice was inadequate. Here White consoled himself with the idea of a possible sacrifice on another, neighbouring square.})) 16... Nxe4 17. Bxe4 (17. Nxd7 $2 Qxf2+ 18. Qxf2 Nxf2 19. Nxf8 Nxd1) 17... Bc8 {Mikhail Tal: '!' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: '!'''} 18. Qh5 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: '!' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'White has a mate threat''''} ({White could have provoked a weakening in the black position by} 18. Qf3 {, but after} f6 {nothing real is achieved. The move in the game is the prelude to an unclear combination.}) 18... Ng6 {Mikhail Tal: 'Evidently the only move.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Evidently the only move.'''} ({Mikhail Tal: 'or'} 18... g6 19. Qf3 $5 (19. Qh6 f6 $13) (19. Ng4 $1 f6 20. Bxf6 $1 {.}) 19... f6 20. Ng4 e5 21. Ne3 $14) ({Out of the question were} 18... f6 19. Bxh7+ $1 {and mate in two moves}) {Mikhail Tal: 'After the immediate' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'After the immediate'''} 19. Nxf7 {Mikhail Tal: '!?' Mikhail Tal: 'It is highly possible that this sacrifice should not have given White a decisive advantage, but it is definite that without it White would not be able to maintain the offensive, since Black is fully prepared to begin simplifying the position.' Mikhail Tal: 'Black does not have this possibility as' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: '!' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: '!?' Mikhail Tal: 'It is highly possible that this sacrifice should not have given White a decisive advantage, but it is definite that without it White would not be able to maintain the offensive, since Black is fully prepared to begin simplifying the position.' Mikhail Tal: 'Black does not have this possibility as'''} (19. Bxg6 hxg6 20. Qf3 {is met by the cold-blooded reply} Rf8 $1 {.}) ({A great deal of time was spent on deciding whether to sacrifice the knight immediately, or after the preliminary exchange of a pair of rooks. However, during my calculations it became clear that after} 19. Rxd8 Rxd8 20. Nxf7 {, Black has the strong rejoinder} Rf8 $1 {, forcing the line} 21. Bxg6 hxg6 22. Qh8+ (22. Nh6+ $2 Kh7 $1) 22... Kxf7 23. Qxg7+ Ke8 24. Qxg6+ Rf7 {, when Black can look confidently to the future.}) 19... Kxf7 (19... Rxd1+ 20. Rxd1 Rf8 {is met by} 21. Bd4 {.}) 20. Qxh7 e5 21. Rxd8 Rxd8 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Black wins a piece''''} (21... Bxd8 {would not change the character of the position. White would have continued} 22. Qh5 {, as in the game.}) 22. Qh5 {Mikhail Tal: '!' Mikhail Tal: 'This is the idea of the sacrifice.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: '!' Mikhail Tal: 'This is the idea of the sacrifice.'''} Qe6 $6 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: '?!''} ({Mikhail Tal: '. The pin on the knight is most unpleasant for Black, and it is not easy for him to free himself.'} 22... Qf6 $5 {Mikhail Tal: 'White gains a marked advantage by'} 23. f4 {Mikhail Tal: '!'} ({but not} 23. h4 $2 Rh8 $1 24. Bxg6+ Qxg6 25. Qxh8 Bh3 $1) {Mikhail Tal: 'or'} 23... Bc5+ (23... Z0) (23... Rh8 24. Bxg6+ Kg8 25. Qxe5) 24. Kh1 $44 Rh8 25. Bxg6+ Kg8 26. Qg5 $1 {.}) (22... Z0) ({. Evidently, it was absolutely necessary for Black to seek counterplay against the one vulnerable point in White's position, f2. After} 22... Rd2 $1 23. Rf1 Bc5 24. Z0 ({. White gains nothing concrete by} 24. Kh1 Rxf2 25. Rxf2+ Bxf2 26. Bd5+ Ke7 (26... Be6 $2 27. Qf5+) {.} 27. Z0) ({. White would probably have had to play} 24. Bc3 Rxf2 ({bad is} 24... Bxf2+ 25. Kh1) 25. Qxg6+ Qxg6 26. Bxg6+ Kxg6 27. Rxf2 {remaining with an extra pawn, but after} Bf5 {the presence of opposite-coloured bishops makes a draw inevitable. Having missed the correct path, Black very quickly finds himself in a critical position.})) (22... Bd7 23. Bxe5 Be8 $1) 23. h3 {Mikhail Tal: '!' Mikhail Tal: 'There is no need for White to hurry. This prophylactic move against the threat of 23...Qg4 is essential.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: '!' Mikhail Tal: 'There is no need for White to hurry. This prophylactic move against the threat of 23...Qg4 is essential.'''} Bc5 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Black has an active position''''} ({Black could have freed his king by} 23... Rd6 24. Re1 Kf8 {, but after} 25. Re3 {his difficulties would not have diminished. In particular, White can transpose into a favourable ending by} Nf4 26. Qxe5 Qxe5 27. Bxe5 Rd1+ 28. Kh2 Bd6 29. Bxd6+ Rxd6 30. Rf3 Rf6 31. Rc3 {.}) (23... Bd7 $142 $5 {should be examined more closely} 24. Rd1 Qf6 $11) 24. Kh1 { f4 Mikhail Tal: 'Now White's f-pawn is ready to advance.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: ' f4 Mikhail Tal: 'Now White's f-pawn is ready to advance. Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): '''''} Bd4 ({Better defensive chances were offered by} 24... Rd6 {when} 25. f4 (25. Re1 Bd4 26. Ba3 {,} ({or} 26. c3 {, White would keep a dangerous initiative.})) 25... exf4 26. Qxc5 Qxe4 27. Qxd6 Bxh3 {is unclear.}) {Mikhail Tal: 'Black probably underestimated the strength of' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Black probably underestimated the strength of'''} 25. Rd1 { d3 Mikhail Tal: '.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: ' d3 Mikhail Tal: '.'''} Rd6 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): '??' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'the pressure is too much, Black crumbles''''} ({Mikhail Tal: 'while in the case of'} 25... Bb6 {Mikhail Tal: ', possible is'} {Mikhail Tal: 'and also the more energetic'} 26. Rxd8 (26. Rf1) 26... Bxd8 27. f4 $16) ({Now material losses result from} 25... Rh8 26. Bxg6+ Kg8 27. Qg5 {, when the sacrifice on h3 is insufficient;} (27. Z0)) (25... Qf6 $142 26. Bxd4 Rxd4 27. Rxd4 exd4 $16) 26. Ba3 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: '!' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): '+-''''} Ra6 $6 {Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: '?!''} (26... Rd8 27. Rd3 $16 (27. c3 Bb6 28. Rxd8 Bxd8 29. f4 $1)) {Mikhail Tal: 'The variation' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'The variation'''} 27. Rxd4 {Mikhail Tal: '!' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: '!' Mikhail Tal: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): '!' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Double attack: b7/f7''''} exd4 28. Bd5 (28. Bd5 Rxa3 29. Qf5+ {Mikhail Tal: 'is completely convincing.' Yudovich,Mikhail Sr: 'Dolmatov,Sergey: 'Mikhail Tal: 'is completely convincing.'''} Ke7 30. Bxe6 Bxe6 31. Qxg6 $18) 1-0

