1. e4 {Marin} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. O-O Nxe4 5. d4 Be7 6. Qe2 Nd6 7. Bxc6 bxc6 8. dxe5 Nb7 9. Nc3 O-O 10. Re1 Nc5 11. Be3 Ne6 12. Rad1 d5 13. exd6 cxd6 14. Nd4 Nxd4 15. Bxd4 Re8 { d7, f8.} 16. Qf3 d5 17. Na4 Bf8 18. Bc5 $5 {This generally desirable move, aiming to exchange the dark-squared bishops in order to block the hanging pawns, is connected with some tactical finesses, typical of Tal.} ({The transfer of the queen to the queenside, pursuing the same purpose,} 18. Qc3 {allows Black obtain certain kingside counterplay:} Rxe1+ 19. Rxe1 Qg5 20. Bc5 Bf5 21. Bxf8 Rxf8 22. Nc5 h6 23. Nb3 Rc8 24. Nd4 (24. Re3 $6 {this is just careless. White should not leave the back rank undefended.} c5 $1 25. Re5 (25. Nxc5 $2 Bh3 $3 {[%cal Gg5c1]} 26. g3 d4 $1 27. Qxd4 Qxc5 $19) 25... Qg6 26. Nxc5 (26. Rxd5 $2 Be4 $19) (26. f3 d4 27. Qd2 Bxc2 $15) 26... Bh3 27. g3 (27. Qxh3 Rxc5 {[%csl Rc2][%cal Gg6b1]} 28. g3 Rxc2 $15) 27... Qc6 {[%csl Gg2][%cal Gd5d4]} 28. Nb3 $6 (28. Nd3 Qxc3 29. bxc3 Rxc3 $15) 28... Qf6 $1 (28... Qa6 $6 29. Qd3 $15 {Haba,P (2435)-Milovanovic,R (2440)/Tuzla 1990/EXT 97 (0-1, 41)}) 29. Qe3 Rxc2 30. Rxd5 Rxb2 $17 {[%csl Gg1]}) 24... Be4 (24... c5 $11 {looks the simplest way to equality to me.}) 25. f3 Bg6 26. b4 Kh8 27. g3 a5 $5 28. b5 $1 (28. a3 axb4 29. axb4) (28. bxa5 c5 $132) 28... c5 29. Nc6 d4 30. Nxd4 (30. Qxa5 $5 Bxc2 31. b6) 30... Rb8 31. Nc6 Rxb5 32. Nxa5 $13 {[%csl Ga2,Rg1] ½-½ Mokry,K (2505)-Milovanovic,R (2440)/Tuzla 1990/EXT 2000}) (18. Rxe8 Qxe8 $10) 18... Rxe1+ 19. Rxe1 Bg4 ({Without previous preparation, Portisch feared to embark on the dangerous line starting with} 19... Qa5 {, but it appears that Black could more or less have forced a draw:} 20. b4 $1 (20. Re8 $2 Bd7 $1 $19) 20... Qxa4 21. Re8 Bb7 22. Qe2 Qxa2 23. h3 $1 (23. g3 Rxe8 24. Qxe8 Qa1+ 25. Kg2 h6 26. Qxf8+ Kh7 27. Qxf7 Ba6 $11 {[%csl Gf1] Marin}) 23... h6 24. Rxa8 Bxa8 25. Qe8 Qa1+ $1 (25... Bb7 26. Qxf8+ Kh7 27. Qxf7 Qa1+ 28. Kh2 {(+- according to Tal. Maybe  is closer to the truth, but the line is clearly unappealing for Black.)} Qe5+ $2 29. f4 $1 $18) 26. Kh2 Kh7 $1 {This move order was not mentioned by Tal in his comments.} 27. Qxf8 (27. Bxf8 Qf6 $3 $11 {threatens with a draw by perpetual, winning time for defending the f7-pawn and to save the bishop.}) 27... Qe5+ {With the pawn on f7 still, this move is possible now, forcing the weakening of the enemy king's fortress.} 28. g3 Bb7 29. Qxf7 Bc8 30. Qxa7 (30. Bxa7 Qf5 $11) 30... Qf5 $132 {(=)}) 20. Qxg4 (20. Qf4 $6 Qa5 {Tal}) (20. Qc3 $5 {Tal,M}) (20. Qe3 $5 {Tal,M}) 20... Qa5 21. c3 Bxc5 22. Nxc5 Qxc5 23. Qd7 { e8} Rf8 $8 (23... g6 24. Re7 {Tal,M}) 24. h4 { h5, e8, Tal,M} (24. Re8 g6 $8 25. Qe7 Rxe8 $10 {Tal,M}) 24... h5 (24... h6 25. h5 $1 { e8 Tal,M}) 25. Re5 (25. Re8 g6 $8 26. Qe7 Qxe7 27. Rxe7 Rb8 28. b3 a5 (28... Rb5 29. Kf1 $1 Rc5 30. Ke2 Rxc3 31. Kd2 d4 32. Rxa7 $16) 29. Rc7 $1 (29. Ra7 Rb5 $10) 29... a4 30. b4 a3 31. Rxc6 d4 32. g3 dxc3 33. Rxc3 Rxb4 34. Rxa3 $16 {Tal,M. Well, maybe  would be closer to the truth, if Black knows this type of ending.}) 25... g6 26. Qe7 (26. g4 hxg4 27. Qxg4 (27. Rg5 Rb8 $1 $36) 27... Qd6 $10 {Tal,M}) 26... Qb5 $1 27. Rxh5 (27. b3 Qa5 $1 {Tal,M}) 27... gxh5 (27... Qxb2 $2 28. Rh8+ $18 {Tal,M}) 1/2-1/2

