hed with the tactical tricks.'} {Rogers: ' '} 19. Bxa3 $1 {Rogers: ' '} Bxc2 20. Nc6 {Rogers: ' White was now anticipating 20...Rc7 21.Nxe7+ Rxe7+ 22.Kd2 Be4 23.b5 1-0. However White's underdeveloped army and king in the centre gives Black a chance to confuse matters with a rook sacrifice.'} Bf6 $1 ({White was now anticipating} 20... Rc7 21. Nxe7+ Rxe7+ 22. Kd2 Be4 23. b5 {1-0. However White's underdeveloped army and king in the centre gives Black a chance to confuse matters with a rook sacrifice.}) 21. Nxa7 {Played reluctantly after great thought.} ({It is too late to bail out with Rogers: ' Played reluctantly after great thought. It is too late to bail out with '} 21. Kd2 {since} {Rogers: ' since '} Rc7 {is good for Black, e.g.} {Rogers: ' is good for Black, e.g. '} 22. b5 {Rogers: ' '} Ra8 $3 {Rogers: ' '} 23. Kxc2 {Rogers: ' axb5.'} axb5) {Rogers: ' '} 21... Bxc3+ {Rogers: ' '} 22. Ke2 {Rogers: ' '} Re8+ {Rogers: ' '} 23. Kf3 Re6 $2 {Rogers: ' the game is essentially over.'} ({When considering 21.xa7 Tal was very worried by Rogers: ' When considering 21.Nxa7 Tal was very worried by '} 23... d4 $1 {keeping alive options such as ...e4+ and ...a8. Post-game analysis tended to give White an edge after Rogers: ' was the only consistent way to play since after Tal's reply to '} {Rogers: ' keeping alive options such as ...Be4+ and ...Ra8. Post-game analysis tended to give White an edge after '} 24. Rac1 {Rogers: ' '} Be4+ {Rogers: ' '} 25. Kg3 {Rogers: ' '} Ra8 {Rogers: ' '} 26. Rhe1 $1 {but in any case, 23...d4 was the only consistent way to play since after Tal's reply to 23...e6? the game is essentially over.}) {Rogers: ' '} 24. Rhc1 $1 {Rogers: ' '} Be4+ {Rogers: ' '} 25. Ke2 $1 {Rogers: ' '} d4 26. f3 ({After Rogers: ' '} 26. f3 {Rogers: ' 1-0 After '} Bf5+ {Rogers: ' '} 27. Kf2 {Rogers: ' '} Re3 $5 {Rogers: ' '} 28. Rab1 $1 {wins comfortably enough. Rogers: ' wins comfortably enough.'}) 1-0

