1. e4 {Postny,E} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. dxe5 Be6 9. Be3 Be7 10. c3 Nc5 11. Bc2 Nd7 12. Nd4 {This move is not the best one, but black needs to play precisely.} ({The main line goes with} 12. Re1 Ndxe5 13. Nxe5 Nxe5 14. Bd4) 12... Ndxe5 (12... Ncxe5 13. f4 Nc4 14. Bf2 Nb8 15. Re1 Qd6 16. f5 Bd7 17. Qe2 Kd8 18. b3 Na5 19. Bg3 Qf6 20. Be5 Qh6 21. Bxg7 Qxg7 22. Qxe7+ Kc8 23. f6 Qh6 24. Qxf7 $18 {½-½ Imanaliev,T-Sagalchik,G/Frunze 1989 (69)}) 13. f4 (13. Nxe6 $6 fxe6 14. Qh5+ g6 15. Qh3 Qd7 $15) 13... Nc4 $1 {This tactical resource neutralizes white's attacking attempts.} 14. Nxc6 Nxe3 (14... Qd6 $6 15. Bd4 Qxc6 16. f5 Bd7 17. Re1 $36 {Black's king is stuck in the centre.}) 15. Nxd8 Nxd1 16. Nxe6 Ne3 17. Nxc7+ Kd7 18. Nxa8 Nxc2 19. Nd2 (19. Nb6+ Kc6 20. Nxd5 Bc5+ 21. Kh1 Kxd5 22. Nd2 Nxa1 23. Rxa1 Re8 24. Rd1 Re2 {Despite being a pawn down, black is nearly winning thanks to great activity of his pieces.} 25. Nb3+ Kc6 26. Nxc5 Kxc5 27. Rb1 Kc4 28. Kg1 Kd3 29. Rd1+ Rd2 30. Rxd2+ Kxd2 $19 {0-1 Denis,L-Flear,G/Le Touquet 1988 (36)}) 19... Bc5+ 20. Kh1 Nxa1 21. Rxa1 Rxa8 {After a massive simplifications the sides landed in an approximately equal endgame, with only is the side who might have a slight pressure thanks to a more centralized king.} 22. Re1 Kd6 23. g3 Rc8 (23... Rc8 24. Kg2 b4 25. cxb4 Bxb4 26. Re2 Bxd2 {½-½ Joecks,C-Blauert,J/Germany 1989}) 1/2-1/2

