{Alexander Volzhin: 'Finally we'll consider the Classical set up with Nf3 and Be2. This system is Karpov's career long favourite. The outstanding Soviet Grandmaster Efim Geller has also greatly contributed to the theory of this line.'} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Be2 O-O 6. O-O Nc6 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Provocative.'} 7. d5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'The only way to fight for the advantage.'} (7. h3 {allows} e5 8. dxe5 ({After} 8. d5 Ne7 {the position looks similar to a main line King's Indian, but with White's pawn on c2. Now it's difficult for White to organise a Queen-side attack, so by playing Nh5 (or Nd7) and f5 Black obtains good counterplay.}) 8... dxe5 {with equality.}) 7... Nb8 8. Re1 (8. h3 {Ü 16/139}) 8... e5 $6 (8... c6) 9. dxe6 $1 Bxe6 10. Bf4 h6 {Alexander Volzhin: '?!'} (10... Nc6 11. h3 (11. Qd2 $5) 11... h6 12. Qd2 g5 13. Bg3 ({According to Efim Geller,} 13. Bh2 {is preferable, intending to meet} d5 {with} 14. e5 Ne4 15. Qe3 {keeping an opening advantage.}) 13... d5 14. exd5 Nxd5 15. Nxd5 Qxd5 {with equal chances in Geller-Kuzmin, USSR,1974.}) 11. Nd4 Bd7 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Now all Black's pieces are very passive.'} (11... Qd7 {should be preferred, although White's advantage is undisputable.}) 12. Qd2 Kh7 13. e5 $1 $16 {Alexander Volzhin: '!' Alexander Volzhin: 'Very logical: White has a development advantage, so he opens the central files. Other moves allow Black to complete his development (Nc6), when White only has a small advantage.'} dxe5 14. Bxe5 Ne4 $2 {Alexander Volzhin: 'It's not easy to find a sufficient defence.'} (14... Nc6 $5 $16 15. Nxc6 bxc6 (15... Bxc6 16. Qxd8 Raxd8 17. Bxc7 {gives White an extra pawn}) 16. Rad1 {, with a decisive advantage.}) 15. Nxe4 Bxe5 16. Nf3 Bg7 {Alexander Volzhin: 'The only move.'} ({Alexander Volzhin: 'Grabbing a pawn with'} 16... Bxb2 {Alexander Volzhin: 'fails to'} 17. Rad1 { b4+-  b4+- Alexander Volzhin: 'threatening Nc5'}) ({and} 16... Nc6 {blunders a piece:} 17. Nxe5 Nxe5 18. f4 Nc6 19. Qxd7) 17. Rad1 Qc8 18. Bc4 Be8 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Again Black is ready to complete his development with Nc6 or Nd7, but again Tal doesn't allow it!'} (18... Bg4 $6) 19. Neg5+ $1 $18 {Alexander Volzhin: '!!'} hxg5 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Loses immediately, but other moves are also hopeless:'} (19... Kg8 20. Ne6 $18) (19... Kh8 20. Qf4 hxg5 (20... Qf5 21. Qxf5 gxf5 22. Rd8 $1 {The rest is easy} Bc6 23. Nxf7+ Kh7 24. Re7 Bxf3 (24... Bf6 25. N7g5+ Kg6 26. Rxf8 Bxe7 27. Rg8+ Kf6 28. Nh7#) 25. Ng5+ Kg6 26. Rxg7+ Kxg7 27. Ne6+) 21. Nxg5 Bh6 22. Nxf7+ $1 $18) 20. Nxg5+ Kg8 21. Qf4 Nd7 {Alexander Volzhin: 'Too late...'} 22. Rxd7 $1 Bxd7 ({Mate is unavoidable after} 22... Qxd7 23. Qh4) 23. Bxf7+ 1-0

