1. e4 {1) Tal in Bulletin ZSK 1964, no 7 (37), p.3-4. Reprinted and translated into german in 2) Kirillov: Michael Tal. Sein Lebenswerk 1962-1973. Chessgate. 2004. S.65-67.} c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. Ndb5 Bb4 7. a3 Bxc3+ 8. Nxc3 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Bd2 O-O 11. Qh5 $1 Nxc3 12. Bxc3 e5 13. Bd3 g6 14. Qh6 Qf6 15. O-O {Mikhail Tal: '!'} ({But not} 15. O-O-O Bf5 $1 {.}) 15... Qg7 {[#]} 16. Qe3 $1 {Mikhail Tal: 'Threatening 17 f4.'} g5 17. h4 h6 18. hxg5 hxg5 19. f3 Be6 20. Kf2 Nd4 21. Rae1 {Mikhail Tal: 'Preventing the blocking of the b1-h7 diagonal.'} Nc6 22. Rh1 ({Transposing into an ending a pawn up by} 22. Bxe5 Nxe5 23. Qxe5 Rae8 24. Rh1 {seemed insufficient to me.}) 22... f6 23. Rh7 Qxh7 24. Bxh7+ Kxh7 25. Qd3+ Kg7 26. Rh1 Rh8 27. Rxh8 Rxh8 28. Qd6 Re8 29. b4 a6 30. a4 Kf7 31. Qd3 Kg7 32. b5 Rd8 33. Qe4 Bd5 34. Qg4 axb5 35. axb5 Ne7 36. Bb4 Ng6 37. Ba5 Ra8 38. Qd7+ Bf7 39. Bd8 {[%csl Rf6] [#] Mikhail Tal: 'The point of White's plan: f6 has been selected as the target.'} Nf4 40. Kg1 Ra2 41. Qf5 Nd5 42. c4 Ra8 ({If} 42... Rxg2+ {, then} 43. Kh1 {.}) 43. Qd7 Nf4 44. Qe7 Ra1+ 45. Kh2 Ra2 46. Qxf6+ Kg8 47. Qxg5+ Bg6 48. Qxe5 Rxg2+ 49. Kh1 Rd2 50. Qxf4 Rxd8 51. Qc7 1-0

