1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. c3 d5 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 11. Rxe5 c6 12. d4 Bd6 13. Re1 Qh4 14. g3 Qh3 15. Be3 Bg4 16. Qd3 Rae8 17. Nd2 Re6 18. a4 Qh5 {various: 'Diagram # The debut of this important variation. Black does not risk a wild attack against his great opponent but trusrs his positional compensation for the sacrificed pawn. Previously Spassky had played 18...bxa4 (against Novpashin, Stein and Parma) so he thus avoided Tal's preparations which were probably extremely detailed. (One may speculate that Tal might have played the line which later surfaced in Gurvich-Grzeskowiak.) Note that Spassky NEVER played 18...f5? which most theoreticians subsequently gave us the main line in books and articles.'} 19. axb5 axb5 20. c4 {Blatny,P: '?!'} bxc4 (20... Bf5 21. Qe2 Bg4 22. cxd5 $1 {Queen sacrifice idea analysed by Pachman:} (22. Qf1 {Shamkovich & Peterson analysed} Bh3 23. Bd1 Bxf1 (23... Qf5 $2 24. Qe2 Nf4 25. Qf3 Nd3 26. Qxf5 Bxf5 27. Bc2 $1) 24. Bxh5 Bxc4 25. Nxc4 bxc4 26. Rac1 Bb4 27. Re2 c3 28. bxc3 Nxc3 $1 29. Rec2 Nd5 30. Rxc6 Nxe3 31. Rxe6 fxe6 32. fxe3 Bd2 $11) 22... Bxe2 23. dxe6 fxe6 24. Bxe6+ Kh8 25. Rac1 $13) (20... Nxe3 $1 21. Rxe3 Be2 $1 22. Qc2 Rh6 23. h4 Bf4 $17) 21. Nxc4 Bb4 22. Rec1 Be2 23. Bd1 Qxh2+ {various: 'A slight inaccuracy by Spassky.'} (23... Bxd3 $142 $11 {Parma-Geller}) 24. Kxh2 Bxd3 25. Ne5 Bb5 (25... Be4 26. Bb3) (25... Nxe3 {best?} 26. Nxd3 Nxd1 27. Nxb4 Nxb2 28. Rxc6 Re2 $140 29. Rc2 $1 {Pachman}) 26. Bb3 Rd8 27. Ra7 {[#]} f6 $11 {various: 'Diagram # Here Tal missed his chance to put on some pressure.'} 28. Nxc6 {various: 'White could also have played'} (28. Rd7 Rxd7 29. Nxd7 Rd6 30. Nb6 Rd8 31. Nxd5 cxd5 32. Rc7 Bf8 33. Rb7 Be8 34. Ba2 Bf7 35. b4 {etc. (Sakharov & Peterson)}) (28. Nf7 Rb8 29. Bxd5 cxd5 30. Bf4 Rbe8 31. Rb7 $16 {Simagin}) 28... Bxc6 (28... Rxc6 29. Ra8 Rcd6 30. Rcc8 Ba5 31. Rxd8+ Bxd8 32. Bf4 Rd7 33. Bc7 $3) 29. Ra6 Kf8 {various: ''} (29... Rc8 30. Raxc6 Rcxc6 31. Rxc6 Rxc6 32. Bxd5+) 30. Raxc6 Rxc6 31. Rxc6 Nxe3 32. fxe3 Bd2 {various: '='} 33. Bc4 (33. Re6 Rb8) 33... Bxe3 34. d5 Bd2 35. Rb6 Ke7 36. Re6+ Kf8 37. g4 1/2-1/2

