{[%mdl 8256] C90: Closed Ruy Lopez with 7...d6: Early deviations} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. d3 d6 9. c3 Na5 10. Bc2 c5 11. Nbd2 Re8 12. Nf1 Bf8 13. Ne3 Bb7 14. b4 cxb4 15. cxb4 Nc6 16. a3 d5 17. Nxd5 Nxd5 18. exd5 Qxd5 {last book move} 19. Bb3 {White threatens to win material: Bb3xd5} Qd7 {Black has an active position} 20. Ng5 {White threatens to win material: Ng5xf7} Nd8 21. Qh5 {[%cal Rb3f7,Rg5f7,Rh5f7,Gd7f7,Gd8f7,Gg8f7] f7 becomes the focus of attention. White has a mate threat} h6 {Black threatens to win material: h6xg5} 22. Re3 (22. Nf3 Bd5 23. Bxd5 Qxd5 24. Rxe5 Rxe5 25. Qxe5 Qxd3 $11) 22... Bd5 (22... Qf5 $142 23. Rh3 e4 24. Nxf7 Qxh5 25. Nxh6+ Kh7 26. Rxh5 gxh6 $17) 23. Bxd5 $11 Qxd5 24. Ne4 Re6 25. Rg3 Kh8 26. Be3 a5 27. Bc5 Bxc5 28. Nxc5 {Menacing} (28. bxc5 Ra7 $11) 28... Rf6 29. Rf1 $2 (29. Ne4 $142 {and White is still in the game} Rc6 30. Rd1 $11) 29... axb4 $17 30. axb4 Rxf2 $1 {Mate attack} 31. Re1 (31. Rxf2 Ra1+ {Mate attack}) (31. Kxf2 Qd4+ {Double attack} (31... Ra2+ {Deflection})) (31. Z0 $140 Rxf1+ {Threat} 32. Kxf1 Ra1+ 33. Ke2 (33. Kf2 Qd4+ {Double attack} (33... Ra2+ {Deflection})) (33. Qd1 Rxd1+ {Combination}) 33... Ra2+ {Combination}) 31... Rf4 32. h3 Ra1 33. Rxa1 Qd4+ 34. Kh2 Qxa1 35. d4 $2 (35. Re3 Nc6 36. Ne4 Qa2 $19) 35... Nc6 36. Ne6 $4 {a blunder in a bad position} (36. Nd3 Rf1 37. Rf3 $19) 36... Rf1 37. Rxg7 (37. Re3 {is the last straw} exd4 38. Re4 Rh1+ 39. Kg3 Qc3+ 40. Kf2 fxe6 41. Rxe6 $19) 37... Rh1+ 38. Kg3 Qe1+ 39. Kg4 Qe2+ 40. Kh4 Qxh5+ (40... Qf2+ $142 {it becomes clear that Black will call all the shots} 41. Rg3 Qf6+ 42. Rg5 Nxd4 $19) 41. Kxh5 Rf1 42. d5 Nd8 43. Kxh6 $4 {the pressure is too much, White crumbles} (43. Rg3 $142 fxe6 44. dxe6 Nxe6 45. Re3 $19) 43... Nxe6 44. Rh7+ (44. Rg4 {is one last hope} Rf6+ 45. Kh5 Nf4+ 46. Kg5 Nxd5 47. Re4 $19) 44... Kg8 45. dxe6 Rf6+ 46. Kg5 Rg6+ 47. Kf5 Kxh7 48. exf7 Kg7 0-1

