'= Bouwmeester/Withuis'''} 29. Qd5 {Hübner Huebner,R: '!' Huebner: 'HÃ'Hübner Garry Kasparov: 'Huebner: 'Hübner''' bner Huebner,Robert: 'Hübner''} ({Huebner: 'Garry Kasparov: 'Tal's move''} 29. Qh5 {Tal Huebner,R: '!''Tal Garry Kasparov: 'can also be answered by' Garry Kasparov: 'can also be answered by Huebner: 'Tal'''} Rf8 (29... Re5) 30. Qxh7 Re5 {and it's anybody's game. When, oh when are people going to realize that it's unwise to allow Tal a pawn on the seventh rank?}) 29... Re5 (29... Re6 {Huebner,R: '?'} 30. Rb6 $18) 30. Qxf7 (30. Qxc4 $5) 30... Rxa5 (30... h5 {Huebner: 'Garry Kasparov: '!' '!''} 31. Rb6 Nxa5 32. Re6 Nc6 33. Rxe5 fxe5 34. Qxc4 a5 {with advantage to Black.}) 31. Qxh7 $16 {h Huebner,R: 'Myers: According to Huebner, although Black is probably equal her'h Garry Kasparov: 'is not so clear' Garry Kasparov: 'is not so clear Huebner: '' Huebner: 'h''' e.' Huebner: 'h Huebner,Robert: 'h''} Rd8 32. Qf7 Rad5 33. Kg2 a5 34. h4 Kd6 $1 $132 {Myers}) (28... Nxe7 {Huebner,R: '!?' Huebner,R: 'Christiansen Fritz 5.00 (5s): '''} 29. Qh5 (29. Qf3 f5) (29. Qc2 f5 30. Qb2 Rc8 (30... Kd6 31. Qb7 Ra7 32. Qb8+ $16 Ke6 (32... Kc6 33. Rb6+) 33. Rb6+) 31. Qb7+ Kd8 32. Qxa6 (32. Rd1+ Ke8) 32... Re2 $17) (29. Qd2 Ra7 $17) 29... f5 30. Qxf7 (30. Qxh7 Rd8 31. Qxf7 {Huebner,R: '?!'} (31. Rb2 Rd3 32. Qh8 Nc8 33. Kg2 Nd6 34. Qb8+ Kd7 35. Rb7+ Nxb7 36. Qxb7+ Kd6 37. Qxa6+ Ke7 $11 {Myers}) 31... Rd3 (31... Rd2 $1 $11) 32. Kg2 Rxc3 33. h4 Rc2 34. Rf1 {Timman} Rd2 $17 {Huebner: 'Huebner,Robert: '   ''}) 30... Rd8 { 31... d3, 31... d2  Huebner,R: '=' Huebner: ' 31... d3, 31... d2  Huebner,Robert: ' 31... d3, 31... d2 ''}) 29. Rb7+ {!! Unzicker !! Unzicker Cyrus Lakdawala: '!' '!' Cyrus Lakdawala: 'ANSWER: Decoy rook sacrifice to b7.'!! Unzicker Garry Kasparov: '!' '!' Garry Kasparov: 'Of course!' Garry Kasparov: 'Of course! Huebner: '!! Unzicker'''  --- Of all the people who made a pact with Satan, Tal was clearly the devil's favourite.' Huebner,R: '!'} Kxb7 30. Qd7+ Kb8 31. e8=Q+ {Cyrus Lakdawala: 'White's two queens believe they are Bonnie and Clyde, or maybe Bonnie and Bonnie. "Why didn't I take the e7-pawn when I had the chance??" Keller must have lamented at this stage.'} Rxe8 32. Qxe8+ Kb7 33. Qd7+ Kb8 34. Qxc6 {Cyrus Lakdawala: '. The queen's hunger is finally abated.'} Ba3 35. Qe8+ Kb7 36. Qxf7+ Kb8 37. Qxc4 $18 {1-0 (37) Tal,M-Keller,D Zuerich 1959 Tal Games [Huebner,R]} 1-0

