1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. dxe5 Be6 9. c3 Be7 10. Be3 O-O 11. Nbd2 Qd7 {Myers Marin: 'Marin: Nowadays, this is a well-known position in the Ruy Lopez, but back in 1962 there was still plenty of room for improvisation.'} 12. Nd4 $2 {Myers Marin: 'Marin: Tal probably hoped that after capturing the pawn Black's pieces would remain exposed in the center, thus giving force to his attack based on f2-f4-f5-f6. However, he failed to take into account all of the tactical complexities.' Another example of Mihail Tal's romantic style. However, this time it did not work out... Another example of Mihail Tal's romantic style. However, this time it did not work out...} (12. Re1 $142 Rad8 13. Bc2 Nxd2 14. Qxd2 Bg4 15. Qd3 g6 16. Bh6 Rfe8 17. Rad1 Na5 18. h3 Bxf3 19. Qxf3 c5 20. Qg3 Nc4 21. b3 Na3 22. e6 Qc6 23. Bf5 Bf6 24. Bg5 Bxg5 25. Qxg5 Rd6 26. Qf6 Rdxe6 27. Bxe6 fxe6 28. h4 b4 29. cxb4 Nc2 30. Re5 Nd4 31. h5 Rf8 32. Qg5 Nf5 33. hxg6 h6 34. Qc1 Qd6 35. Rde1 {1-0 Kamsky,G-Piket,J/Dos Hermanas 1995/}) (12. Bc2 $142 f5 13. exf6 Nxf6 14. Qb1 Bg4 15. h3 Bxh3 16. Ng5 Ng4 17. Nxh3 Qd6 18. Re1 d4 19. cxd4 Qh2+ 20. Kf1 Bb4 21. Bb3+ Kh8 22. Qe4 Bxd2 23. Qxg4 Bxe1 24. Rxe1 Rae8 25. Ng1 Qd6 26. Nf3 Na5 27. Bc2 Nc4 28. Qh4 h6 29. Ne5 Nxe5 30. Qe4 Ng6 31. Qxg6 Qxg6 32. Bxg6 Re6 33. Bd3 c6 34. b4 g5 35. d5 Kg8 36. dxe6 {1-0 Keres,P-Friedemann,G/corr 1936/}) 12... Nxd2 {Myers Marin: '!'} 13. Qxd2 (13. Bxd2 Nxe5 14. Bc2 Nc4 15. Bc1 Bf6 16. b3 Nd6 17. Qd3 g6 18. Bh6 Rfe8 $17 {Myers}) 13... Nxe5 (13... Na5 $2 14. Bc2 (14. Nxe6 $1 fxe6 15. Bc2 Nc4 16. Qd3 g6 17. Bh6 $14 {Myers}) 14... c5 15. Qd3 g6 16. Nxe6 fxe6 17. Bh6 Rf7 18. Rae1 Nc6 19. f4 Bf8 20. Bg5 Be7 21. Bh6 Bf8 22. Bg5 Ne7 23. g4 Re8 24. h4 d4 25. cxd4 c4 26. Qe4 h5 27. gxh5 gxh5 28. Bxe7 Qxe7 29. f5 Rg7+ 30. Kf2 exf5 31. Qd5+ Kh8 32. Qf3 Qxh4+ 33. Ke2 Qxd4 34. Rg1 Rxe5+ {0-1 Kitto,F-Euwe,M/Bournemouth 1939/}) 14. f4 (14. Bc2 Nc4 15. Qd3 g6 16. Bh6 Nxb2 $1 17. Qg3 Rfe8 18. Rae1 Bf6 19. f4 Qd6 $1 $19 {Marin}) 14... Nc4 15. Bxc4 (15. Qf2 Nxe3 16. Qxe3 c5 {Marin} 17. Nxe6 Qxe6 18. Rae1 c4 19. Qxe6 fxe6 20. Bd1 Bc5+ 21. Kh1 Rf6 22. Bg4 Re8 $17 {Myers}) 15... dxc4 16. f5 Bd5 17. f6 {Myers Marin: '!?' White is being consequent. Otherwise he is just a pawn down, without any compensation. White is being consequent. Otherwise he is just a pawn down, without any compensation.} (17. g4 $2 c5 $1 18. Nf3 Qb7 19. Qf2 Rfe8 $19 {Myers}) (17. Qf2 $6 Be4 $1 18. Rfe1 Rfe8 19. Bf4 Bf6 $19 {Myers}) 17... Bxf6 18. Rxf6 {Myers Marin: '?!'} (18. Nf5 $5 {[%cal Yf5h6]} Kh8 $1 19. Rad1 c6 20. Bd4 Bxd4+ 21. Qxd4 Qa7 $19 {Marin}) 18... gxf6 19. Bg5 $146 {Myers Marin: 'N!?' Myers Marin: 'Myers: It is entirely possible that Tal was aware of the game Enevoldsen-Unzicker from Oldenburg 1949 and felt that White's play at this point could be improved.'} (19. Bh6 Rfe8 20. Rf1 Re4 21. h3 Qd6 22. Nf5 Qe5 23. Ne3 Be6 24. Rf3 Kh8 25. Kf2 Rg8 26. a3 Rh4 {0-1 Enevoldsen,J-Unzicker,W/Oldenburg 1949 (26) Myers Marin: '0-1 Enevoldsen,J-Unzicker,W/Oldenburg 1949/'}) (19. Rf1 Be4 $1 20. Bh6 Rfe8 21. Qf4 Qd6 22. Qh4 Bg6 23. Bf4 Qe7 24. Bd2 c5 $19 {Myers}) 19... Qg4 $1 (19... fxg5 $4 20. Qxg5+ Kh8 21. Qf6+ Kg8 22. Nf5 {and white is on top. and white is on top.} Qxf5 $8 23. Qxf5 c6 24. Rf1 $16 {Marin}) 20. Bxf6 c5 {Myers Marin: '!' Myers Marin: 'Marin: A logical complement to the previous move: Black fights for the initiative by driving the knight to a passive square while this is still possible. At the same time, he correctly evaluates that the apparently loose position of his bishop has no relevance here.' Driving away the knight from it's active position. Driving away the knight from it's active position.} 21. Nc2 (21. Nxb5 $2 Bxg2 22. Qxg2 Qxg2+ 23. Kxg2 axb5 24. Kf3 Rfe8 25. Rg1+ Kf8 $19 {Korchnoi}) 21... Qg6 {Myers Marin: '?!'} ({Probably more accurate is Probably more accurate is} 21... Be4 {Myers Marin: '!'} 22. Rf1) 22. Rf1 {Myers Marin: '?'} ({Objectively better was Objectively better was} 22. Be7 {still retaining some chances. For instanse: still retaining some chances. For instanse:} Rfe8 $6 (22... Be4 23. Bxf8 Rxf8 24. Ne1 (24. Ne3 f5 25. Re1 f4 $19) 24... Re8 25. b3 cxb3 26. axb3 Qf6 $19 {Marin}) 23. Qxd5 Qxc2 24. Rf1 Qg6 25. Rf3) (22. Qxd5 $2 Qxf6 23. Qxc5 $19 {Korchnoi}) 22... Be4 23. Ne3 Rae8 $19 {Myers Marin: 'Marin: 'A better way to reach the game position.''} (23... Rfe8 $5) 24. h3 {Myers Marin: '?!'} (24. Rf4 $142 h5 25. Qf2 Re6 26. Qh4 Kh7 $1 27. Be7 Re8 $1 $19 {Marin}) 24... Re6 25. Ng4 h5 26. Ne5 (26. Rf4 Rfe8 $1 27. Bh4 Bf5 $1 28. Qd5 Bxg4 29. hxg4 hxg4 30. Qd7 Re4 $19 {Myers}) 26... Qg3 {Myers Marin: '!'} 27. Qf2 {White is forced to exchange queens and go for the hopeless endgame, otherwise heavy material losses are inevitable. White is forced to exchange queens and go for the hopeless endgame, otherwise heavy material losses are inevitable.} (27. Nd7 Rd6 $1 28. Qe2 Bxg2 $1 29. Qxg2 Qxg2+ 30. Kxg2 Rxd7 $19 {Marin}) 27... Qxf2+ 28. Rxf2 Rfe8 29. Nd7 Bc6 30. Nxc5 Re1+ 31. Rf1 (31. Kh2 R8e2 $19) 31... R8e2 32. Rxe1 Rxe1+ 33. Kf2 Rb1 34. b4 cxb3 35. axb3 a5 0-1

