1. d4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir Sokolov,Vladimir} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. Nc3 Bb4 5. cxd5 exd5 6. Bg5 h6 7. Bh4 c5 8. e3 O-O 9. Be2 $6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Practice has proven that the development of the bishop to e2 is too modest. Swapping the c5-pawn may not promise much, but it forces Black in a well defined direction with little risk for the first player.'} (9. Bd3 $1 {Sokolov,Vladimir}) (9. dxc5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} Nbd7 (9... Nc6 10. Be2 Be6 11. O-O Bxc5 {Black is accepting a standard type of position with an isolated pawn on d5.}) 10. Be2 (10. Rc1 Qa5 11. Nd2 g5 (11... Re8 $2 12. a3 Bxc3 13. Rxc3 d4 14. Nb3 Qd8 15. Qxd4 g5 16. Bg3 Ne4 17. Rc1 Qe7 18. Bd6 Qe6 19. Bc4 Qg6 20. O-O $18 {1-0 Nyback,T (2458)-Kanep,M (2445)/Jyvaskyla 2003 (34)}) (11... b6 $2 12. c6 d4 13. exd4 (13. cxd7 $1 Nxd7 14. Nb5 dxe3 15. fxe3 $18) 13... Re8+ 14. Be2 Ba6 15. cxd7 Nxd7 16. O-O Bxc3 17. Bxa6 Bxd2 18. Rc7 Qxa6 19. Qxd2 Re2 20. Qd1 Nf8 21. d5 $16 {1-0 Horvath,J (2545)-Zaiatz,E (2340)/Leeuwarden 1993 (27)}) 12. Bg3 Nxc5 13. Be5 Nfe4 14. a3 Bxc3 15. Bxc3 Nxc3 16. Rxc3 Ne4 17. Nxe4 dxe4 18. Bc4 $14) 10... Bxc3+ (10... Qa5 11. O-O $1 Bxc3 12. bxc3 Qxc5 (12... Ne4 13. c4 dxc4 14. Bxc4 Ndxc5 15. Nd4 $14) 13. Rc1 b6 (13... Qe7 { ...b6}) 14. c4 Bb7 15. Nd4 Rac8 (15... dxc4 $142 16. Bxc4 Qa5 $14) 16. Bf3 Qb4 17. a3 $1 Qxa3 18. Ra1 Qc5 19. Rxa7 $16 {1-0 Petrosian,T-Matanovic,A/Portoroz 1958 (23)}) 11. bxc3 Nxc5 12. O-O Nce4 13. Rc1 Qa5 14. Bxf6 Nxf6 15. Qb3 b6 16. Nd4 Bd7 17. Qb4 Qa4 18. Qxa4 Bxa4 $11 {1-0 Levin,F (2445)-Mitkov,N (2490)/Groningen 1991 (71)}) 9... g5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Black can play 9..c4 immediately. It is quite amazing, how often Black's pawn structure c4-d5 solves at least some of his problems in this opening.'} (9... c4 $5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} 10. O-O (10. Nd2 Bxc3 11. bxc3 Bf5 12. O-O (12. e4 Bxe4 13. Nxe4 dxe4 14. Qa4 Nbd7 15. Qxc4 Rc8 16. Qb3 Qa5 17. Rc1 Nd5 18. O-O Rxc3 19. Qxb7 Rxc1 20. Rxc1 Qd2 21. Rf1 N7b6 $17 {½-½ Gavrikov,V (2430)-Kupreichik,V (2570)/Yerevan 1982 (32)}) 12... Re8 13. e4 Bxe4 14. Nxe4 Rxe4 15. Bxf6 gxf6 16. Qd2 Kg7 17. Bf3 Re6 18. Qf4 Na6 19. Qg4+ Kf8 20. Qh5 f5 21. Qxf5 Nc7 22. Rae1 $16 {½-½ Dautov,R (2515)-Shereshevski,M/Minsk 1988 (61)}) 10... g5 11. Bg3 Bxc3 12. bxc3 Ne4 13. Rc1 Nc6 14. Nd2 Nxg3 15. hxg3 f5 16. g4 b5 17. Bf3 fxg4 18. Bxg4 a5 19. a3 Qd6 20. Bf3 Be6 21. e4 $13 {½-½ Geller,E (2545)-Kupreichik,V (2570)/Yerevan 1982 (34)}) 10. Bg3 Ne4 11. Rc1 Qa5 (11... c4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} 12. Nd2 Nxg3 13. hxg3 Kg7 14. b3 Ba3 (14... cxb3 15. Qxb3 Qa5 16. Ndb1 Nc6 17. Bf3 Be6 $14) 15. Rb1 Bf5 $2 (15... Bb4 16. Qc2 Qa5 17. Rc1 $14) 16. bxc4 Bxb1 17. Qxb1 Nd7 18. Nxd5 $16 {1-0 Roiz,M (2659)-Berkovich,M (2413)/Israel 2008 (32)}) 12. O-O Bxc3 13. bxc3 c4 $1 14. Ne5 {Sokolov,Vladimir: '!' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Tal prefers to play a bit in the style of va banque as compared to the more solid defence of the c3-pawn.'} (14. Qc2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} Bf5 15. Qb2 Nc6 16. Rfd1 (16. Qxb7 Qb6 $15) 16... Qb6 17. Qa3 $11) 14... f6 15. Ng6 Rf7 16. Bh5 (16. Bxb8 Rxb8 17. Bh5 Rg7 18. f3 Nd6 (18... Nxc3 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} 19. Qe1 Bf5 $15) 19. e4 {Sokolov,Vladimir: '' Ftacnik,Lubomir: ''}) 16... Nc6 17. f4 $2 (17. Nf4 $5 Rf8 (17... gxf4 18. Bxf7+ Kxf7 19. Qh5+ Kg7 20. Bxf4 Ng5 21. Bxg5 hxg5 22. f4 { Sokolov,Vladimir: '+-'}) (17... Re7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} 18. Ne2 Qxa2 $17) 18. Ne2 f5 19. Be5 Be6 {Sokolov,Vladimir: ''}) (17. f3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} Nxc3 18. Qd2 Na4 $15) 17... Be6 18. fxg5 $2 (18. f5 Bd7 19. Ne5 Re7 20. Ng4 {Sokolov,Vladimir: '' Ftacnik,Lubomir: ''}) 18... hxg5 19. Ne5 $2 (19. Be1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} Rg7 20. h4 Kh7 $17) 19... fxe5 20. Bxf7+ Bxf7 {Sokolov,Vladimir: '-+'} 21. dxe5 Qc5 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: '-+!'} 22. Qf3 Rf8 23. Kh1 Kg7 24. Qg4 Be6 25. Qe2 (25. Qxe6 Nxg3+ 26. hxg3 Rh8+ 27. Kg1 Qxe3+ {Sokolov,Vladimir: '-+'} 28. Rf2 Qxc1+ 29. Rf1 Qe3+ $19) 25... Nxg3+ 26. hxg3 Rh8+ 27. Kg1 Nxe5 28. Rce1 Nd3 29. Qf3 Rh6 30. Rb1 b6 31. Rb5 Qe7 32. e4 a6 33. Qe3 axb5 34. exd5 Qc5 35. Qxc5 bxc5 0-1

