{Petronijevic,Zoran: 'In 1966 when this game was played both Tal and Botvinnik were former World Chess Champions. White plays this game masterfully.' Petronijevic,Zoran: '1966, als diese Partie gespielt wurde, waren Tal und Botwinnik Exweltmeister. Weiß spielte diese Partie meisterlich.'} 1. e4 {Myers Keene Yudovich Petronijevic,Zoran} c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. c4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Qb3 Bg7 7. cxd5 O-O 8. Nge2 ({Nowadays Heute wird} 8. Be2 {Petronijevic,Zoran is more often played. öfter gespielt}) 8... Na6 {Petronijevic,Zoran: 'This move has a complex idea: Black wishes  1. to exchange the queens by playing b6 and to try to exploit weakened white squares (c2 and d3) by playing b4 (as in this game); or 2. to apply the maneuver c7, thus exerting pressure on the d5-square by playing b6 and b7; or 3. to launch an action on the queenside by playing b5 (this idea is applied recently).' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Dieser Zug verfolgt eine komplexe Idee: Schwarz möchte  1. b6 spielen und die Damen tauschen, versuchen, mit b4 die geschwächten weißen Felder (c2 und d3) ausnutzen (wie in dieser Partie); oder 2. das Manöver c7 spielen können, was den Druck auf das Feld d5 verstärkt, b6 und b7 spielen; oder 3. am Damenflügel mit b5 aktiv werden (diese Idee wird neuderdings gespielt).'} 9. g3 {Petronijevic,Zoran: 'For White the most logical plan is to fianchetto his light-squared bishop, thus supporting the d5-square.' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Für Weiß ist der logischste Plan, seinen weißfeldrigen Läufer zu fianchettieren, der dann das Feld d5 kontrolliert. '} Qb6 {Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Black wishes to exchange the queens. Nowadays more often played are the following moves:' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Schwarz möchte die Damen tauschen. Heute werden die folgenden Züge öfter gespielt:'} (9... Nc7 {[%cal Yb7b6,Yc8b7,Yb7d5,Yc7d5,Yf6d5,Yd8d5] Petronijevic,Zoran}) (9... b5 {Petronijevic,Zoran}) 10. Qxb6 ({Inferior is Schlechter ist} 10. Bg2 {Petronijevic,Zoran} Qxb3 11. axb3 Nb4 $11) 10... axb6 11. Bg2 Nb4 {Petronijevic,Zoran: 'This is the idea of 8... a6. Black exerts pressure on the d5-square and threatens c2.' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Das ist die Idee, die hinter 8... a6 steht. Schwarz drückt auf das Feld d5 und droht c2.'} 12. O-O Rd8 {Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Diagram '} 13. d6 $1 {Petronijevic,Zoran: 'An excellent move! It was played for the first time by Spassky. White returns the pawn but increases the scope of g2.' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Ein ausgezeichneter Zug! Er wurde zum ersten Mal von Spassky gespielt. Weiß gibt den Bauern zurück, verlängert aber die Wirkung seines g2.'} exd6 ({Petronijevic,Zoran: 'The move' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Der Zug'} 13... Rxd6 {was played in Spassky-Petrosian, Moscow 1966. Myers Keene Yudovich: '!' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'is discussed in the MODEL GAME Spassky-Petrosian, 1966.' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'wurde in der Modellpartie Spassky-Petrosian, 1966, diskutiert.'} 14. Bg5 {Myers Keene Yudovich} (14. Bf4 {Myers Keene Yudovich} Rd7 15. Rfd1 Nbd5 16. Be5 $14 {Yudovich}) 14... Rd8 15. a3 Nc6 16. Bxf6 exf6 17. Nd5 Bg4 18. Nec3 Nxd4 19. Nxb6 Ra6 20. Nbd5 Nb3 21. Rae1 Nd2 22. Rd1 Nxf1 23. Ne7+ Kf8 24. Rxd8+ Kxe7 25. Rd3 Nxg3 26. hxg3 Be6 27. Bxb7 Ra7 28. Bf3 f5 29. b4 Bc4 30. Re3+ Kd6 31. Bd5 Ba6 32. Bb3 Bd4 33. Rf3 Re7 34. Nd5 Re1+ 35. Kh2 Bb7 36. Re3 Bxe3 37. Nxe3 {0-1 Yepes Martinez,E-Arkell,K/Barcelona ESP 2001/}) 14. Bg5 $1 {Petronijevic,Zoran: '' Myers Keene Yudovich: 'Keene: A brilliant positional move which, surprisingly, decides the game. The exchange of White's QB for Black's KN leaves Black helplessly exposed on the light squares in the center.' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'White has a clear plan to develop the initiative. Since the Black pawns are separated and weak White has a clear advantage.' Petronijevic,Zoran: 'Weiß hat einen klaren Plan, wie er die Initiative verstärken kann. Da die Bauern von Schwarz vereinzelt und schwach sind, steht Weiß klar besser.'} Re8 15. a3 {Myers Keene Yudovich: '!'} (15. Nf4 $2 {Myers Keene Yudovich} Ra5 16. Bxf6 Bxf6 17. a3 Nc6 18. Ne4 Bxd4 19. Nxd6 Rd8 20. Nxc8 Rxc8 21. Rab1 Rd8 22. Rfd1 Kg7 23. Rd2 Be5 24. Rxd8 Nxd8 25. Nd3 Bf6 26. Rc1 Nc6 {½-½ Zude,A-Baumhus,R/Hessen GER 1991/}) 15... Nc6 (15... Nd3 $5 {Petronijevic,Zoran} 16. Bxf6 (16. Rab1 $16 {(Myers Keene Yudovich) Myers}) 16... Bxf6 17. Nd5 Rxe2 18. Nxf6+ Kg7) 16. Rfe1 Bg4 17. Bxf6 {Petronijevic,Zoran: '!?'} ({White wishes to use the d5-square for his pieces. Probably, better is Weiß möchte das Feld d5 für seine Figuren nutzen. Besser ist wahrscheinlich} 17. h3 $1 {Petronijevic,Zoran} Bxe2 18. Nxe2 $16) (17. f3 $2 {Myers Keene Yudovich} Bd7 18. Nb5 Nd5 $14 {Myers}) 17... Bxf6 18. Nd5 (18. Ne4 $5 {Myers Keene Yudovich}) 18... Bd8 (18... Kg7 $142 {Petronijevic,Zoran}) 19. Nec3 Rxe1+ 20. Rxe1 Ra5 $4 {Botvinnik blunders dreadfully. Botvinnik blunders dreadfully. Petronijevic,Zoran: '?' Myers Keene Yudovich: '?'} ({Judovic analyses} 20... Nxd4 $1 {Petronijevic,Zoran: '' Myers Keene Yudovich: ''} 21. Re8+ Kg7 22. Nxb6 Rb8 23. Nc4 {Petronijevic,Zoran: '' Myers Keene Yudovich: ''} Bd7) 21. Ne3 $2 {Petronijevic,Zoran: '?!' Myers Keene Yudovich: '?!' Myers Keene Yudovich: 'Keene: Tal was criticized for this move, but it leaves Black in a deadly vice. It is notoriously difficult to judge positions with two minor pieces for a rook.'} (21. Re8+ $1 Kg7 22. Ne3 $1 Bd7 23. Bxc6 {Petronijevic,Zoran: '+-' Myers Keene Yudovich: '+-'} Bxe8 24. Bxe8 {decides the game at once.}) 21... Bd7 22. Nc4 Ra8 ({Or} 22... Ra6 23. Nb5 $1) 23. d5 Nd4 (23... Ne5 $5 {Myers Keene Yudovich} 24. Nxd6 Nd3 25. Rb1 Bf6 26. Bf1 Nxb2 27. Rxb2 Bxc3 28. Rxb6 Ra7 29. Rb3 $16 {Myers}) 24. Nxd6 Rb8 25. Nce4 (25. Nc4 $5 {Myers Keene Yudovich} Kg7 26. Ne5 Bf5 27. Rd1 Nb3 28. d6 Nc5 29. f4 f6 30. Nf3 $18 {Myers}) 25... f6 26. Nc4 Kf8 27. h3 (27. Nc3 $5 {Myers Keene Yudovich} b5 28. Ne3 Ba5 29. d6 Bc6 30. Ned5 $18 {Myers}) 27... Nb3 28. Bf1 (28. Nc3 $5 {Myers Keene Yudovich} Nc5) 28... b5 (28... Nc5 $5 {Myers Keene Yudovich} 29. Nc3 Na4 (29... Ra8 {Myers Keene Yudovich} 30. Nd6 f5 31. Bb5 Bf6 32. Bxd7 Nxd7 33. Nxb7 Be5 34. Nb5 $18 {Myers}) 30. Nxa4 Bxa4 31. Re3 Rc8 32. Nd6 Rc1 33. Nxb7 Bc7 $16 {Myers}) 29. Ncd6 {Myers Keene Yudovich: '!'} f5 (29... b6 {Myers Keene Yudovich} 30. Rd1 Nc5 31. Nc3 Na4 32. Ndxb5 Nxb2 33. Rb1 Bxb5 34. Nxb5 Na4 35. d6 $18 {Myers}) 30. Re3 {Myers Keene Yudovich: '!'} fxe4 31. Rxb3 Ke7 32. Nxe4 {Petronijevic,Zoran: '+-'} Rc8 (32... Bf5 {Myers Keene Yudovich} 33. Nc3 Kd6 34. g4 Bc2 35. Rxb5 g5 36. Kg2 $18 {Myers}) 33. g4 {Myers Keene Yudovich: '!'} Rc1 34. Kg2 Re1 35. f3 Rd1 36. d6+ Kf7 37. Bxb5 Be6 (37... Bxb5 {Myers Keene Yudovich} 38. Rxb5 b6 39. a4 Rc1 40. b4 Ra1 41. a5 bxa5 42. Rb8 Bh4 43. Rb7+ Ke6 44. Rxh7 Ra2+ 45. Kf1 Ra1+ 46. Ke2 Bd8 47. Rh8 $18 {Myers}) 38. Rc3 (38. Ba4 $1 {Myers Keene Yudovich} b6 39. Rxb6 Rg1+ 40. Kxg1 Bxb6+ 41. Kg2 $18 {Myers}) 38... Rd4 39. Rd3 (39. b4 $1 {Myers Keene Yudovich} h6 40. Rc5 b6 41. Rc1 Rd5 42. Ba6 Re5 43. Kf2 Bd7 44. Bc8 Bb5 45. Rc7+ $1 $18 {Myers}) 39... Rxd3 40. Bxd3 Bd5 41. Nc5 (41. Nc3 $1 {Myers Keene Yudovich} Bb3 42. Be4 b6 43. Bc6 Ke6 44. d7 Kd6 45. Bb5 Be6 46. f4 $18 {[%cal Gg2f3] Myers}) 41... b6 42. Be4 Be6 43. Nd3 Bb3 44. f4 Ke6 45. f5+ 1-0

