queen to c5 and to carefully observe White's operation on the kingside. It is clear that the defense will be arduous, passive, and unpleasant, and we know that Gligoric dislikes passive defense. Be that as it may, I went to the adjournment session ready to accept the fact that a draw would result.'} (41. Qxa5 $2 Qf4+ $11 {Myers Gligoric Tal: 'Gligoric'}) 41... Nf5 (41... h5 $11) 42. Qd1 Qb2 (42... Qc5 $1 {(Myers Gligoric Tal) Tal}) 43. Kg1 Nd6 (43... a4 {Myers Gligoric Tal} 44. d6 Nxd6 45. Qxd6 axb3 46. Qb8+ Kg7 47. axb3 $18 {Tal}) 44. Qg4 (44. g3 $5 {Myers Gligoric Tal}) 44... Qe5 45. g3 h5 46. Qa4 {Myers Gligoric Tal: '!'} Nf5 $2 (46... Qc3 $11 {Myers Gligoric Tal: ''}) 47. Qxa5 Nxg3 $1 {Myers Gligoric Tal: '?'} (47... h4 $8 {Myers Gligoric Tal} 48. g4 Ng3 49. Qd2 Ne2+ 50. Kf1 Nf4 51. Bd1 Nxh3 52. d6 Qh2 53. Qd4 Nf4 54. Qe4 Nh3 55. Qd4 Nf4 56. Qe4 Nh3 $11 {Myers}) 48. fxg3 Qxg3+ 49. Kf1 Qxh3+ 50. Ke2 Qg4+ 51. Kd3 Qg3+ $4 (51... h4 $1 $14) 52. Kc4 $1 h4 53. Kc5 $1 (53. Qb6 $1 {[%cal Gd5d6,Yb6d4] Myers Gligoric Tal} h3 54. d6 h2 55. d7 Qf4+ 56. Qd4 Qc7+ 57. Kb4 Qb8+ 58. Kc3 Qg3+ 59. Kb2 Qg2+ 60. Ka1 h1=Q+ 61. Bd1 Qd5 62. d8=Q+ $18 {Myers}) 53... Qe3+ $18 (53... h3 {Myers Gligoric Tal} 54. d6 h2 55. Bd5 Qg4 56. Qb5 Qc8+ 57. Kb4 Kg7 58. d7 Qd8 59. a4 $18 {Myers}) 54. Kc6 {Myers Gligoric Tal: '!'} Qe8+ 55. Kb7 h3 56. Qc7 Kg7 (56... g5 {Myers Gligoric Tal} 57. Ka6 $1 Kg7 58. Qc3+ Kg8 59. Qxh3 Qa8+ 60. Kb5 Qb8+ 61. Kc4 Qc7+ 62. Kd3 $18 {Myers}) 57. Qc3+ f6 58. Qxh3 Qb5+ 59. Kc7 Qc5+ 60. Kd7 Qa7+ 61. Ke8 Qb8+ 62. Ke7 Qe5+ 63. Qe6 Qc7+ 64. Qd7 Qe5+ 65. Kd8+ Kf8 66. Kc8 1-0

