Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak: '1-0 Avrukh,B-Donk,M/Antwerp 1998/'} Kxg5 25. Qh5+ {Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak: '1-0 De La Vega,H-Gonzalez,G/Mar del Plata ARG 1970/'} Kf4 26. Qf5#) 23. Nxf7+ Kh7 (23... Kxh5 {Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak} 24. g4+ Kg6 25. Qf5# {Burgess}) 24. Qf5+ Kg8 25. e6 $1 {Diagram [#] Polugaevsky had reached this position during his analysis when Geller entered his room. Judging from a later comment by Polugaevsky, ("an analysis until move 25") he had stopped here. Of course, excellent intuition is needed to do that, as White still is a piece down, but Polugaevsky rightly evaluated that the e-pawn has a decisive strength. ***To the young modern player, Polugaevsky's analysis may not seem so impressive. But we have to take into account that nowadays one only has to push the engines a bit to work out such an analysis or longer. In 1969, a chess playing computer existed only in the dreams of such visionaries as Botvinnik. Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'Diagram [#] Polugaevsky had reached this position during his analysis when Geller entered his room. Judging from a later comment by Polugaevsky, ("an analysis until move 25") he had stopped here. Of course, excellent intuition is needed to do that, as White still is a piece down, but Polugaevsky rightly evaluated that the e-pawn has a decisive strength. ***To the young modern player, Polugaevsky's analysis may not seem so impressive. But we have to take into account that nowadays one only has to push the engines a bit to work out such an analysis or longer. In 1969, a chess playing computer existed only in the dreams of such visionaries as Botvinnik.'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'Diagram [#] Polugaevsky had reached this position during his analysis when Geller entered his room. Judging from a later comment by Polugaevsky, ("an analysis until move 25") he had stopped here. Of course, excellent intuition is needed to do that, as White still is a piece down, but Polu