32. f3 Ree8 33. Nd4 Ba6 34. g4 $16 {Myers}) (28... Kg7 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) (R.Scherbakov) was losing to} 29. e7 $18 {followed by Nf7-d8. 'with the idea' 30.Nd8$18}) 29. Nh6+ $1 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '!' '!' Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Shifting the knight to the dominating position on f5.'''} ({The pawn on e6 could not be saved anyway:} 29. Rbe2 $6 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) R.Scherbakov} Bc8) (29. f3 $5 {Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak}) 29... Kh7 30. Nf5 {Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak: '!' Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak: 'Keres: Returning the extra pawn, White builds up an easily won endgame. The knight on f5 in conjunction with the bad position of Black's king will decide.'} Rexe6 31. Rxe6 Rxe6 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Black has restored the material balance but it won't make his life easier.'''} 32. Rc2 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: '!'''} Rc6 ({After} 32... Bc6 {(Knaak,Rainer) (Polugaevsky,Lev) (R.Scherbakov) White would simply improve by} 33. g4 a5 34. f3 {etc.}) 33. Re2 $18 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-' '+-' Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Securing a decisive invasion. White's powerful rook on the 7th rank, combined with no less a powerful knight on f6 and strong h5-passer give Black no chance to survive.''' Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak: '!' Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak: 'Keres: The decisive maneuver. Black cannot prevent the white 's penetration to the 7th rank.'} Bc8 ({Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Or'''} 33... Rc7 34. Re6 $18 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-'' Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: '+-' '+-''} Bc8 {Knaak,Rainer Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov''} 35. Rxf6 Bxf5 36. Rxf5 $18 {Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak: 'Polugaevsky'}) 34. Re7+ Kh8 {Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak: '?'} (34... Kg8 $142 $5 {Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak}) 35. Nh4 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'With a simple idea to give checkmate by 36. Ng6 Kg8 37.h6 and 38.Rg7X''' ! 'with the idea' 36.Ng6 Kg8 37.h6} f5 36. Ng6+ Kg8 37. Rxa7 {Knaak,Rainer: 'Polugaevsky,Lev: 'R.Scherbakov: 'Black resigned. Wonderful play by Lev Polugaevsky!''' Myers Burgess Keres Belov Polugaevsky Knaak: 'Polugaevsky: It goes without saying that an innovation lasting 25 moves is a rarity, but it once more emphasizes what a great return--both competetive and creative--a player can expect from searching and experimenting. In itself, such a success far exceeds the disappointment from other, less successful attempts, and it is quite capable of inspiring a player, as the game with Tal inspired me in that USSR Championship.'} 1-0

