1. c4 {Berg,Emanuel} g6 {Berg,Emanuel: 'Black is in no hurry to take control in the centre but rather gives white the opportunity to grab more central space.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Schwarz hat es nicht eilig, die Kontrolle im Zentrum zu übernehmen, sondern gibt Weiß die Möglichkeit, mehr Raum im Zentrum zu gewinnen.'} 2. Nc3 {Berg,Emanuel: 'Larsen prefers not to push his d-pawn and we soon enter a symetrical English setup.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Larsen zieht es vor, seinen d-Bauern nicht zu schieben und wir kommen bald in eine symmetrische Englisch-Stellung.'} Bg7 3. Nf3 c5 {Mikhail Tal: 'Since White, by avoiding the advance of his d-pawn, has not insisted on the King's Indian Defence, the game now goes into one of the popular systems of the English Opening. The theoretical opinion, that Black obtains a comfortable position, has been confirmed on numerous occasions. The one drawback to the system was disclosed by Taimanov in my game with him a few rounds earlier. If White wants to draw, then he can. But against a player like Larsen, one doesn't have to worry about such 'aggressive peacefulness'. '} 4. g3 {Berg,Emanuel: 'Alike black white now heads for a fianchetto on the kingside.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Ähnlich wie Schwarz-Weiß steuert nun ein Fianchetto am Königsflügel an.'} Nc6 5. Bg2 e6 {Berg,Emanuel: '!?' Berg,Emanuel: 'Black breaks the symmetry and aims for a setup with the knight on e7 which will keep the long diagonal open for his bishop.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Schwarz durchbricht die Symmetrie und strebt einen Aufbau mit dem Springer auf e7 an, der die lange Diagonale für seinen Läufer offen hält.'} 6. O-O {Berg,Emanuel: 'White continues with normal development which does not cause black any particular difficulties in the opening.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Weiß fährt mit einer normalen Entwicklung fort, die Schwarz in der Eröffnung keine besonderen Schwierigkeiten bereitet.'} ({A sharp move worth paying attention to is Ein scharfer Zug, den es zu beachten gilt, ist} 6. d4 $5 {Berg,Emanuel This pawn sacrifice opens up the position and the newly weakend square on d6 might become an issue for black while his king in the centre also might become a target. Dieses Bauernopfer öffnet die Stellung und das neu entstandene Schwachfeld auf d6 könnte für Schwarz zum Problem werden, während sein König im Zentrum ebenfalls zum Ziel werden könnte.}) 6... Nge7 7. d3 {Mikhail Tal: 'The supposition is proved correct; the Danish grandmaster avoids a symmetrical pawn set-up in the centre.' Berg,Emanuel: 'White continues to play solid but also rather passive which gives black a comfortable game.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Weiß spielt weiterhin solide, aber auch ziemlich passiv, was Schwarz ein komfortables Spiel ermöglicht.'} ({Once again Wieder einmal sind} 7. d4 $5 {Berg,Emanuel or oder}) (7. e3 {Berg,Emanuel intending d4 are interesting alternatives. beabsichtigend d4 interessante Alternativen.}) 7... O-O 8. Bd2 (8. Bf4 $5 {Ü 13/731}) 8... d5 $11 {Berg,Emanuel: 'Finally black is the one who is first to push another pawn into the centre.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Schließlich ist Schwarz derjenige, der als erster einen weiteren Bauern ins Zentrum schiebt.'} 9. Qc1 {Mikhail Tal: 'As the Petrosian-Fischer game from the 'Match of the Century' showed, immediate operations on the queenside similarly do not promise White a great deal. Larsen aims to exchange off the dark-squared bishops, but while he is doing this Black has time to become fully mobilised. ' Berg,Emanuel: 'White aims for an exchange of the dark squared bishops. However this gives black plenty of extra time to take further control in the centre and allowing the exchange of bishops is not much of a problem.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Weiß strebt einen Abtausch der schwarzfeldrigen Läufer an. Dies verschafft Schwarz jedoch viel zusätzliche Zeit, um die Kontrolle im Zentrum zu übernehmen, und der Läufertausch ist kein großes Problem.'} (9. a3 {Ü 9/55} b6) (9. Rb1 b6 10. a3 {Ü 10/81}) 9... b6 10. Bh6 Bb7 (10... d4 $5 {Berg,Emanuel}) 11. Bxg7 Kxg7 {=} 12. cxd5 {Mikhail Tal: 'Here White already had to reckon with the possibility of the advance ...d4.' Berg,Emanuel: 'White opens up the centre avoiding the advance ...d4 by black. Now black's king might also become more exposed.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Weiß öffnet das Zentrum und verhindert den Vorstoß ...d4 von Schwarz. Nun könnte auch der schwarze König stärker exponiert werden.'} (12. b3 $6 {?!} d4 $15 {Ü 10/82}) 12... Nxd5 {Mikhail Tal: 'The position is roughly equal.'} ({Mikhail Tal: 'On'} 12... exd5 {Mikhail Tal: 'White would have the favourable reply'} 13. d4 $5 {Mikhail Tal: '. The placing of the black pieces is far from ideal for play with an isolated d-pawn.' !}) 13. h4 {Mikhail Tal: 'I remember that several years ago Polugaevsky wrote about the fact that the Danish Grandmaster was far from indifferent to advancing his rooks' pawns. In the present position White does not succeed in exploiting the absence of the black bishop from g7, while the weaknesses on his kingside may with time become noticeable.' Berg,Emanuel: 'White is grabbing some space on the kingside but pushing the h-pawn also creates weaknesses in front of his own king.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Weiß gewinnt etwas Raum am Königsflügel, aber das Vorstoßen des h-Bauern schafft auch Schwächen vor seinem eigenen König.'} ({Mikhail Tal: 'A more complicated game results from'} 13. a3 $5 {Mikhail Tal: '. The move chosen by Larsen also should not have lost, although it is by no means the strongest.' !?}) ({White could play} 13. Nxd5 Qxd5 14. Qc3+ Kg8 (14... f6 15. Rfe1 e5 {= Larsen - Gheorghiu, Lugano, 1968}) 15. Rfe1 {=} ({but not} 15. Nd2 {?} Nd4 {!}) ({or} 15. Ne5 {in view of} Nd4 $1 {. !} 16. Bxd5 Nxe2+ 17. Kg2 Bxd5+ {'with the idea' 18... Nc3})) 13... Nd4 {Berg,Emanuel: 'A perfectly fine move but perhaps' Berg,Emanuel: 'Ein absolut ordentlicher Zug, aber vielleicht wäre'} (13... Re8 {Berg,Emanuel or oder}) (13... Rc8 {Berg,Emanuel would be even stronger in order to avoid simplifications. noch stärker gewesen, um Vereinfachungen zu vermeiden.}) 14. Re1 {Mikhail Tal: 'It would have been simpler to relieve the situation by the exchange of all the minor pieces.'} (14. Nxd4 $11 {!?} cxd4 {Berg,Emanuel} 15. Nxd5 Bxd5 16. Qf4 {'with the idea' Rfc1=} Bxg2 17. Kxg2 Qd5+ 18. Qf3 {was seen in 1-0 (69) Socko,B (2618)-Cramling,P (2459) Tornelo INT 2021 with a pretty balanced game. geschah in 1-0 (69) Socko,B (2618)-Cramling,P (2459) Tornelo INT 2021, mit einer ziemlich ausgeglichenen Partie.}) 14... h6 {Mikhail Tal: 'Although I hadn't realised it, this move sets a trap into which my opponent falls. The initial idea was simple - to guard the gS-square, and to emphasise the futility of White's play on the kingside. '} 15. Ne5 $2 {Mikhail Tal: 'With this move Larsen was intending to start a most interesting combination, but then he suddenly noticed that it could be very simply refuted.' Berg,Emanuel: '?!' Berg,Emanuel: 'An unfortunate move for white which black immediately takes advantage of.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Ein unglücklicher Zug für Weiß, den Schwarz sofort ausnutzt.'} ({Mikhail Tal: 'Of course, here also'} 15. Nxd4 $11 {Mikhail Tal: 'should have led to a quick draw.'} cxd4 16. Nxd5 Bxd5 17. Qf4 {'with the idea' Rec1=}) (15. Qd2 {=}) 15... Nxc3 $15 {Berg,Emanuel: '!'} 16. Qxc3 ({Mikhail Tal: 'At first White had planned'} 16. bxc3 $2 {?} Bxg2 {Berg,Emanuel: ''} 17. Ng4 (17. cxd4 Qxd4 $1 {simply leaves Black a pawn up !} 18. Nxf7 (18. Nxg6 fxg6 $19) 18... Rxf7 $19) (17. Kxg2 Qd5+ 18. Nf3 Nxf3 19. exf3 Qxd3 $19) 17... h5 $1 $17 {'-+' Tal} ({Mikhail Tal: ', preparing, in answer to'} 17... Nxe2+ $2 18. Rxe2 Bf3 19. Qxh6+ Kg8 {Mikhail Tal: ', the spectacular'} 20. h5 $1 {Mikhail Tal: '!!' '!!'} (20. Rxe6 {leads only to a draw}) 20... Bxe2 21. hxg6 fxg6 22. Qxg6+ Kh8 23. Qh6+ Kg8 24. Qxe6+ {obtaining two pawns for the exchange and with the black king in an exposed position. Alas, the whole variation does not work because of the reply 17 ...h5 when once again White remains a pawn down. Therefore he had to agree to the loss of two tempi, which naturally gives Black a certain advantage. ''}) (17... Bh3 {!?} 18. Qxh6+ Kg8 19. h5 Nf5 $19)) 16... Bxg2 17. Kxg2 Qd5+ 18. Nf3 Rad8 {Mikhail Tal: '!' '!' Mikhail Tal: 'On this occasion Black solves correctly that eternal problem of how best to place the rooks. The queen's rook stands on the d-file, preventing 19 e4 followed by the capture of the knight, since in this case the rook ending will be hopeless for White. As, in all probability, White will be sooner or later forced to exchange on d4, Black's king's rook will come into play along the then open e-file. ' Berg,Emanuel: 'Black has achieved a nice space advantage and also has chances to create counterplay towards white's king.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Schwarz hat sich einen schönen Raumvorteil verschafft und hat auch Chancen, Gegenspiel gegen den weißen König zu erzeugen.'} (18... e5 $2 19. e4 $11) 19. Kg1 e5 {Berg,Emanuel: '!' Berg,Emanuel: 'Preparing to capture with the e-pawn on d4.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Bereitet das Schlagen mit dem e-Bauern auf d4 vor.'} 20. Nxd4 {Berg,Emanuel: 'Naturally white likes to exchange off this strong knight. However it strenghtens black's centre and gives him a half open e-file for his rooks.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Natürlich tauscht Weiß diesen starken Springer gerne ab. Er stärkt jedoch das Zentrum von Schwarz und gibt ihm eine halboffene e-Linie für seine Türme.'} ({After} 20. Nd2 {the drawbacks to White's 13th move could have been exposed by} g5 {. '' !}) 20... exd4 21. Qc4 {Berg,Emanuel: 'White now looks for an inferior rook endgame but Tal has ambitions for more!' Berg,Emanuel: 'Weiß sucht nun nach einem schlechteren Turmendspiel, aber Tal hat Ambitionen auf mehr!'} (21. Qa3 $5 {!?} a5 22. Qb3 Qc6 23. e4 dxe3 24. Rxe3 $15) 21... Qh5 {Berg,Emanuel: '!?' Berg,Emanuel: 'Now white's kingside is very vulnerable and accurate defence is necessary not to perish.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Jetzt ist der weiße Königsflügel sehr verwundbar und eine genaue Verteidigung ist notwendig, um nicht unterzugehen.'} (21... Qxc4 {Berg,Emanuel} 22. dxc4 Rfe8 {intending ...g5 next gives black a promising endgame. mit der Absicht ...g5 als Nächstes gibt Schwarz ein vielversprechendes Endspiel.}) 22. Qa4 $2 {Mikhail Tal: 'White is over-optimistic. In my opinion, he had to advance his e-pawn in order to defend against the threatened attack. The capture of the a-pawn consumes too much time. ' Berg,Emanuel: '??' ?! Berg,Emanuel: 'There was no time start hunting pawns. Necessary was' Berg,Emanuel: 'Es war keine Zeit, mit der Jagd auf Bauern zu beginnen. Nötig war'} (22. b4 $2 cxb4 23. Qxb4 Rfe8 $17) (22. e4 $5 {Berg,Emanuel: '!' '' Berg,Emanuel: 'or' Berg,Emanuel: 'oder'}) 22... Rfe8 $1 {Berg,Emanuel: 'Tal completely abandons his queenside in order to setup a massive attack towards the white king.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Tal gibt seinen Damenflügel komplett auf, um einen massiven Angriff auf den weißen König zu starten.'} 23. Qxa7 Rd6 {Mikhail Tal: 'Not so much to defend the b-pawn as to attack the f-pawn.' '' ! Berg,Emanuel: 'Defending b6 while preparing the rook lift to f6.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Verteidigt b6 und bereitet gleichzeitig den Turmaufzug nach f6 vor.'} 24. b4 (24. f3 {%03'better is'} Rde6 25. Kf2 Qe5 {'with the idea' 26... Qe3, 27... Qd2$19} 26. Rad1 g5 $17 {!}) 24... Rf6 $1 $19 {Mikhail Tal: '!' '!' Berg,Emanuel: '!' Berg,Emanuel: 'Preparing ...f5 or ...xe2 with a continuous attack towards f2.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Vorbereitung von ...Df5 oder ...Txe2 mit einem kontinuierlichen Angriff auf f2.'} (24... cxb4 {was also good, but the position is already ripe for a forced variation. ''}) 25. bxc5 {?} ({More stubborn is Hartnäckiger ist} 25. Qc7 {Berg,Emanuel} Qf5 26. Qf4 Qh3 27. Qc7 Ree6 $3 {intending ...xf2! mit der Absicht ...Txf2!} 28. Rf1 Rxe2 29. bxc5 bxc5 30. Qxc5 Rf3 31. Qxd4+ Kh7 32. Qd6 Rexf2 33. Rxf2 Rxg3+ 34. Qxg3 Qxg3+ $19) {Mikhail Tal: 'as'} 25... Qf5 {Mikhail Tal: '!' '!' Mikhail Tal: 'This forces a serious weakening,'} 26. f3 (26. Rf1 {loses immediately to ?} Rxe2 {. '-+'}) 26... Qh3 {Berg,Emanuel: 'Now the backside of white's 13.h4 becomes clear.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Jetzt wird die Kehrseite des weißen 13.h4 deutlich.'} 27. Qc7 Rf5 {Mikhail Tal: '!' '!' Mikhail Tal: 'A quiet move with an irresistible threat. Once one of the black rooks reaches e5 the white king will be absolutely defenceless. ' Berg,Emanuel: '!!' !! 'with the idea' 28... Rfe5 Berg,Emanuel: 'Black aims to block the diagonal for white's queen while showing no fear of the running passed pawn.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Schwarz versucht, die Diagonale für die weiße Dame zu blockieren, während er keine Angst vor dem laufenden Freibauern zeigt.'} 28. cxb6 Rfe5 $1 {'-+' Berg,Emanuel: 'Now black primarily threatens the crucial ...xe2 with a mate attack while ...xg3+is another serious issue. There is no longer any way of escape for white.' Berg,Emanuel: 'Jetzt droht Schwarz vor allem das entscheidende ...Txe2 mit einem Mattangriff, während ...Dxg3+ ein weiteres ernstes Problem ist. Für Weiß gibt es keine Möglichkeit mehr zu entkommen.'} ({Mikhail Tal: 'This is simpler than'} 28... Ree5 29. g4 $1 Qg3+ 30. Kh1 (30. Kf1 Rxf3+) 30... Rh5 $1 {which also wins. '-+' ! Tal}) 29. e4 ({In planning his attack, Black considered the main variation to be the following:} 29. Qxe5+ Rxe5 30. g4 {, hoping with rook against queen to exploit the strength of the b-pawn. In this case I was planning} Qg3+ 31. Kh1 ({after} 31. Kf1 Qh2 $1 {White can undertake nothing, since on !} 32. b7 ({while in reply to} 32. a4 {the simplest solution is} Rxe2 33. Rxe2 Qh1+ 34. Kf2 Qxa1 {and both pawns will fall in the not too distant future '-+'}) {, there follows} 32... Rb5 {and he cannot playa rook to b1}) 31... h5 $1 {!} 32. b7 Rb5 33. Reb1 hxg4 $1 {!} 34. Rxb5 Qh3+ 35. Kg1 g3 {. '-+' Tal}) 29... Qxg3+ 30. Kh1 Qxh4+ {Mikhail Tal: 'Here there are already many ways to win.'} 31. Kg2 Rg5+ 32. Kf1 Qh3+ 33. Ke2 Rg2+ 34. Kd1 Qxf3+ 35. Kc1 Qf2 {Berg,Emanuel: 'A well played game by Tal with a very accurate tactical finish in the last part of the game!' Berg,Emanuel: 'Eine gut gespielte Partie von Tal mit einem sehr präzisen taktischen Abschluss im letzten Teil der Partie!'} 0-1

