{Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'B40: Sicilian: 2...e6, Unusual lines '} 1. e4 {Fritz 5.00 (5s) ChessBase II ChessBase II Komodo 9 64-bit (20s) ChessBase II: 'Keres,Paul; Nei,I' ChessBase II: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s) Keres,Paul; Nei,I Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'ChessBase II''} c5 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): 'Opening = B40_02 Sizilianische Vert 3.b3 / Sicilian Defence 3.b3'} 2. Nf3 e6 3. b3 {'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'ChessBase II: 'Mikhail Tal: 'The Finnish master adopts this move fairly often; indeed, two years ago here in Tallinn, he defeated L. Stein in this variation. Looking through some chess magazines literally half an hour before the start of the game, I came across the game Westerinen-Kaplan, Skopje 1972, which White had lost in 20 moves, and without checking any further I decided to follow the Puerto-Rican. ''''} Nf6 4. e5 Nd5 5. Bb2 Be7 6. c4 Nc7 ({ChessBase II: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'Mikhail Tal: 'Of course, the normal continuation is'''} 6... Nb4 $1 {ChessBase II: 'Keres,Paul; Nei,I: '!'' ChessBase II: 'Keres,Paul; Nei,I: '!' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): '(ChessBase II) Mikhail Tal: ', but after all, Kaplan had won quickly ...'''} 7. Nc3 {ChessBase II} f5 {½-½ Westerinen,H (2465)-Hartston,W (2480) Nice ol (Men) fin-A 1974 (3)}) 7. Nc3 f6 8. Ne4 fxe5 9. Nxe5 O-O {'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'ChessBase II: 'Mikhail Tal: 'At Skopje in this position Westerinen continued 10 Qg4?, and after 10...Ne8 Black quickly seized the initiative, as within two moves (11...d6 and 12...e5) the activity of the bishop on b2 was curtailed. Of course, it was extremely naive to expect that the Finnish master would repeat the game to the end. ''''} 10. d4 $1 {ChessBase II: 'N' 'N' 'N' ChessBase II: 'Keres,Paul; Nei,I: '!'''Keres,Paul; Nei,I: '!' Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'ChessBase II: 'N' ChessBase II: 'Mikhail Tal: 'It turns out that White has a certain advantage on his side.'''' 'N'} (10. Qg4 {ChessBase II: '' '' '' ChessBase II: 'Komodo 9 64-bit (20s): 'ChessBase II'' ''} Ne8 { d6, e5 ChessBase II: 'Ker