1. e4 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} Nc6 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): 'Opening = C79 - Spanisch-Russische Variante /Ruy Lopez-Russian Variation'} 2. Nf3 {Tal:"The young East German Champion plays very actively, and in games with him there is no necessity to avoid the main theoretical continuations." Tal:"The young East German Champion plays very actively, and in games with him there is no necessity to avoid the main theoretical continuations." Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'The young East German Champion plays very actively, and in games with him there is no necessity to avoid the main theoretical continuations. ''} e5 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 d6 5. O-O (5. Bxc6+ $5) 5... Bd7 6. d4 Nf6 7. Bxc6 $5 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Strange, but it would appear that this has not been played before in this position. Several times I have made the exchange after a different order of moves: 6 Re1, 7 Bxc6 and 8 d4, but in the tournament at Lublin (1974) the Polish master Pytel answered 7 Bxc6 with 7...bxc6 and got a reasonable game. Here, however, Black is practically forced into a not especially favourable variation of the Steinitz Defence. ''} (7. dxe5 Nxe5 8. Bxd7+ Nfxd7 (8... Qxd7 9. Nc3 Be7 10. Nxe5 dxe5 11. Qxd7+ Nxd7 12. Nd5 $14) 9. Nc3 Be7 10. Nd4 O-O $11) (7. Re1 Be7 8. Bxc6 bxc6 $1) 7... Bxc6 (7... bxc6 8. Re1 exd4 9. e5 dxe5 10. Nxe5 Be6 11. Nxc6 Qd5 12. Qf3 Qxf3 13. gxf3 Bc5 14. b4 $1 Bb6 15. Bb2 $16) 8. Re1 Be7 ({Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Clearly, on''} 8... Nxe4 $2 {Tal,Mihail: '??' '??' Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'there would follow''} 9. d5 $18) ({Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'while on''} 8... Bxe4 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'comes''} 9. Nc3 $36 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'when White has the initiative;''} ({or} 9. dxe5 dxe5 10. Nbd2 {, as in Tal-Kogan, Latvia-'Avantgarde' match 1974.})) 9. Nc3 exd4 ({Tal,Mihail: 'Black is practically forced to surrender the centre, since it has been known for about 80 years now that after'} 9... O-O $2 10. dxe5 dxe5 11. Qxd8 Raxd8 12. Nxe5 Bxe4 13. Nxe4 Nxe4 14. Nd3 f5 15. f3 Bc5+ 16. Nxc5 Nxc5 17. Bg5 {Tal,Mihail: 'Black loses material.'} Rde8 18. Be7 $18) 10. Nxd4 Bd7 11. Qf3 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'It cannot be said that White is playing originally, but this does not make Black's position any more attractive. All the more since the black pieces are being handled by a player who cannot bear passive defence. Here, instead of the usual 11...0-0 12 Bf4 Re8 with a position which is difficult to breach, Knaak chooses a pseudo-active continuation, which leads to practically insurmountable difficulties. ''} Bg4 $2 {Tal,Mihail: '?!' '?!' Tal,Mihail: '?!' '?!' Tal,Mihail: '?!' '?!' Tal:"A pseudo - active continuation."} (11... O-O {Tal,Mihail: '!?' '!?'} 12. Bf4 {Tal,Mihail: '' ''} (12. Nf5) 12... Re8) 12. Qg3 Qd7 13. h3 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'The simplest.'' Fritz 5.00 (5s): 'last book move'} Bh5 ({Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'After''} 13... Be6 $5 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: '. Instead he plays''} 14. e5 $1 {Tal,Mihail: '!?' '!?' Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: '!''} ({Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: ', White is not forced to go in for the doubleedged''} 14. f4 O-O-O 15. f5 Bc4 $13 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'etc.''}) (14. Z0) 14... dxe5 15. Nxe6 fxe6 (15... Qxe6 16. Rxe5) 16. Qxe5 $16 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'and soon wins a pawn. Even so, this line was probably the lesser evil for Black.''}) 14. Nf5 (14. Qxg7 $2 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} Rg8 15. Nf5 Rxg7 16. Nxg7+ Kf8 17. Nxh5 Nxh5 18. Bh6+ Ng7 $19) 14... O-O-O {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'The black king soon finds out that on the queens ide, life is also not a bed of roses.''} {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Thus''} 15. Bg5 $18 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Black's position is probably already lost.'' Fritz 5.00 (5s): ''} (15. Qe3 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} Rhg8 $16) 15... Ng8 $5 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): ''} (15... Bg6 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'fails to''} 16. Nxe7+ Qxe7 17. Nd5 Qe6 18. Bxf6 gxf6 19. Qc3 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'and 20 Nxf6. Knaak finds a clever, but nevertheless insufficient, defence.''} c6 20. Nxf6) (15... h6 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} 16. Nxe7+ Qxe7 17. Nd5 $16) 16. Bxe7 $1 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): ''} ({Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'I could also have contented myself with''} 16. Nxe7+ $5 Nxe7 17. Qh4 f6 18. Qxh5 $16 {Tal,Mihail: '+-' '+-'} ({Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'or''} 18. Bxf6 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: ', but I did not want to open in the first case the f-file, and in the second the g-file. I therefore decided to win a pawn in a different way, while setting my opponent a trap. Knaak falls into it.'' Fritz 5.00 (5s)} gxf6 19. Qxh5 Rdg8 $16)) 16... Nxe7 17. Qg5 Nxf5 $2 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Capitulation.''} ({Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Relatively better was the pawn sacrifice''} 17... Nc6 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: '!''} 18. Qxh5 g6 19. Nxd6+ Qxd6 20. Qg4+ Kb8 21. a3 $18 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: ', although even here the path to victory is accompanied by only technical difficulties.''}) 18. exf5 (18. Qxf5 $6 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} Bg6 19. Qf3 Rhe8 $11) 18... g6 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'The attempt to complicate the game does not work:''} 19. g4 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Straightforward and simple.''} Qc6 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Now 20 gxh5 gxf5 leads to great and unnecessary complications, but White has no reason to hurry.''} (19... gxf5 20. Qxh5 fxg4 21. hxg4 Rhg8 (21... Rdg8 22. Kf1 Rxg4 23. Re7 $18) 22. Kf1 (22. Kh1 Rxg4 23. Re7 {.}) 22... Rxg4 23. Re7 $18) 20. f6 {c3-d5 c3-d5 Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'With the threat of 21 Nd5.''} d5 21. Re7 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): ''} (21. gxh5 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} d4 22. Qg4+ Kb8 $16) 21... h6 {Fritz 5.00 (5s): '+-'} (21... Rhg8 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} 22. Qf4 $16 (22. gxh5 $4 gxh5 23. h4 Qxf6 $19)) 22. Qe5 d4 $5 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: '!?' Mikhail Tal: 'A cunning trap 'just before the curtain'.''} 23. Ne2 {Tal,Mihail: '!' '!'} ({Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'The natural''} 23. Ne4 $2 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'would allow Black to confuse matters by''} Rd5 24. Rxc7+ Kb8 $1 $44 {Tal,Mihail: '!' '!' Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: '!!' Mikhail Tal: '.''}) (23. gxh5 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} dxc3 24. bxc3 gxh5 25. Rxf7 Rhf8 $15) 23... Rd5 {Tal,Mihail: 'Mikhail Tal: 'Equally unacceptable for Black are''} 24. Nxd4 $1 {Tal,Mihail: 'and'} Rxe5 (24... Qc5 25. Rxc7+ Qxc7 26. Qxd5 {Tal,Mihail: '.'} Bxg4 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} 27. hxg4 $18) (24... Qc4 {Fritz 5.00 (5s)} 25. Rxc7+) 25. Nxc6 1-0

