g2 Rf7 33. Be6 Rfb7 34. Ra2 e4 35. Bf5 e3 36. Kf3 Bb6 37. Ra4 Rc7 38. h4 Re8 39. g5 hxg5 40. hxg5 Rc5 41. g4 Rxd5 42. Rxc4 Rc5 43. Rd4 Rc6 44. Rf4 Rh8 45. Bd3 Rh1 46. Rf5 a4 47. Rb5 Rf1+ 48. Kg2 Rd1 {1-0 Seeger,C-Burgemeister,W/corr GER 1991/}) 11. Ne1 (11. Nh2 Nh5 12. Nc4 Qe8 13. g4 Nf4 14. Bxf4 exf4 15. Qd2 g5 16. Nf3 b5 17. Na5 Ng6 18. Nd4 Bxd4 19. Qxd4 Ne5 20. f3 Qe7 21. Rad1 h5 22. c4 hxg4 23. hxg4 bxc4 24. Nxc4 Bb5 25. Rf2 Bxc4 26. Bxc4 Kg7 27. Kf1 Rh8 28. Ke2 Qf6 29. Bb3 Rh3 30. Qc3 Nxg4 31. Qxf6+ Nxf6 32. Rc1 g4 33. fxg4 Re3+ 34. Kf1 f3 35. Re1 Rh8 {0-1 Kotan,L-Klemanic,E/Bratislava SVK 1986/}) 11... c6 12. dxc6 Bxc6 13. Qe2 d5 14. exd5 Nfxd5 15. Ndf3 Qc7 16. Nc2 Rae8 17. Bd2 Nf5 18. Rfe1 a5 19. Na3 e4 20. Nd4 Nxd4 21. cxd4 Bxd4 22. Bxd5 Bxd5 23. Nb5 Qb6 24. Nxd4 Qxd4 25. Bh6 Bc6 26. Rad1 Qe5 27. Bxf8 Rxf8 28. Qd2 a4 29. Qd4 Qxd4 30. Rxd4 Ra8 31. Re3 Ra5 32. f3 exf3 33. gxf3 Rf5 34. Kf2 Kg7 35. f4 Rc5 36. Rc3 Rb5 37. b4 axb3 38. axb3 Ra5 39. Rd2 Ra1 40. Ke3 Re1+ 41. Re2 Rd1 42. Rf2 Kf6 43. Rd3 Rh1 44. Kd4 Bd7 45. Kc5 Bxh3 46. Kb6 Bf5 47. Rd6+ Be6 48. b4 Rb1 49. Rd4 h5 50. Kxb7 Kf5 51. Kc6 Rc1+ 52. Kd6 Rb1 53. Kc6 Rc1+ 54. Kb6 Rc8 55. b5 Rc4 56. Rxc4 Bxc4 57. Kc5 Bxb5 58. Kxb5 Kg4 59. Kc4 Kg3 60. Rf1 Kg2 61. Ra1 h4 62. Ra7 h3 63. Rxf7 h2 {½-½ Broberg,H-Buchal,S/BL2 GER 1994/}) 10. c4 {After a solid start, White has displayed certain territorial ambitions. But this involves a considerable loss of time, including c2-c3-c4 and the long bishop manoeuvre, which still has not come to an end. What is even more significant is that his queen's knight stands on d2, blocking his other bishop's development. Developing the bishop to b2 is not very effective, as it would hit into a defended pawn, so White still has to work a bit to bring his position in order. On the other hand, the centre is blocked and he has more space, elements he must have counted on.} (10. Re1 {Myers Gallagher Tal} a5 11. h3 Bd7 12. Bc2 Na6 13. Nc4 Nc5 14. b4 axb4 15. cxb4 Na4 16. Bd2 $14 {Myers}) 10... Na6 (10... c5 $5 {(Myers Gallagher Tal) Tal}) (10... a5 $5 {(Myers Gallagher Tal) Tal}) (10... Nh5 $5 {(Myers Gallagher Tal) Gallagher}) 11. Bc2 c6 {Myers Gallagher Tal: '!?'} (11... Nb4 $5 {Myers Gallagher Tal}) 12. a3 (12. h3 $5 {(Myers Gallagher Tal) Gallagher}) 12... cxd5 13. cxd5 Rc8 {The first critical moment. Black has developed harmoniously while White is still struggling to complete his development.} 14. h3 {The most natural decision. Myers Gallagher Tal: '!'} ({The attempt to achieve optimal coordination with} 14. Nb1 {followed by Nc3 and Be3 allows} Bxf3 {Due to the hanging bishop, White has to weaken his kingside structure with} 15. gxf3 {, when after} Nh5 {Black has excellent play on the dark squares.}) (14. b4 $6 {Myers Gallagher Tal} Nxd5 $1 15. exd5 e4 16. Nxe4 Bxa1 17. Bg5 f6 18. Bh6 Be5 $5 (18... Rf7 {Tal} 19. Qxa1 Bxf3 20. gxf3 Rxc2 21. Bf4 Kg7 22. Rd1 $11) 19. Bxf8 Qxf8 20. Ned2 Rc3 21. Bb3 Qh6 22. h3 Bxf3 23. Nxf3 Nc7 24. Re1 Qf4 $15 {Myers}) 14... Bh5 $3 {The result of an accurate judgement of the position, this is the only move to keep White under pressure. The text move involves a piece sacrifice which White would have better declined. Myers Gallagher Tal: '!?'} (14... Bxf3 {not only gives up the bishops' pair but also frees White's play after} 15. Nxf3 {followed by Be3.}) (14... Bd7 {allows the optimal regrouping with} 15. Nb1 $1 {followed by Nc3 and Be3.} (15. b4 $5 {Myers Gallagher Tal} Bb5 (15... Nxd5 $2 16. exd5 e4 17. Nxe4 Bxa1 18. Bg5 f6 19. Bh6 Be5 $11 {According to Tal.} 20. Nxe5 $1 dxe5 21. d6 Nb8 22. f4 $1 $18 {Myers}) 16. Re1 Qd7 17. Nf1 Rc7 18. Ng3 Rfc8 19. Bb3 b6 20. Bd2 Nb8 21. a4 Bd3 22. Rc1 $14 {Myers})) 15. g4 $2 {Weakening the kingside with incomplete development can hardly be a good idea. Myers Gallagher Tal: '?!'} ({White should have kept manoeuvring with, say,} 15. Re1 {Myers Gallagher Tal: '!?'} Qd7 16. Bd3 Nc5 17. Bf1 Bh6 {Even though Black's position is very active, we can notice that ... Bh5 also had a minor drawback: Black does not have ...Nh5 followed by ...f7-f5 anymore.}) 15... Nxg4 $1 16. hxg4 Bxg4 17. Bd3 {In view of the threat ...f7-f5 the bishop hurries to unpin the knight on f3.} (17. b4 {Myers Gallagher Tal} f5 $1 18. Rb1 Qd7 19. Rb3 fxe4 20. Bxe4 Bh6 21. Bb2 Bh5 22. Nxe5 dxe5 23. f3 Rfd8 $17 {[%cal Yh6f4,Gb7b5] Myers}) 17... Bh6 $6 {This unnecessarily offers White some free tempi for developing.} ({Everything was ready for the resolute} 17... f5 $1 {, with a very dangerous attack.} 18. Be2 Nc5 19. Ne1 Bh3 20. Ng2 Bxg2 21. Kxg2 fxe4 22. Bg4 Rf4 23. Nb3 ({In view of the threat ...Qg5 there is hardly anything better. If} 23. Nb1 Qg5 24. Bxf4 exf4 $19 {, with a crushing attack.}) 23... Rxg4+ 24. Qxg4 Nxb3 $17 {With two pawns for the exchange, the better structure and active play.}) (17... Nc5 $5 {Myers Gallagher Tal}) 18. Nc4 (18. Be2 $6 {Myers Gallagher Tal} f5 $1 {Tal} 19. Ne1 Bf4 20. Ng2 Bh3 21. Nxf4 exf4 22. Kh1 fxe4 $19 {Myers}) (18. Re1 $6 {Myers Gallagher Tal} f5 $1 19. exf5 Nc5 20. Be2 Bxf5 21. Nc4 Bxc1 22. Rxc1 e4 $19 {Myers}) 18... Bxc1 19. Rxc1 Nc5 20. Be2 {Relatively best. Myers Gallagher Tal: ''} (20. b4 {runs into Myers Gallagher Tal: '?'} Nb3 $1 21. Rc3 {Trying to keep the c4-knight defended. Myers Gallagher Tal: 'Tal'} (21. Qxb3 $6 Bxf3 {mates soon.}) 21... Nd4 {Myers Gallagher Tal: '!'} 22. Be2 Bxf3 23. Bxf3 b5 $19 {Black retrieves the piece, retaining a few extra pawns and a strategic advantage.}) (20. Rc3 {does not work either, as after Myers Gallagher Tal: '?'} f5 {he has to either give up the e4-pawn as in the game or return the piece with Myers Gallagher Tal: '!'} 21. exf5 (21. Be2 {Myers Gallagher Tal} Nxe4 22. Rc2 f4 23. Re1 Ng5 $19 {Myers}) 21... e4 $17) (20. Bc2 $2 {Myers Gallagher Tal} f5 $1 {Tal} 21. Ne3 fxe4 22. Bxe4 Rf4 23. Nxg4 Rxg4+ $19) 20... Nxe4 $15 {Black has three pawns for the piece and attacking chances.} 21. Re1 $6 {Weakening the pawn on f2 and keeping the knight on f3 under pressure. Myers Gallagher Tal: '?'} (21. Nfd2 $5 Bxe2 22. Qxe2 Qg5+ 23. Kh1 Qh4+ 24. Kg2 Nf6 $15) (21. Ne3 $5 Bh5 (21... Bh3 {Myers Gallagher Tal} 22. Re1 f5 {Tal} 23. Qa4 a6 24. Qb4 Qe7 25. Nc4 Rc5 $36 {Myers}) 22. Rxc8 Qxc8 23. Nd2 Bxe2 24. Qxe2 Ng5 $15) (21. Nfxe5 $2 {Myers Gallagher Tal} Bh3 {Tal} 22. Nf3 Bxf1 23. Bxf1 Qf6 24. Rb1 Rfe8 25. Ne3 Qf4 $17 {Myers}) 21... Bxf3 $5 {The introduction to another combination.} (21... f5 {was also strong.}) 22. Bxf3 Nxf2 $1 23. Kxf2 Qh4+ 24. Kg2 Rxc4 25. Rxc4 Qxc4 {With four pawns for a relatively passive bishop, Black has excellent winning chances already.} 26. Re4 Qc7 27. Qa4 {Myers Gallagher Tal: '!'} f5 {Myers Gallagher Tal: '!'} 28. Rc4 Qe7 (28... Qb6 $5 {Myers Gallagher Tal} 29. Kf1 e4 30. Be2 Qxb2 31. Qd7 Qf6 32. Rc7 Rf7 33. Qc8+ Kg7 34. Qxb7 Rxc7 35. Qxc7+ Kh6 $19 {Myers}) 29. Qxa7 e4 30. Bd1 f4 {Myers Gallagher Tal: '!'} (30... e3 {Myers Gallagher Tal} 31. Kf3 Re8 32. Be2 Qg5 33. Qa4 b5 34. Qxb5 Kf8 35. Qd7 $2 Qh5+ $19 {Myers}) 31. Bg4 Qg5 {Myers Gallagher Tal: '!?'} 32. Kh3 Qh6+ {Myers Gallagher Tal: '?!'} (32... f3 $3 $19 {Myers Gallagher Tal Myers Gallagher Tal: '!!' Myers Gallagher Tal: 'Myers: Overlooked by Tal and Gallagher.'} 33. Qf2 {Myers Gallagher Tal} e3 34. Qg1 e2 35. Qf2 Re8 36. Be6+ Rxe6 37. dxe6 Qf5+ 38. Kh4 Qe5 39. Kg4 e1=Q 40. Rc8+ Kg7 41. Rc7+ Kh6 42. Qxe1 Qxe1 $19 {Myers}) 33. Kg2 f3+ 34. Kf1 Qg5 (34... Qd2 $5 {Myers Gallagher Tal} 35. Be6+ Kg7) 35. Be6+ (35. Qg1 $2 {Myers Gallagher Tal} Qd2 36. Be6+ Kg7 37. Qd4+ Qxd4 38. Rxd4 Rf4 $1 (38... e3 $2 {Myers Gallagher Tal} 39. Re4 (39. Rb4 $2 g5 40. Rxb7+ Kg6 $19 {Myers}) 39... e2+ 40. Kf2 h5 41. Bd7 $1 $132 {Gallagher}) 39. Rb4 Kf6 40. Kf2 Ke5 $19 {Myers Myers Gallagher Tal: '-+!'}) 35... Kg7 36. Qg1 Qh4 37. Qg4 {Myers Gallagher Tal: '?'} (37. Qf2 $6 {Myers Gallagher Tal} Qh1+ 38. Qg1 Qxg1+ {Myers Gallagher Tal: '!?'} 39. Kxg1 e3 40. Re4 (40. Rc7+ {Myers Gallagher Tal} Kh6 41. Bh3 Kg5 42. Rxh7 Kf4 $19 {Myers}) 40... f2+ 41. Kf1 Rf3 $19 {Gallagher}) (37. Rc7+ $5 {Myers Gallagher Tal} Kh6 38. Rc2 Qf4 39. b3 g5 40. Rc7 Qh4 41. Rd7 Kg6 42. Bg4 Rf6 $19 {Myers}) 37... Qh2 {Myers Gallagher Tal: '!'} 38. Rxe4 f2 0-1

