 Bxg3 $1 {is crushing.}) ({. If White tries} 19. h3 {, Black switches to the queenside with} Bb4 $1 {, winning material.} 20. Rxe5 Nxe5 21. Qxe5 Qxe5 22. Nxe5 Bxd2 23. Rd1 Bc3 $19)) 19. Nxf3 Bc7 {'' !} (19... Nxf3+ 20. gxf3 Qb7 (20... Bb4 {?} 21. Rxe7 Bxa5 22. Rxa7 $16) 21. Qf5 $13) 20. Qd2 Nxf3+ 21. gxf3 Qd6 $17 22. f4 Nd5 23. Rxe8+ Rxe8 24. Re1 Re6 {, White has a very difficult position.}) 18... Bxe5 {ChessBase: 'Colin Crouch: 'Black is attacking, using the bishop pair as potential sacrificial forces, and White does not even have an extra pawn to offer any sort of counter-chances.''} 19. Nc4 {ChessBase: 'Colin Crouch: '?' '?' '?' '?' Colin Crouch: 'A continuation of Spassky's Qa5 plan, but it indicates that his sense of danger had really gone awry. Here Tal is lining up for a kingside attack and Spassky responds by moving his pieces over to the queenside. Not the recipe for a successful defence. Having said that, White is in serious trouble here, and may already be losing.'' '' ?! Colin Crouch: 'A continuation of Spassky's Qa5 plan, but it indicates that his sense of danger had really gone awry. Here Tal is lining up for a kingside attack and Spassky responds by moving his pieces over to the queenside. Not the recipe for a successful defence. Having said that, White is in serious trouble here, and may already be losing. Garry Kasparov: 'This leads to a rapid loss, but it is hard to offer White any good advice.'' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Dragging the last piece capable of helping the king away must have been painful decision for the defender. More resilient 19.Nf1 was at least asking black to realize, that Nh5 is stronger than centralizing Nd5.' Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Die letzte Figur, die dem König helfen kann, wegzuziehen, muss eine schmerzhafte Entscheidung für den Verteidiger gewesen sein. Das widerstandsfähigere 19.Sf1 sollte Schwarz zumindest zu der Einsicht bringen, dass Sh5 stärker ist als das zentralisierte Sd5.'} (19. Nf1 $5 {ChessBase} Nd5 (19... Nh5 $1 20. f3 Nf4