1. e4 {Flohr,S} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. dxe5 Be6 9. Nbd2 Nc5 10. c3 d4 11. Bxe6 {Flohr,S: 'N'} Nxe6 12. Nb3 {This attempt to avoid main lines doesn't promise any opening advantage. This attempt to avoid main lines doesn't promise any opening advantage.} (12. cxd4 {Flohr,S: '=' is the main line. is the main line.}) 12... dxc3 13. Qc2 (13. Qe2 {½-½ Tseshkovsky,V-Pudovkin,D/Krasnodar 1997/EXT 2000 (45) ½-½ Tseshkovsky,V-Pudovkin,D/Krasnodar 1997/EXT 2000 (45)}) 13... Qd5 $5 {[%cal Gd5c6] Flohr,S: '!'} ({Not bad also immediate Not bad also immediate} 13... Nb4 {½-½ Mednis,E-Tarjan,J/Pasadena 1978/MCD (20). (20) ½-½ Mednis,E-Tarjan,J/Pasadena 1978/MCD (20). (20)}) (13... Be7 $2 {Flohr,S} 14. Rd1 $16) 14. Rd1 $2 {Tactical blunder. White has missed an important intermediate move and since now on has to look for escape, but it turns out to be too late. Tactical blunder. White has missed an important intermediate move and since now on has to look for escape, but it turns out to be too late.} ({Also after Also after} 14. Qxc3 Bb4 {Flohr,S: ''} 15. Qe3 Rd8 {Black is fine Black is fine}) 14... Nb4 $1 {[%csl Rc2,Rd1] Flohr,S: '!'} 15. Qe2 $8 (15. Rxd5 $2 {loses on the spot. loses on the spot.} Nxc2 16. Rb1 Nb4 $1 17. Rd1 $140 $4 c2) 15... Qc4 $1 {As usually Tal plays with a lot of energy. As usually Tal plays with a lot of energy.} 16. Qxc4 $1 { } ({After After} 16. Nbd4 Qxe2 17. Nxe2 Nc2 18. Rb1 Na3 19. Ra1 cxb2 20. Bxb2 Nc4 $17 {Black's a pawn up for nothing. Black's a pawn up for nothing.}) 16... bxc4 17. Na5 $8 {Only move again. Only move again.} (17. bxc3 {is bad in view of is bad in view of} Nc2 $1 18. Rb1 cxb3 19. axb3 Ba3 $1 $19) 17... Nc2 18. Rb1 Na3 (18... Rb8 {18...a3 19 a1 c2 20. b1 b8}) 19. Ra1 $8 (19. bxa3 $4 c2 {[%csl Rb1,Rd1]}) 19... Nc2 20. Rb1 Rb8 $1 {[%csl Rb2][%cal Gc2a3] Pinning the b-pawn Black converts the game into a better endgame. 18...a3 19 a1 c2 20. b1 b8 Pinning the b-pawn Black converts the game into a better endgame. 18...a3 19 a1 c2 20. b1 b8} 21. Nxc4 $8 Na3 22. Nxa3 Bxa3 {[%cal Gc3c2,Gc3b2]} 23. Ne1 $8 cxb2 24. Nc2 $1 { } bxc1=Q 25. Rxb8+ Ke7 26. Rxc1 Rxb8 27. Nxa3 Rb2 $1 28. Rc2 Rxc2 29. Nxc2 $15 {It's interesting that after 14.d1? all the moves were forced and a better for Black knight endgame has arised on the move 29(!) which later was converted into a win. It's interesting that after 14.d1? all the moves were forced and a better for Black knight endgame has arised on the move 29(!) which later was converted into a win.} Kd7 {Flohr,S: ''} (29... c5 $5) 30. g3 c5 31. f4 Nd4 32. Ne3 Ke6 33. Kf2 Nf5 34. Nd1 Kd5 35. g4 Nh6 36. Kf3 Kd4 37. Ne3 g6 38. g5 Ng8 (38... Nf5 $2 {Flohr,S} 39. Nxf5+ gxf5 40. h4 { h5+-}) 39. Ng4 c4 40. Ke2 c3 41. Kd1 Ne7 42. Nf6 Nf5 43. Kc1 a5 44. Nd7 (44. Nxh7 {Flohr,S} Kd3 { d4}) 44... Ne3 45. Nb8 Kd3 46. Nc6 a4 47. Nd8 Nd5 48. e6 fxe6 (48... Nxf4 {(Flohr,S)  e2, c2}) 49. Nxe6 a3 50. Nc5+ Kc4 51. Ne4 Nb4 52. Kb1 Kd4 0-1

