ity.'} 17. Qg6+ Kh8 18. Qh6+ {.}) 14... Nbd5 ({Garry Kasparov: 'But not'} 14... Nfd5 $2 15. Qd3 $16 {Garry Kasparov: ';'}) ({Raetsky/Chetverik: 'White has strong pressure following' Raetsky/Chetverik: 'White has strong pressure following' Garry Kasparov: 'and not'} 14... Bd7 {Garry Kasparov: '?!'} 15. Qd3 { h5  Nh5 Garry Kasparov: 'with the threat of Nh5.'} Rc8 16. Ne4 Nbd5 17. Be5 {.}) 15. Be5 {Garry Kasparov: 'Now if'} Qb6 $5 {GM Mihail Marin: 'White is better developed and has two active bishops, but it is not easy to launch an attack due to Black's stable blockade on d5. Tal's solution is absolutely fantastic:'} 16. Qd3 $1 {GM Mihail Marin: '!!' GM Mihail Marin: 'Threatening Nh5 and practically forcing the next move. But how many would think of inviting such a double attack, eliminating the c2-bishop with gain of time?' Garry Kasparov: '!?' Garry Kasparov: 'Nevertheless;' Garry Kasparov: ', Flesch has in mind'} ({White could also try to sacrifice a pawn with Raetsky/Chetverik: 'White could also try to sacrifice a pawn with' Garry Kasparov: 'or'} 16. Bb3 $5 {Garry Kasparov: '.'} Bd7 17. Nh5 Nxh5 18. Qxh5 f6 19. Bg3 Qxd4 20. Rad1 {, with good compensation. Raetsky/Chetverik: ', with good compensation.'}) (16. Nh5 {is not dangerous:} Nxh5 17. Qxh5 Bd7 18. Qg4 (18. Rfe1 Rac8) 18... f6 19. Qg6 fxe5 20. Qh7+ Kf7 21. Bg6+ Kf6 {Tal}) ({although there was also the quieter} 16. Qd2) 16... Nb4 $6 {GM Mihail Marin: 'The most principled.' Garry Kasparov: 'The critical reply.'} ({Garry Kasparov: 'Otherwise White could have developed a dangerous initiative without interference:'} 16... Rd8 {GM Mihail Marin: '!?'} 17. Ne4 $14 {Garry Kasparov: '!'} Nd7 $14) ({Garry Kasparov: 'or'} 16... Bd7 $5 {Raetsky/Chetverik: 'would be met by'} 17. Bxf6 (17. Nh5 $2 Bb5 $1) 17... Nxf6 18. Nh5 {Raetsky/Chetverik: '!' '!'} Rfd8 $1 (18... Rfc8 19. Nxf6+ gxf6 20. Qh7+ Kf8 21. Bb3 $1 {and Black is in trouble Raetsky/Chetverik: 'and Black is in trouble'}) 19. Nxf6+ gxf6 20. Qh7+ Kf8 $13 {GM Miha