1. c4 {Ftacnik Ftacnik Ftacnik,L Gurevich,Mikhail} e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 c5 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. g3 Nf6 7. Bg2 Be7 8. O-O O-O 9. Bg5 cxd4 10. Nxd4 h6 11. Be3 {Raetsky/Chetverik: 'The main line Tarrasch.'} Re8 12. Rc1 Bf8 13. Qa4 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '!?'} Ne5 (13... Bd7 14. Nxd5 Nxd5 15. Bxd5 Na5 (15... Nb4 {Gurevich,Mikhail} 16. Qb3 $14) 16. Nb5 { f4 Gurevich,Mikhail: '!'}) 14. Rcd1 {N Gurevich,Mikhail: 'N'} (14. Qb3 {Gurevich,Mikhail: 'Ü 18/(537)'} Nc4 $6 15. Bf4 { c7; Rajkovic-Abramovic/Jugoslavija/1974/}) (14. Bf4 $5 {Gurevich,Mikhail} Ng6 15. e3 Nxf4 16. exf4) 14... Bd7 (14... Nc4 15. Bc1 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '!?'} (15. Nxd5 {Gurevich,Mikhail} Nxb2 16. Nxf6+ gxf6 $15) 15... Bd7 16. Qb3 Nb6 $13 (16... Na5 {Gurevich,Mikhail} 17. Qc2 Rc8 18. Qd3 $14) 17. a4 $5 $14 {Gurevich,Mikhail}) 15. Qb3 Bc6 16. Nxc6 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '!?'} bxc6 17. Bd4 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '' Gurevich,Mikhail: '[ e4]'} Rb8 18. Qc2 (18. Qa4 $14 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '!?'}) 18... Qa5 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '!?'} (18... c5 $6 19. Bxe5 Rxe5 20. Nxd5 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '!'} Nxd5 21. Qd3 Rxb2 22. Bxd5 Qf6 23. e3 $14) 19. Qf5 $5 (19. e4 dxe4 20. Nxe4 Nxe4 21. Bxe4 Qxa2 $13 22. Rfe1 {Gurevich,Mikhail} g6 $13) 19... Rxb2 $2 {Raetsky/Chetverik: '!?' Raetsky/Chetverik: 'A clever try to seize the initiative. White, however, has an effective reply.'} (19... Ned7 20. e4 g6 21. Qf4 Nh5 22. Qg4 (22. Qh4 $2 c5 $1 {Gurevich,Mikhail: ''}) 22... Ndf6 23. Qh4 Nxe4 24. Nxe4 dxe4 25. Bxe4 Qxa2 26. Bxc6 $14) 20. Nxd5 $1 ({Raetsky/Chetverik: 'On'} 20. Bxe5 {Raetsky/Chetverik: 'Black has the strong' Gurevich,Mikhail: '?'} d4 $1 {Raetsky/Chetverik: '. White's queen is unprotected on f5 and Black wins back the piece with an active position. White's move in the game is far stronger and gives him the better chances.' Gurevich,Mikhail: '' Gurevich,Mikhail: 'Raetsky/Chetverik: '!' Raetsky/Chetverik: '. White's queen is unprotected on f5 and Black wins back the piece with an active position. White's move in the game is far stronger and gives him the better chances.''}) 20... Rxe2 21. Nxf6+ gxf6 22. Be4 $1 Bg7 (22... Nf3+ 23. Qxf3 R2xe4 24. Qxf6 Rxd4 {Gurevich,Mikhail: ''} 25. Rxd4 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '+-'} Bg7 26. Rg4 $18) 23. Qh7+ Kf8 24. Rc1 $1 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '[ c5]'} f5 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '!?'} (24... Nd7 25. Bxc6 $18) 25. Bxc6 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '!?'} (25. Bc5+ Qxc5 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '!'} 26. Rxc5 fxe4 $16) 25... Re7 {Raetsky/Chetverik: 'White has a good position, with the bishop pair and active possibilities against Black's exposed king. There are a couple of good moves here, Gurevich choosing' Gurevich,Mikhail: ''} 26. Bb5 $1 {Raetsky/Chetverik: '!?'} (26. Kg2 {is a good prophylactic move against ...Nf3.}) (26. Bg2 {Gurevich,Mikhail} Rc7 $16) 26... Nf3+ (26... Qxb5 27. Rc8+ Re8 28. Bc5+ Qxc5 29. Rxc5 $18) 27. Kg2 Nxd4 {Gurevich,Mikhail: ''} (27... Bxd4 {Gurevich,Mikhail} 28. Rc8+ Re8 29. Qxh6+ Bg7 30. Qd6+ $18) (27... Qxb5 {Gurevich,Mikhail} 28. Rc8+ Re8 29. Bc5+ $18) 28. Rc8+ Re8 29. Bxe8 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '+-'} Qd5+ 30. Kh3 {Raetsky/Chetverik: 'So far, so good. Black has to take on e8 and the position is simplified.'} Rxe8 31. Rxe8+ Kxe8 32. Qxg7 Qe4 (32... Nf3 33. Qxh6 $18 {Gurevich,Mikhail: ' e3+-'}) 33. f4 $1 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '[ e5+-]'} Ne6 {Gurevich,Mikhail: ''} 34. Qe5 Qc2 35. Rf3 {Gurevich,Mikhail: '[ b3-b8]'} Kf8 36. Rb3 {Ftacnik,L Ftacnik,L Raetsky/Chetverik: '. White is an exchange up, is well coordinated and now turns his attention to Black's king.'} (36. Rb3 Kg8 37. Rb8+ Kh7 38. Rh8+ Kg6 39. Rg8+ Kh5 40. g4# {Gurevich,Mikhail: '#'}) 1-0

