 44. Rb3 Bd6 45. Kg1 Ra2 46. Kf1 Ra3 47. Rxa3 Bxa3 48. e4 Bd6 49. Ke2 f6 50. Ke3 Kf7 51. Kd4 Bb8 52. Kd5 h5 53. e5 fxe5 54. Nxe5+ Kg7 55. Ke6 Ba7 56. Nd3 Bb8 57. Kf5 Kh6 58. Nc5 Ba7 59. Ne4 Bd4 60. f4 gxf3 61. gxf3 Bb6 62. f4 Bc7 63. Ng5 Bb8 64. Nf7+ Kg7 65. Ne5 Ba7 66. Nd3 Bg1 67. Kg5 Bh2 68. Kh4 Kh6 69. Ne5 Bg1 70. Kh3 Ba7 71. Kg2 Kg7 72. Nf3 Kf6 73. Nh4 Bb6 74. Kf3 Ba7 75. Ng2 Bb6 76. Ne3 Ba5 77. Ke4 Be1 78. Nf1 Ba5 {½-½ Pytel,K-Nicevski,R/Polanica Zdroj POL 1971/}) 15. O-O (15. a4 Nd7 16. Qc2 Ne5 17. Nxe5 Qxe5 18. O-O Re8 19. Rab1 a6 20. Rfd1 Rb8 21. Rd2 Bd7 22. a5 b5 23. axb6 Rxb6 24. Ra1 Reb8 25. Qc1 Bb5 26. Ra3 Bxe2 27. Rxe2 Qf5 28. e4 Qg4 29. Qe1 Bd4 30. Nd1 Rb3 31. Rxb3 Rxb3 32. Ne3 Qxe4 33. Nc2 Qxd5 {0-1 Belmonte,D-Soria,A/corr LAMER 1969/}) (15. Qd3 Nd7 16. Bd1 Ne5 17. Nxe5 Qxe5 18. Bc2 f5 19. f4 Qe7 20. O-O-O c4 21. Qd2 a6 22. Rde1 b5 23. a3 Qb7 24. fxg5 a5 25. gxh6 Bf6 26. h7+ Kh8 27. e4 b4 28. Nd1 c3 29. Qh6 cxb2+ 30. Kb1 Bg7 31. Qg5 Rf8 32. exf5 b3 33. Be4 Qc7 34. Rhf1 Bxf5 35. Rxf5 Qc5 {0-1 Baturinsky,V-Sorokin,G/corr URS 1969/}) 15... Nd7 16. a4 (16. e4 Ne5 17. Ne3 {[%cal Gf2f4] Tal} a6 18. a4 Ng6 19. Nc4 Bd4 20. Nb6 Rb8 $11 {Myers}) (16. Qc2 Ne5 17. Rfe1 Nxc4 18. Bxc4 a6 19. a4 b6 20. Qe2 Re8 21. Rad1 {Tal: '½-½ Baumbach,F-Golz,W/Aschersleben DDR 1963/'} Qd7 22. Ra1 Qe7 23. Rad1 Qd7 24. Ra1 Qe7 25. Rad1 {½-½ Baumbach,F-Golz,W/Aschersleben DDR 1963/}) 16... Ne5 17. Nxe5 (17. Nd2 $2 g4 $1 {Tal} 18. e4 h5 19. Qb3 h4 $1 20. Nb5 a6 $36 {Myers}) 17... Qxe5 {Myers: Tal prefers 17...xe5 here, because the queen "blocks the bishop's path", but it is doubtful that this would constitute any real improvement.} (17... Bxe5 $5 {Tal} 18. Bd3 f5 19. Qh5 Bg7 20. a5 Qf7 21. Qe2 Bd7 22. Qc2 h5 23. f4 $11 {Myers}) 18. a5 Rb8 19. Ra2 $5 Bd7 20. Nb5 (20. Bb5 $5 Qe8 $5 21. Qd3 (21. Bxd7 Qxd7 $11 {[%cal Gb7b5] Tal}) 21... Bxc3 22. Bxd7 Qxd7 23. bxc3 $5 (23. Qxc3 Qf5 {Tal} 24. Rd1 Rd7 $11) 23... Qg4 24. e4 Re8 25. f4 $36 {Myers}) 20... Bxb5 (20... a6 $6 21. Na3 f5 (21... b5 $2 22. axb6 Rxb6 $4 23. Nc4 $18 {Tal}) 22. Nc4 Qf6 23. Qc2 Rf8 24. b4 $5 $14 {Myers}) 21. Bxb5 {Tal: In this position, I offered my opponent a draw. Botvinnik asked me to make the next move, and as often happens in similar situations, it did not turn out successfully. After the move in the game, the queenside becomes blocked, and White has the possibility of switching the game's center of gravity into the center and the kingside where his prospects are better. And Botvinnik understandably declined the draw.} b6 $6 (21... a6 $142 22. Bc4 b5 23. axb6 Rxb6 24. b3 Ra8 $11 {Tal}) 22. a6 $1 Rbc8 23. Qd3 Rc7 24. b3 Qc3 $6 (24... Re7 $5) 25. Qxc3 Bxc3 26. Rc2 Bf6 (26... Bg7 $5 {[%cal Gf7f5] Tal}) 27. g4 (27. f3 $5 Re7 28. Kf2 Kg7 29. Rh1 Re5 30. e4 $14 {Myers}) 27... Re7 28. Rc4 {Tal: Now Black sees that his position is extremely unpleasant, and he has no active possibilities. White can prepare at will an advance in the center via g3, f4, e4, e5, and then undermine the queenside with b3-b4. After the opening of files, Black's weaknesses, especially the a-pawn, will become tangible. Therefore, Black decides to upset his opponent with unexpected counterstrokes.} (28. g3 $5) 28... Rc8 29. g3 $1 Bg7 30. Rd1 (30. Kg2 $5) 30... Rf8 {Tal: Black is "speculating", hoping to undermine with ...f7-f5. It should be understood that at the end of a game, when fatigue begins to increase, you try to prevent your opponent from carrying out his intentions the first chance you get. It was precisely due to fatigue that White played his next move.} 31. Rd3 $6 (31. b4 $142 $5 {Tal} cxb4 32. Rxb4 Rc8 33. Bc6 Kh7 34. e4 $5 Bc3 35. Rc4 Bg7 36. f4 $1 $36 {Myers}) 31... Kh7 32. Kg2 Kg6 33. Rd1 (33. f4 $5 h5 34. f5+ (34. gxh5+ Kxh5 35. f5 $2 g4 $1 {Tolush}) 34... Kh6 35. gxh5 Kxh5 36. g4+ Kh6 37. Rd1 $36 {[%cal Yd1h1] Myers}) 33... h5 34. gxh5+ Kxh5 35. g4+ (35. Rg4 Kxg4 $2 (35... f5 $5) 36. Bd3 $8 Rxe3 $8 37. fxe3 {Romanovsky} Be5 38. Rh1 Rg8 39. Bc2 $1 $18 {Myers}) (35. b4 Kg6 (35... cxb4 36. Rxb4 Rc7 $4 37. Bd3 $1 g4 38. Bf5 $16) 36. bxc5 bxc5 37. Rb1 f5 38. g4 $5 Be5 39. gxf5+ Kxf5 40. Ba4 $14 {[%cal Ya4c2,Rb1b7] Myers}) 35... Kg6 36. Rc2 (36. Rh1 Rh8 37. Rcc1 Rh6 38. Rxh6+ Bxh6 39. Rh1 Bg7 40. Kg3 $14 {Myers}) 36... Rh8 37. Bd3+ (37. Rh1 $5) 37... Kf6 38. Kg3 Ree8 (38... Rh4 $5) 39. Bb5 Re4 $1 {[%cal Ye4b4,Yh8h4]} 40. Rc4 $1 Rxc4 41. bxc4 Ke7 42. Ba4 (42. f4 Bf6 $1 43. Rg1 Rh7 44. Kf3 Rh2 45. Ke4 Rh3 46. Rg2 Rh1 47. Re2 Rg1 48. Kf5 Rf1 $11 {Myers}) 42... Be5+ 43. Kf3 (43. f4 Bf6 {Tal} 44. Rb1 Rh6 45. Rxb6 $5 axb6 46. a7 gxf4+ 47. Kxf4 Rh8 48. Bc6 Rg8 49. a8=Q Bg5+ 50. Ke4 Rxa8 51. Bxa8 Kf6 $11 {Myers}) 43... Rh4 44. Rg1 (44. Bc2 Rh3+ 45. Ke4 Rh2 46. Rf1 Bg3 $1 47. Kf3 Bh4 $1 $11 {Tal}) 44... f5 (44... f5 45. gxf5 Rxc4 46. Rg4 Rxg4 47. Kxg4 Kf6 $11) 1/2-1/2

