{[%mdl 296]} 1. e4 {Myers Tal} c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. Bc4 e6 7. N1e2 Bd6 8. h4 h6 9. Nf4 Bxf4 10. Bxf4 Nf6 11. Qd2 {Myers: Tal considered this to be a new move, and certainly it was so far as chess theory was concerned. It is safe to assume that both players were familiar with Geller-Bagirov from the 1960 URS Championship, which had been played at the beginning of the year, but we should take note of Karaklajic-Udovcic from the 1957 YUG Championship, though it is not mentioned by Tal.} (11. Qe2 Nbd7 12. O-O-O Nb6 13. Bb3 Nfd5 14. Bd2 Qd7 15. Ne4 Bxe4 16. Qxe4 O-O-O 17. Ba5 Rde8 18. Rhe1 Kb8 19. c4 Nc7 20. Bd2 Nc8 21. Bf4 Rhg8 22. Qe5 f6 23. Qa5 g5 24. hxg5 hxg5 25. Bg3 Nb6 26. Re3 g4 27. c5 Nbd5 28. Bxd5 exd5 29. Rde1 Rxe3 30. Rxe3 Rc8 31. Bd6 Qd8 32. Re7 a6 33. g3 f5 34. Qb6 Ka8 35. Rxc7 {1-0 Rohacek,I-Opocensky,K/Luhacovice POL 1935/}) (11. h5 Bh7 12. Qe2 Nbd7 13. O-O-O Nd5 14. Bd2 N7f6 15. Bd3 Bxd3 16. Qxd3 Qc7 17. Kb1 O-O-O 18. Rh4 Qe7 19. c4 Nc7 20. Rhh1 Rd7 21. Rhe1 Rhd8 22. Qc3 Qd6 23. Bc1 Kb8 24. Qa5 Na6 25. Ne4 Nxe4 26. Rxe4 Ka8 27. Bf4 Qf8 28. Qc3 Nc7 29. Rde1 Ne8 30. Be5 Nd6 31. Rf4 Ne8 32. Rfe4 Nd6 33. Rf4 Ne8 34. Rfe4 Nd6 {½-½ Geller,E-Bagirov,V/Leningrad URS 1960/}) 11... Nbd7 12. O-O-O Nd5 (12... Nb6 13. Bb3 Nbd5 (13... a5 14. a3 Nfd5 15. h5 Bh7 16. Rhe1 Nxf4 17. Qxf4 Qg5 18. Qxg5 hxg5 19. Re5 Ke7 20. Rxg5 Kf6 21. Re5 a4 22. Ba2 Nd5 23. Bxd5 cxd5 24. f3 Rhc8 25. c3 b5 26. Kd2 Ke7 27. Rde1 b4 28. axb4 a3 29. b3 a2 30. Ra1 Bb1 31. Ne2 Ra3 32. Nc1 f5 33. g4 fxg4 34. fxg4 Rf8 35. Re2 Rf4 36. Rg2 Be4 37. Rh2 Rxg4 38. Rxa2 Rxa2+ 39. Nxa2 Rg2+ 40. Rxg2 Bxg2 41. c4 Bf3 42. Nc3 Bxh5 43. b5 dxc4 44. bxc4 Kd7 45. Ke3 Bf7 46. c5 Bg6 47. Ne4 Bh5 48. Kf4 Be2 49. Nd6 Bd3 50. b6 Kc6 51. Nf7 Ba6 52. Ke5 {1-0 Baschi-Sommovigo,A/corr ITA 1969/}) 14. c4 (14. Be5 O-O 15. Ne2 Rc8 16. Nf4 Bh7 17. f3 Qe7 18. g4 Nd7 19. Bxg7 Kxg7 20. Nh5+ Kh8 21. Qxh6 Rg8 22. c3 Qf8 23. Qd2 Bg6 24. Ng3 Qd6 25. h5 Bh7 26. Ne2 Qe7 27. Rdg1 N7b6 28. g5 Bf5 29. g6 Qf8 3