{[%mdl 2112] Myers: In the August 1998 issue of Chess Life, Hanon Russell published an artcle containing several games from 1949-50 by a youth named Mikhail Tal. These games were a selection from a small notebook which had come into Russell's possession and in which Tal had recorded some three dozen games from the very beginning of his chess career. Many of these games had never been published before. I have taken the liberty of adding plausible first names for his opponents where this information was not provided in Russell's article.} 1. e4 {Myers Alburt} Nf6 2. Nc3 e5 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. Bb5 Bb4 5. O-O d6 6. d3 O-O 7. Bg5 Bxc3 8. bxc3 h6 9. Bh4 Qe7 10. Qd2 Nd8 11. Rfe1 $146 c6 12. Bc4 Be6 13. Bb3 Bxb3 (13... Bg4 $5) 14. axb3 $1 Ne6 15. d4 Nf4 $1 16. g3 (16. dxe5 $5) 16... Ng6 17. c4 (17. Qe3 $5) 17... Rfd8 18. Ra4 (18. c3 $5) 18... a6 19. c3 b5 $5 20. cxb5 (20. Ra5 $5 {Alburt}) 20... axb5 21. Rb4 $2 (21. Rxa8 $5 Rxa8 22. Qb2 Nxh4 23. Nxh4 Qe6 $36 {Myers}) 21... Ra5 (21... Rdb8 $5 22. Qd3 Ra5 23. Bxf6 Qxf6 24. dxe5 Nxe5 25. Nxe5 dxe5 26. c4 Rd8 $19 {Myers}) 22. c4 Rda8 (22... c5 $5) 23. cxb5 cxb5 24. Qc3 Nxh4 25. Nxh4 g6 (25... d5 $5) 26. Nf3 $2 (26. dxe5 $5) 26... Ng4 $2 (26... d5 $5) 27. h3 exd4 28. Nxd4 Nf6 (28... Ne5 $5) 29. Nc6 $2 (29. Nxb5 $5 Kh7 30. Kg2 R8a6 31. Nd4 Ra2 32. Nc2 Qe6 33. Rb7 $16 {Myers}) 29... Qc7 $1 30. Rc1 R5a6 $1 31. f3 (31. Qxf6 $5) 31... d5 (31... Nh5 $5) 32. e5 (32. Qxf6 $5) 32... Ra2 (32... Kh7 $5) 33. Rxb5 Nh5 34. Rxd5 $2 (34. f4 $1 Kh7 35. Qe3 Rc8 $1 36. g4 d4 37. Qf3 d3 38. gxh5 d2 39. hxg6+ Kg7 40. Rd1 Qxc6 41. Qxc6 Rxc6 42. Rd5 Rxg6+ 43. Kf2 $16 {Myers}) 34... Nxg3 35. Rd2 $2 (35. Qc5 $8) 35... Ne2+ 36. Rxe2 Rxe2 37. Qc5 $2 (37. Kf1 $5) 37... Kh7 (37... Qd7 $1 38. Ne7+ Kg7 39. Qd6 Qa7+ 40. Kh1 Rh2+ 41. Kxh2 Qf2+ 42. Kh1 Qxf3+ 43. Kg1 Qe3+ 44. Kf1 Qxc1+ $19 {Myers}) 38. Kf1 $2 (38. Qd6 $5) 38... Raa2 (38... Rh2 $5 39. Kg1 Raa2 40. Qd5 Rhd2 $19 {Myers}) 39. Nd4 Qxc5 40. Rxc5 Red2 41. Rc1 Rxd4 42. Ke1 Rdd2 43. b4 Rh2 0-1

