1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 (4. Bxc6 dxc6 5. O-O) 4... Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O 9. h3 Na5 $5 10. Bc2 c5 11. d4 Nd7 12. dxc5 (12. Nbd2 cxd4 (12... exd4 13. cxd4 Nc6 14. d5 Nce5) 13. cxd4 Nc6) (12. dxe5 Nxe5) (12. d5) 12... dxc5 13. Nbd2 Qc7 (13... f6 14. Nh4 Nb6 15. Nf5 Rf7 16. Qg4 (16. Nxe7+) 16... Kh8 17. h4 g6 18. Nh6 Rg7 19. Qf3) (13... Bb7 14. Nf1 Nc4 15. b3 Nd6) 14. Nf1 Nb6 15. Ne3 Rd8 16. Qe2 $14 Be6 17. Nd5 Nxd5 (17... Bxd5 18. exd5 f6 19. h4 Nxd5 (19... Nac4 20. h5 Nd6 21. Qd3 e4 22. Rxe4 Nxe4 23. Qxe4) 20. h5) 18. exd5 Bxd5 19. Nxe5 Ra7 (19... Bd6 20. Qd3 Bxe5 21. Qxh7+ Kf8 22. f4) (19... Be6 20. Nxf7) (19... Bf8 20. Qh5 g6 (20... h6 21. Ng4) 21. Qh4 Bg7 (21... Be7 $14 {½-½ Atalik,E (2481)-Fominykh,M (2253)/Moscow 2012/CBM 146 Extra (68)} {Interesting is} 22. Qg3 $5) 22. Ng4) (19... f6 20. Qh5 fxe5 21. Bxh7+ Kf8 22. Rxe5 Bf7 23. Rf5 Bf6 24. Rxf6 gxf6 25. Bh6+ Ke7 26. Re1+ Be6 (26... Kd6 27. Bf4+ Kc6 28. Be4+) 27. Bf5 $14 {1-0 Vaisser,A (2530)-Ivkov,B (2470)/Belgrade 1988/CBM 010 (43)} Rd6 28. Bf4) (19... Re8 20. Qd3) 20. Bf4 Qb6 (20... Qc8 21. Rad1) 21. Rad1 g6 $11 (21... Bxa2 22. Rxd8+ Qxd8 (22... Bxd8 23. Nc4 $14 {or} Qe6 $5 24. Qd1 Rd7 25. Nd2) 23. b4 cxb4 $11 {½-½ Olafsson,H (2555)-Ljubojevic,L (2620)/Reykjavik 1987/CBM 002 (24)} {A better move is} 24. cxb4 $1 $14 {White is also slightly better after} Bxb4 (24... Nc4 $14 {½-½ Knaak,R (2515)-Middendorf,F (2250)/Muenster 1991/EXT 1997 (85)} 25. Nc6 $5) 25. Qe4 Bxe1 26. Qxh7+ Kf8 27. Qh8+ Ke7 28. Bg5+ f6 29. Ng6+ Kd7 30. Bf5+ Kc7 31. Bf4+) 22. Ng4 $5 Nc4 (22... Bxa2 23. Rxd8+ Qxd8 24. Bh6 f5 (24... f6 25. b3 $6) (24... Bf8 $1 25. Qe8 Ra8 26. Nf6+ Kh8 27. Bxf8) 25. Qe5 Bd6 (25... Bf8 26. Qe8 Qxe8 27. Rxe8 Rf7 28. Ne5 $14 {½-½ Lautier,J (2632)-Hauchard,A (2513)/Paris 2000/CBM 077 (49)} {Another kind of pawn structure arises after} Rf6 $5 29. Nd7) 26. Rd1 Nc4 (26... fxg4 27. Rxd6 Rd7 28. Qg7+) 27. Qe6+ Kh8 (27... Rf7 28. b3 fxg4 29. bxc4 Qh4 30. Rxd6 Qxh6 (30... Qxf2+ 31. Kh1) 31. Rd8+ Kg7 32. Qe5+ $14 {½-½ Donner,J (2500)-Ivkov,B (2560)/Wijk aan Zee 1972/MCD (19)}) 28. b3 $11 {1-0 Tal,M (2620)-Klaric,Z (2405)/Sochi 1977/EXT 1999 (48)} fxg4 {is better:} 29. bxc4 Rd7 $14 {One more possibility is} 30. Bg5 $5) 23. Bh6 (23. Nh6+ Kg7 24. Rxd5 Rxd5 25. Nxf7 Qf6) 23... Be6 (23... Nxb2 24. Rxd5 Rxd5 25. Be4 Rd8 26. Qxb2 f5 $11 {0-1 Miles,A (2505)-Kagan,S (2460)/Hastings 1976/EXT 1999 (53)} {Also possible is} 27. c4) 24. Bb3 Qb8 25. Rxd8+ Bxd8 (25... Qxd8 26. Bxc4 Bxc4 (26... bxc4 27. Qe5) 27. Nf6+ Kh8 28. Qe5) 26. Bxc4 bxc4 27. Qxc4 Qd6 (27... Qxb2 28. Rxe6) (27... Bxc4 $14 {½-½ San Segundo Carrillo,P (2516)-Rogers,I (2593)/Mallorca 2004/CBM 104 (43)} {The position is equal after} 28. Re8#) 28. Qa4 Qe7 29. Nf6+ Kh8 30. Nd5 Qd7 31. Qe4 Qd6 (31... Bxd5 32. Qe8+ Qxe8 33. Rxe8#) 32. Nf4 (32. c4) 32... Re7 33. Bg5 (33. Bf8) 33... Re8 34. Bxd8 {is too slow:} Rxd8 (34... Qxd8 35. Qe5+ f6 $16 {1-0 Crouch,C (2410)-Norwood,D (2535)/England 1998/EXT 2000 (31)} (35... Kg8 36. Nd5) {White preserves a more active position after} 36. Qxc5 Bxa2 37. Rxe8+ Qxe8 38. c4) 35. Nxe6 Qxe6 (35... Re8 36. Qe5+) 36. Qxe6 fxe6 37. Rxe6 Rd1+ 38. Kh2 Rd2 39. Rb6 Rxf2 $11 {½-½ Garcia,R-Najdorf,M/Buenos Aires 1965/MCD (37)} {White can try} 40. Rb7 $5 Rf6 41. Kg3 (41. Kg3 Kg8 42. b4 cxb4 43. cxb4 $2 Rd6 $1 44. a4 Rd3+ 45. Kh2 Ra3 $18 {1-0 Ivkov,B (2525)-Kagan,S (2445)/Rio de Janeiro 1979/IZT} 46. a5 Ra4 $5 {is interesting:} (46... Kh8 47. Kg1 Ra2 48. Kf1 Kg8 49. Ke1 Rxg2 50. b5 axb5 51. a6 Ra2 52. a7) 47. Kg3) 1/2-1/2

[Event "URS-chT Cup 03rd sf"]
