1. e4 {Marin,Mihail} e5 {1) Tal in Shakmatyi v SSSR 1960. Reprinted in 2) Kirillov,V: Mikhail Tal 1949-1961. Riga. 1996. p.217-229.} 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 {[%cal Ge2e4]} O-O 9. h3 Bb7 10. d4 { b4-b5 gefolgt von a3} Re8 11. a4 Bf8 (11... h6 $1 12. Nbd2 exd4 {Marin,Mihail: 'Tal'} 13. cxd4 $5 {Schipkov, B} Nb4 14. Qe2 Bf8 15. e5 dxe5 $14 16. dxe5 Qd3 17. Qxd3 Nxd3 18. Re3 Nxc1 {Marin,Mihail: '' Marin,Mihail: 'Tal'} 19. Rxc1 {[%csl Yc4,Yc6,Yc7]} Nd5 20. Bxd5 $5 {Schipkov, B} Bxd5 21. axb5 axb5 22. Rxc7 Ra1+ 23. Kh2 $36 {Marin,Mihail: 'Tal'} Ra2 $2) (11... Qd7 $19 {[%csl Yh3]} {Marin,Mihail: 'Instead of this over-optimistic move, Tal recommended'} 12. Nbd2 $1 {Marin,Mihail: 'which has done quite well in later correspondence games:'} Bf8 13. axb5 axb5 14. Rxa8 Bxa8 15. d5 {[%cal Gf7d6] Marin,Mihail: 'd6 Tal'} {oder} Ne7 16. Nf1 {Marin,Mihail} h6 17. Ng3 {Hondema,E-Wind,M/NED-ch M corr 1990/Corr Nr. 1} c6 18. dxc6 Bxc6 19. Nh2 d5 $1 {we can feel that the white king side is left without sufficient defenders, which enables Black maintain equality in spite of his hanging d6- and a5-pawns.} 20. Nh5) 12. d5 Ne7 (12... Na5 13. Ba2 c6 14. Na3 (14. dxc6 Bxc6 15. axb5 axb5 16. Bg5 $1 Be7 17. Bxf6 Bxf6 18. Na3 Qd7 $1 19. Bd5 Qb7 20. Bxc6 Qxc6 21. Nc2 Nc4 22. Nb4) 14... cxd5 (14... Rc8 15. axb5 axb5 $1 16. b4) 15. exd5 e4 (15... Qd7 $1 16. Bg5 e4 17. Nh2 bxa4 18. Bxf6 gxf6 19. Nc4 Nxc4 20. Bxc4 f5 21. Rxa4 Bh6 {Der Abgabezug} 22. Bb3 Re7 23. Nf1 Bc8 24. Rc4 Rb8 25. Ba4 Qd8) (15... bxa4 16. Qxa4 Nxd5 $18 (16... Bxd5 17. Bxd5 Nxd5 18. Nc2 Nb7 19. Qc6) 17. Ng5 Re7 (17... h6 $18 18. Nxf7 $142 Kxf7 19. Rd1 $2 {Schipkov, B} Kg8 20. Rxd5 Bxd5 21. Bxd5+ $143 Kh8 $142 $1 22. Bxa8 Qxa8 23. Qxa5) 18. b4 Nxc3 19. Qc2) (15... Rc8 16. axb5 axb5 17. Nxb5 $16 Rc5) 16. Nd4 Nc4 {Marin,Mihail: ''} 17. Nxc4 bxc4 18. Bxc4 Qc7 19. Qb3 Rac8 20. Nc6 Nxd5 21. Bxd5 Bxc6 $1 {[%cal Re2e7]} 22. Be3) (12... Nb8) 13. axb5 (13. Bg5) 13... axb5 14. Rxa8 Bxa8 15. Na3 $1 {Marin,Mihail: 'Aiming to cause Black problems with the advance of the e-pawn.'} Qd7 {[%cal Rd6d5]} 16. Bg5 c6 {Marin,Mihail: '?!'} 17. dxc6 Bxc6 18. Nc2 Qb7 19. Bxf6 $14 {Schipkov, B: 'White holds a slight lead in development.' Schipkov, B: 'Weiß hat leichten Entwicklungsvorsprung.'} gxf6 20. Nd2 {Marin,Mihail: ''} Ng6 21. Nb4 Nf4 22. h4 Ng6 23. h5 Nf4 24. Nxc6 Qxc6 25. Qg4+ $16 {Schipkov, B: 'Black's pawns are weak.' Schipkov, B: 'Die schwarzen Bauern sind schwach.'} 1-0

