1. Nf3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} Nf6 2. c4 c6 3. g3 g6 4. b3 Bg7 5. Bb2 d5 6. Bg2 O-O 7. O-O Nbd7 8. Qc2 Re8 9. Nc3 $6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Practice has proven that the development of the bishop to e2 is too modest. Swapping the c5-pawn may not promise much, but it forces Black in a well defined direction with little risk for the first player.'} (9. Ne5 $2 Nxe5 10. Bxe5 d4 11. e3 (11. Qb2 d3 12. e3) 11... Bf5 12. Qb2 dxe3 13. fxe3 Qd3) (9. d4) 9... a6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Black can play 9..c4 immediately. It is quite amazing, how often Black's pawn structure c4-d5 solves at least some of his problems in this opening.'} (9... dxc4 10. bxc4 $1 e5 11. d3 Nc5 12. Rfd1 (12. Rab1 $14) 12... Bf5 13. h3 Qc8 (13... Nfd7 14. Rab1 Qc7 15. g4 $16 {1-0 Petrosian,T-Matanovic,A/Portoroz 1958 (23)} Be6 $142 16. Ng5) 14. g4 Bd7 15. Ba3 Ne6 16. e3 $1) (9... e5 { ...b6} 10. cxd5 Nxd5 11. d3 Nb4 (11... Nxc3 12. Bxc3 Nb6 13. Bb2 Nd5 14. Nd2 $14) 12. Qb1 c5 $14 13. Nd2 Nf8 14. a3 Nc6 15. b4 cxb4 16. axb4 Nxb4 17. Ba3 Nc6 18. Nde4) 10. d4 (10. d3 e5 11. cxd5 cxd5 $11 {1-0 Levin,F (2445)-Mitkov,N (2490)/Groningen 1991 (71)}) 10... Nf8 (10... b5 11. Rac1 (11. Ne5 Bb7 (11... Nxe5 12. dxe5 Bf5 13. Qd2) 12. e3 Qc7 (12... Nxe5 13. dxe5 Ng4 14. e6) 13. Rfd1 Red8 14. Rac1 Rac8 15. f4 dxc4 16. bxc4 c5 $17 {½-½ Gavrikov,V (2430)-Kupreichik,V (2570)/Yerevan 1982 (32)} 17. Nxd7 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} Nxd7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} 18. d5 Nb6 19. cxb5 Nc4 20. b6 Nxb6 21. Ba1) 11... Bb7 12. Rfd1 e6 13. e3 Rc8 $16 {½-½ Dautov,R (2515)-Shereshevski,M/Minsk 1988 (61)} 14. Qe2 dxc4 15. bxc4 b4 16. Na4 Qa5 17. Qc2 c5) 11. Rfd1 (11. Ne5 Bf5 12. Qd2 Ne4 13. Qe3 Nxc3 14. Bxc3) 11... Bf5 12. Qc1 Ne4 (12... b5 13. Ne5 Rc8 14. Qd2 bxc4 (14... Qd6 15. c5 Qc7 16. f3 N6d7 17. e4 dxe4 18. fxe4 Be6 19. Nf3) 15. bxc4 N8d7 16. Rac1 Nb6 17. e3 Ng4 18. cxd5 cxd5 19. Qe2 Nxe5 20. dxe5 Bxe5 21. Nxd5 Rxc1 22. Bxc1 Nxd5 23. Bxd5 $13 {½-½ Geller,E (2545)-Kupreichik,V (2570)/Yerevan 1982 (34)} Qc7) 13. Nxe4 (13. Ne5) 13... Bxe4 $1 14. Qe3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: 'Tal prefers to play a bit in the style of va banque as compared to the more solid defence of the c3-pawn.'} (14. Bh3 Bxf3 15. exf3 $14 e6 $5 {Ftacnik,Lubomir}) 14... Qb6 15. Bf1 Bxf3 (15... a5) 16. c5 (16. Qxf3 dxc4 17. e4 cxb3 $14 18. Bc4 e6 19. axb3) 16... Qc7 17. Qxf3 $2 e5 18. e3 $2 (18. dxe5 Bxe5 19. Bxe5 Qxe5 20. Rac1 $2 a5 21. Qc3 Qxc3 22. Rxc3 Ne6 $16 {1-0 Roiz,M (2659)-Berkovich,M (2413)/Israel 2008 (32)}) 18... Ne6 19. b4 $2 Re7 (19... exd4 20. exd4 a5) 20. Rab1 Rae8 21. a4 f5 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: '-+!'} 22. b5 axb5 23. axb5 exd4 24. exd4 f4 25. Qg4 Rf8 26. Rd2 Rf5 27. Qd1 fxg3 28. hxg3 Ref7 29. Re2 Ng5 30. Bg2 Nf3+ 31. Bxf3 Rxf3 32. Bc1 h5 33. bxc6 bxc6 34. Bg5 Qd7 35. Re7 Rxe7 36. Qxf3 Rf7 37. Qd3 Kh7 38. Bf4 Re7 39. Be3 Qg4 40. Qd1 Qe4 $19 41. Rb3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} Rf7 42. Qb1 Qe7 $17 43. Rb6 Qd7 44. Qd1 Re7 45. Kg2 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: ''} Qe6 $5 46. Qb1 h4 47. Rb3 Qg4 48. Qh1 Bf6 49. Qh3 Qe4+ 50. Kg1 Ra7 51. Qg2 Ra1+ 52. Kh2 Qg4 53. Bf4 {} Bxd4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} 54. Qf3 Qxf3 $17 55. Rxf3 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} Bxc5 56. Rc3 Bxf2 $15 57. Rxc6 Bxg3+ 58. Bxg3 hxg3+ 59. Kxg3 Rf1 60. Rd6 {Ftacnik,Lubomir: ''} Rf5 $1 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} 61. Rd7+ Kg8 $15 62. Kg4 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} Kf8 63. Kh4 Ke8 64. Rd6 g5+ 65. Kg4 $11 Re5 66. Rg6 $15 Ke7 {Ftacnik,Lubomir} 0-1

