1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. a3 c5 (4... Ba6) (4... Bb7) 5. d5 exd5 6. cxd5 d6 7. Nc3 g6 8. e4 (8. Bg5 h6 9. Bh4 a6 10. a4 Bg7 11. Nd2 g5 {Acosta,A-Geller,E (2590)/Bogota 1978/EXT 98 (0-1, 70)} 12. Bg3 Nh5 13. Nde4 Nxg3 14. Nxg3 {Tal,M} f5 15. e4 $1 f4 16. Qh5+ $13 Kf8 17. Nf5 Bxf5 18. exf5 Nd7 19. h4 Qf6 20. Be2 Re8 21. O-O Re5 22. Bxa6 Qxf5 23. Bc8 Ke7 24. Bxd7 Qxd7 25. Rfe1 Kd8 26. a5 Rxe1+ 27. Rxe1 bxa5 28. hxg5 Re8 29. Ra1 Qf5 30. Rxa5 Re1+ 31. Kh2 hxg5 32. Ra8+ Kc7 33. Ra7+ Kb6 34. Rxg7 f3 35. Qxg5 Qf8 36. Rg8) (8. Bf4) 8... Bg7 9. Bb5+ (9. Be2 O-O 10. O-O Re8 $5 11. Nd2 Na6 {The activity of this knight is an important achievement for Black.} 12. f3 Nc7 13. a4 a6 14. Nc4 Rb8 15. Bf4 Bf8 $13 16. Qd2 b5 17. axb5 axb5 $36 18. Na5 Bd7 $1 {Tal} 19. Rfe1 b4 20. Nd1 Nb5 21. Bxb5 Bxb5 $44 {[%csl Gd4,Gd5][%cal Gf7f5]} 22. Ne3 Nh5 23. Nec4 Nxf4 24. Qxf4 Ra8 25. Nb7 $13 Qc7 {Tal,M} 26. Ncxd6 $14 Ba6 {can be met by the surprising sacrifice} 27. e5 Reb8 28. Na5 Rd8 29. Nc6 $5 {[%cal Gc8c2]} Rxd6 30. exd6 Bxd6 31. Qf6 c4 32. Rxa6) 9... Bd7 10. Be2 O-O 11. Bf4 Bg4 12. O-O a6 13. h3 (13. Nd2 $1 Bxe2 14. Qxe2 b5 {This move leads to chronic kingside weaknesses, but Black's piece activity and the relative vulnerability of the white centre seem to compensate for this drawback.}) 13... Bxf3 14. Bxf3 Ne8 15. Qd2 Nd7 16. Bg5 (16. Bh6 $1 Ne5) 16... Nef6 17. Rae1 b5 18. Bd1 Re8 $5 {This is an interesting move, keeping an eye on both enemy wings.} 19. Bc2 b4 (19... c4) 20. Nd1 Qc7 $6 {This move is based on some very nice tactical nuances, but, taking into account Tal's recommended improvement on the 22nd move, it may be not the strongest.} 21. Kh1 bxa3 22. bxa3 c4 23. f4 Nc5 24. Bxf6 Bxf6 $1 25. Nf2 Bg7 26. e5 dxe5 27. f5 Rad8 28. Ne4 Nd3 (28... Nxe4 {Tal,M} 29. Bxe4 $1) 29. Ba4 (29. Bxd3 Rxd5 $14 30. Rc1 $2) (29. fxg6 hxg6 30. Bxd3 Rxd5 31. Rc1 $1 $16) 29... Nxe1 30. Qxe1 (30. Bxe8 Rxe8 31. Qxe1) 30... Rf8 $1 31. f6 (31. Bc6 $1 {Tal,M}) 31... Bh6 32. Qh4 Be3 33. Bc6 (33. Rf3 Bd4 (33... Qb6) 34. Ng5 $16 h5 $2 {Tal,M} 35. g4 e4) 33... Kh8 34. Rf3 Qb6 35. Qe1 Bh6 36. h4 Qd4 37. h5 gxh5 $6 {Tal,M} 38. Rh3 Rg8 39. d6 Rxd6 40. Rxh5 Qd1 41. Qxd1 Rxd1+ 1/2-1/2

