1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. d4 d6 4. Nf3 g6 5. Bc4 Nb6 6. Bb3 Bg7 7. Ng5 e6 8. Qf3 $1 Qe7 $1 9. Ne4 dxe5 10. Bg5 $6 Qb4+ 11. c3 Qa5 $132 12. Nf6+ $6 Kf8 13. d5 e4 $17 {Keres} 14. Qg3 N6d7 (14... Nxd5 15. Bxd5 h6 16. b4 Qb6 17. Be3) (14... Na6 15. dxe6 Qf5 (15... h6 16. e7+ Kxe7 17. Nd5+ Ke8 18. Nxc7+ $6 Nxc7 $1 19. Qxc7 $2 Qxg5 20. Qxf7+ Kd8 21. Qxg7) (15... Bxe6) 16. e7+ Kxe7 17. Nd5+ $19 {(Vainstein 76)} (17. Nh5+ f6) (17. Ng8+ {(Vainstein 76)} Ke8 18. Nh6 Bxh6 19. Bxh6 $15 {(Bronstein)} Be6 20. O-O $1 $17 {(Bronstein)} Rg8 $2 21. Be3 $1 Nd5 22. Nd2 $16 {(Bronstein)} g5 23. Bc2 Qg6 24. Nxe4 $2 f5 25. Nxg5 Kd7 $18 {Vainstein} 26. Rad1) 17... Kf8 18. Ne3 $1 (18. Nxc7 Be5) 18... Qd7) 15. Nxd7+ (15. dxe6 $1 $17 {(Bronstein)} Nxf6 $2 16. Qf4 $1 $16 {(Bronstein)} Bxe6 $3 17. Bxe6 Nbd7) 15... Nxd7 16. dxe6 Nc5 17. e7+ Ke8 {"Der Bauerngewinn ist in dieser Stellung unwesentlich, jedoch versperrt der Bc3 die c-Linie und schrankt die Entwicklungsmoglichkeit del Lc1 ein." (Slotnik 82)} 18. O-O h6 (18... Nxb3 19. axb3 Qxa1 $2 20. Qxc7 $1 f6 21. Rd1 $1 Kf7 22. e8=Q+ $1 $40 {(Bronstein)}) 19. Bf4 $1 {"Brilliantly played. After the exchange of the last central pawns, the black king will be stripped naked, and his life now is not valued very highly." (Vainstein 76)} (19. Be3) 19... Nxb3 20. Bxc7 Qg5 21. axb3 {For Tal, the exchange of Queens was out of the question.} Qxg3 22. hxg3 Kxe7 23. Nd2 f5 $1 {"Der Turm soll auf der vierten Reihe vor allem die Felder d4 und f4 kontrollieren." (Bronstein)} 24. Bb6 $1 a6 25. Nc4 Be6 26. Bc5+ (26. Na5 $1 Bd5 $1 27. Rfd1 Ke6 {(Vainstein 76, Slotnik 82)} 28. Rd2) 26... Kf7 $1 27. Nd6+ Kg8 28. b4 Rb8 $6 29. Ba7 $1 {"Mit diesem Springeropfer versucht Tal neue Drohungen zu schaffen." (Slotnik 82)} Ra8 (29... Rd8 30. Nxb7 $19 {(Bronstein)} Rd7 $142 $1 31. Nc5 {(Bronstein)}) 30. Bb6 {"Tal has eliminated the c3 pawn and opened the maximum number of files and ranks, but this would still be endurable, except that he has also opened the black-squared diagonals, and the black king has to fear for its life." (BSV)} Be5 $1 31. Rfd1 Rh7 {"Bronstein takes an heroic decision -- to transfer his king to f6, closer to his pieces, so that they should be in direct contact with the king, allowing it to exercise its right to self-defense." (Vainstein 76)} 32. Ra5 Bf6 $1 {"Es klingt sicher seltsam, aber fur den Konig ist f6 das sicherste Feld; dorthin strebt der schwarze Monarch!" (Bronstein)} (32... Bxd6 33. Rxd6 Re8 34. Re5 Bf7 (34... Kf7 35. Bd4) 35. Rc5) 33. Bd4 Bxd4 (33... Bb3 34. Rd2 Bg5 35. Be3) 34. Rxd4 $6 {"Eine entscheidende Verrechnung, die nur erklarlich ist durch die vielen Varianten, die nachzuprufen waren. Nach 34 Le3! hatte Schwarz sehr aufpassen mussen, um den zahlreichen weissen Kombinationen zu begegnen." (Bronstein)} Rb8 $1 35. Re5 Re7 36. g4 Kf8 $1 37. gxf5 Bxf5 $1 38. Rxe7 Kxe7 39. Nxe4 Bxe4 40. Rxe4+ Kd6 41. f3 Rf8 42. Kf2 h5 43. Rd4+ Ke6 44. c4 $1 Rc8 45. Ke3 $1 {(Bronstein)} Ke5 46. b3 Rc6 47. Rd5+ Kf6 $1 48. c5 g5 49. Rd7 Re6+ 50. Kd3 Re7 51. Rxe7 $1 Kxe7 52. Kc4 $1 Ke6 53. b5 a5 54. b6 $19 {(Bronstein)} 0-1

