removing the virtual pin on the other knight.)} Rb5 34. R1c3 h6 (34... Kf7) 35. Rc5 Rb6 (35... Rb2 36. Rc2) 36. R5c4 {with chances for equality despite White's activity.} g5 37. hxg5 $5 hxg5 $5 $14 {Black should keep the position closed with} 38. Rg3 $5 $11 {retaining an adequate deployment.} (38. Rb4 Rxb4 39. axb4) 38... Rb1+ {looks more adequate.} 39. Kh2 Rh7+ 40. Rh3 Rh1+ $11 41. Kg3 R7xh3+ 42. gxh3 f4+ $15 {½-½ Fedoseev,V (2505)-Malaniuk,V (2518) Marianske Lazne 2011} 1-0

