1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. dxe5 Be6 9. c3 Be7 10. Nbd2 O-O 11. Bc2 f5 12. Nb3 Qd7 13. Nfd4 Nxd4 14. cxd4 a5 {Black will be just in time to prove that the white knight is just as vulnerable as the black one.} 15. f3 a4 16. fxe4 (16. Nd2 Ng5 17. f4 Ne4 18. Nf3 c5 19. Be3 c4 20. Ng5 Bxg5 21. fxg5 b4 22. Qe1 Qb7 23. Rc1 Rfc8 24. h4 c3 25. Bxe4 {½-½ Horowitz,I-Reshevsky,S/New York 1941/HCL}) 16... axb3 17. Bxb3 fxe4 {Without knights on the board, neither side can take advantage of the weaknesses in the enemy camp.} 18. Be3 (18. Rxf8+ Rxf8 19. Be3 Kh8 20. Rc1 c6 21. Qd2 Bg4 22. a4 bxa4 23. Bxa4 Rc8 24. b3 Qb7 25. h3 Be6 {½-½ Lein,A (2525)-Tarjan,J (2495)/Mentor 1977/MCL}) 18... Rxf1+ 19. Qxf1 Rf8 (19... c6 20. Rc1 Qb7 21. Qe2 Ra6 22. Qc2 Qa7 23. Qf2 Qb6 24. h3 Qb8 25. Qg3 Qe8 26. Bh6 Qg6 27. Qxg6 hxg6 28. Be3 b4 $11 {½-½ Bogoljubow,E-Rubinstein,A/Gothenburg 1920/HCL (61)}) 20. Qe2 h6 21. Rf1 Rxf1+ 22. Qxf1 Qc6 23. Qe2 b4 24. Qc2 Qxc2 25. Bxc2 Kf7 26. Ba4 Bc8 27. Bc6 Ke6 28. Kf2 Ba6 29. Bc1 Bc4 1/2-1/2

