{Meat and Potatoes: Benoni hero Tal plays simple chess to notch up a straight forward victory.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 e6 4. Nc3 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. Nf3 g6 7. e4 Bg7 8. Bd3 O-O 9. O-O {Nowadays everyone would play 9 h3, preventing the pin and transposing into the Modern Classical Variation.} a6 10. a4 Bg4 11. h3 Bxf3 12. Qxf3 Nbd7 {And here either 13 Qe2 or 13 Qd1 are preferable.} 13. Bf4 Qc7 14. Qe2 Rfe8 15. Bh2 Rac8 16. Bc4 Ne5 $1 17. f4 Nxc4 18. Qxc4 Nd7 {With simple play Tal has accumulated a pleasant advantage. In particular the bishop on h2 is no match for his opponent on g7.} 19. Rfe1 $2 Qb6 $1 20. Rab1 Qb4 21. Qf1 c4 $1 {The queenside attack is well and truly moving. White is already positionally lost.} 22. Re2 b5 23. axb5 axb5 24. Kh1 Bxc3 $1 {It seems unusual to give up such a good Benoni bishop, but this is the clearest route to victory.} 25. bxc3 Qxc3 26. Rxb5 Qd3 {The c-pawn suddenly becomes a little monster.} 27. Qe1 c3 28. Rb1 Nc5 {And White resigned. There is no defence, for example} (28... Nc5 29. Qd1 Rxe4 $1 30. Qxd3 Nxd3 31. Rxe4 c2) 0-1

