{Smash and Grab: Benoni hero Mikhail Tal plays a brilliant miniature.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 e6 4. Nc3 exd5 5. cxd5 d6 6. Nf3 g6 7. e4 Bg7 8. Be2 O-O 9. O-O Re8 10. Nd2 Na6 11. Re1 {The super-solid 11 f3 is the most popular move nowadays.} Nc7 12. a4 b6 13. Qc2 Ng4 14. h3 $2 {This walks into a typical Tal attack.} (14. Bxg4 Bxg4 15. Nc4 Qf6 16. Be3 Bd7 17. Qd2 {would have left White with a small advantage.}) 14... Nxf2 $3 15. Kxf2 Qh4+ 16. Kf1 {This is forced as} (16. g3 {allows a brilliant mate with} Bd4+ 17. Kg2 Qxh3+ 18. Kf3 Bg4+ 19. Kf4 g5+ 20. Kxg5 Be3+ 21. Kf6 Qh6#) 16... Bd4 17. Nd1 {The only move to avoid mate in one with Qf2.} Qxh3 $3 18. Bf3 (18. gxh3 Bxh3# {is a very pretty checkmate.}) 18... Qh2 19. Ne3 f5 $1 20. Ndc4 ({The attack is relentless.} 20. exf5 $2 Bxe3 {wins for Black.}) 20... fxe4 21. Bxe4 Ba6 $1 {Introducing another pin. White is totally tied up.} 22. Bf3 Re5 23. Ra3 Rae8 24. Bd2 $2 (24. Rd3 {was the last chance.}) 24... Nxd5 $1 {The winning move. White has no defence to all the threats.} 25. Bxd5+ Rxd5 26. Ke2 Bxe3 27. Rxe3 Bxc4+ ({It's mate after} 27... Bxc4+ 28. Qxc4 Qxg2+ 29. Kd1 Qxd2#) 0-1

