{Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Unsurprisingly Tal, emaciated yet full of energy, featured in many players' memories about the tournament. ("He was a walking god," said Tibor Karolyi jr. , and the admiration for him among ordinary Estonians was remarkable. Though when he was described as a living legend he corrected it and said "a barely-living legend!") Kalle Kiik, a Tartu University student competing in his first big tournament, was at the tail of the field when he faced Tal in the tenth round. Yet the youngster outplayed the legend until in mutual time trouble disaster struck.'} 1. e4 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian} c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. f4 e6 7. a4 $5 (7. Qf3 {(Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian) Glek,Igor 2395 - Itkis,Boris 2300, USSR 1985 - 39/  (287)}) 7... Nc6 8. Be3 e5 9. Nf3 exf4 (9... Ng4 10. Bg1 exf4 11. Nd5 {b6 ×b6}) 10. Bxf4 Be7 11. Bd3 O-O 12. O-O Be6 (12... Qb6+ 13. Kh1 Qxb2 14. Nd5 Nxd5 15. exd5 Ne5 16. Rb1 Qc3 17. Nxe5 dxe5 18. Qh5 g6 19. Qxe5 $16) 13. Nd5 (13. Kh1) 13... Bxd5 14. exd5 Nb4 (14... Nxd5 15. Bxh7+ Kxh7 16. Qxd5 $16) (14... Ne5 15. Nxe5 dxe5 16. Bxe5 Qxd5 17. Rf5 $16) 15. c4 Qb6+ 16. Kh1 Ng4 $2 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Diagram [#]'} 17. Nd4 $5 (17. Bf5 $1 Ne3 (17... Nf2+ 18. Rxf2 Qxf2 19. Qb3 $1 a5 20. Be3 Qe2 21. Re1 $18) (17... Nf6 18. a5 { Qb3+-  b3+-}) 18. Bxe3 Qxe3 19. Re1 Qf4 20. Bxh7+ Kxh7 21. Rxe7 Qxc4 22. Ng5+ $40) 17... Nxd3 18. Qxd3 Bf6 19. Rad1 Qxb2 20. Bxd6 Rfe8 (20... Rfc8 $142) 21. Nc2 $8 Rad8 22. Bg3 $1 Qa2 23. h3 $16 Ne5 24. Bxe5 Bxe5 25. Rb1 Re7 (25... Rd7 $142) 26. Ne3 Qxa4 27. c5 Qd7 28. Nf5 Ree8 (28... Re6 $5) 29. d6 Qc6 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Diagram [#]'} 30. Qc4 $1 {[f7] [×f7]} Rd7 31. Rb6 $18 Qc8 32. c6 $6 (32. Qd5 $1 { Rfb1+-  fb1+-}) 32... bxc6 33. Ne7+ Rdxe7 34. dxe7 Rxe7 $2 (34... Bf6 35. Rxc6 Qd7 36. Rc7 Qb5 37. Rc8 Qd7 38. Rxe8+ Qxe8 39. Rxf6 gxf6 40. Qc7 { Qd8+-  d8+-}) (34... Qe6 35. Qxe6 fxe6 36. Rxc6 Bf6 37. Rxe6 Kf7 38. Rxa6 (38. Rfe1 Rxe7 39. Rxe7+ Bxe7 40. Ra1 h5 $1 41. Rxa6 g6 $11) 38... Rxe7 $16 {Hermlin,  Kiik,K Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Hermlin,Aarne,  Kiik,Kalle' Hermlin,  Kiik,K}) 35. Rxc6 Qd7 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Diagram [#]'} 36. Rxf7 $4 ({Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Instead, White should win after'} 36. Rc8+ Re8 37. Rxe8+ Qxe8 38. Re1 $18 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'winning the bishop soon. Unfortunately, Kiik saw a different combination and played a losing rook move.'}) 36... Qxc6 $1 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'A really strong rejoinder.'} 37. Rxg7+ $4 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'So, Kiik decided to pick up an extra pawn, only to discover that after'} ({Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Now'} 37. Qxc6 $11 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'and'} Kxf7 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian} 38. Qxa6 $11 {is only a draw.}) 37... Kxg7 38. Qxc6 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'Diagram [#]'} Rc7 {Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: '!' Kiik,Kalle; Rogers,Ian: 'it is White who had to resign. The evening after the tournament, Kiik's second Aarne Hermlin brought Kiik to meet his old friend Tal in Tal's hotel room. After greetings in Russian, Tal said to Kiik: "You could have beaten me." Then, after a long pause, he added: "But you didn't." Kiik says he has never forgotten the message in Tal's words, suggesting to him that he did not fight hard enough until the very last move.'} 0-1

