1. e4 e6 {Prepared in advance by Tal and Koblenz for this encounter despite Tal's indifferent success with the French Defense. They reasoned -- correctly -- that Fischer was not totally at ease with the Winawer.} 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 6. b4 cxd4 7. Qg4 Ne7 8. bxa5 dxc3 9. Qxg7 Rg8 10. Qxh7 Nbc6 {'!'} (10... Nd7 11. Nf3 Qc7 12. Bb5 a6 13. Bxd7+ Bxd7 14. O-O d4 $5 15. Nxd4 (15. Bg5 Bc6 16. Bxe7 Kxe7 17. Qh4+ Ke8 18. Ng5 Qxe5 19. f4 $14 {Euwe ECO 2.Auflage 16/17 Fußnote 80} Qf5 $17) 15... Qxe5 16. Qd3 $16 {Fischer / HÜbner} Qg7 (16... O-O-O 17. Qc4+ (17. Qxc3+ $2 Bc6 $19) (17. g3 Nd5 (17... Bb5 $2 18. Qxc3+ Nc6 19. Nxb5 $18) 18. Rb1 Qc7 $15) 17... Kb8 18. Bf4 Rxg2+ 19. Kh1 (19. Kxg2 Qxf4 $40 {-+  20... e5}) 19... Rxh2+ 20. Bxh2 Rh8 21. f4 (21. Nf3 Bc6 22. Qxc6 Rxh2+ $17) 21... Qe4+ 22. Rf3 Nf5 23. Qd3 (23. Qe2 $2 Ng3+ $19) 23... Qxd4 $19) (16... Rd8 17. Qe3 Qg7 (17... Qd5 18. f3 Ba4 19. Ne2 Nf5 20. Qxc3 (20. Qf2 Qc4 $17 21. Bf4 Bxc2 22. Rac1 Rd2) 20... Bb5 21. Nf4 Qd4+ 22. Qxd4 Nxd4 23. Rf2 Nb3 $19) 18. g3 e5 (18... Nd5 19. Qe4 $10) (18... Ba4 19. Ne2 Nd5 (19... Bxc2 20. Qxc3) 20. Qe4 Bb5 21. Re1 $10 (21. a4 $10)) 19. Nf3 $14) 17. g3 e5 18. Ne2 Bb5 19. Qf3 Qh7 20. Re1 Bc6 21. Qe3 O-O-O $17 22. Qxe5 $2 (22. Nxc3 $2 Nf5) 22... Qxh2+) 11. Nf3 (11. f4) 11... Qc7 (11... Qxa5 $1 12. Rb1 (12. Ng5 Rf8 13. f4 Bd7 14. Be2 {(Levy)}) 12... Qc7 13. Bf4 Bd7 14. Bg3 O-O-O {Damjanovic-Yudovich Yugoslavia 1963}) 12. Bb5 {'!' "Sharper and boosted by Fischer's advocacy but still not necessarily better than 12 B-KB4." (Wicker 79)} (12. Bf4 $1 {This move is recommended by Tal, although Fischer prefers 12 Bb5.}) 12... Bd7 {"Now both White's KNP, which Black seriously threatens to capture, and his KP are attacked. After lengthy reflection Fischer decided to give up his central pawn." (Tal 76)} (12... Rxg2 $2 13. Kf1 $1 Rg8 14. Rg1 $1 Rxg1+ 15. Kxg1 $16 {"... and Black's King remains hemmed in the center while White merely marches his KRP to victory." (Fischer 1969)}) 13. 