o 81)} (17. Bd2) (17. Bd2) 17... Rdf8 { (Euwe)   (eco 74)}) 16. Bg5 $1 {"The basic problem which now confronts White is how to keep the Black King in the center. In this respect, the loss of White's King Pawn played into White's hands, since new threats can be created by openning the King file."} Nc6 (16... f4 $6 17. d4 $1 Qf5 (17... Qe4 18. Bxf4 $16 {(Schwarz 67)}) 18. Nxf4 Qc2 19. Ne2 $16 {(Tal 77)}) (16... d4 17. cxd4 Qa5+ 18. Bd2 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67, Euwe 76)}) 17. d4 Qc7 (17... Qe4 $6 18. Rc1 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67)}) (17... Qh8 $6 18. Nf4 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67)}) 18. h4 $1 $16 {(Keres 69, eco 74/81, Suetin 88, mco 90)} (18. Nf4 $2 Nxd4 $1 $19) 18... e5 (18... Nce7 19. Bxe7 (19. Rh3 $1 Rh8 (19... O-O-O 20. Re3 {(Schwarz 67)}) 20. Qf3 O-O-O 21. h5 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67)}) 19... Qxe7 20. Nf4 $5 (20. Qg5 $18 {(Tal)}) (20. Qg5 $18 {(Tal)}) 20... Qf6 21. Nxg6 Rxg6 22. g4 $1 O-O-O 23. g5 $17 {(Petrosian)}) 19. Rh3 $1 $16 {(Pachman 68)} Qf7 (19... e4) (19... f4 $2 20. Qg4 $1 $16 {(Tal)}) (19... e4) 20. dxe5 Ncxe5 (20... Rh8 $2 21. e6 $1 Qxe6 (21... Rxh5 22. exf7+ Kxf7 23. Ng3 $1 $16 {(Euwe 76)}) 22. Re3 Rxh5 23. Rxe6+ Kf7 24. Rxg6 $1 {(Tal 77)} Kxg6 25. Nf4+ $18) 21. Re3 Kd7 (21... Rh8 $2 22. Rxe5+ Kd7 23. Re7+ Qxe7 24. Qxg6 $18 {(Tal 77)}) 22. Rb1 b6 $6 (22... Bc6 $1 23. Nd4 (23. Rb4 $2 Rh8 $19) (23. Nf4 Rae8 24. Qd1 Ng4 25. Rxe8 Rxe8+ 26. Be2 Nxf4 27. Bxf4 Qf6 $132 {(Euwe 76)}) 23... f4 24. Rxe5 $1 Nxe5 25. Qxf7+ Nxf7 26. Bxf4 Rae8+ 27. Kd2 $16 {(Tal 77)}) 23. Nf4 Rae8 (23... Rh8 24. Nxg6 $1 Nxg6 25. Qe2 {(Tal 77)} Rxh4 26. Qa6 $16) 24. Rb4 $1 $16 {(Schwarz 67)} Bc6 25. Qd1 $1 Nxf4 (25... Ng4 26. Rxe8 (26. Re2) (26. Re2) 26... Rxe8+ 27. Be2 $18 {(Tal 77)} Nxf4 28. Rxf4 $18) 26. Rxf4 Ng6 27. Rd4 Rxe3+ (27... f4 28. Qg4+ $18) 28. fxe3 (28. Bxe3 f4) 28... Kc7 29. c4 $1 dxc4 (29... Ne7 30. cxd5 Bxd5 (30... Nxd5 31. Bc4 Kd6 32. Bf4+ Kc5 33. Qc2 $18 {(Euwe 76)}) 31. Bxe7 Qxe7 32. Qc1+ $18 {(Tal 77)} (32. Rxd5 Qxe3+ 33. Qe2 $18 {(Euwe 76)})) 30. Bxc4 Qg7 31. Bxg8 Qxg8 32. h5 1